// 2. Grammar MCQ (~40 道)
const GRAMMAR_QUESTIONS = [{"q":"Of the two routes, the one through the park is ___ but far more scenic.","opts":["longer","the longest","long","more longer"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"比较级","explain":"两条路比较用比较级 longer。最迷惑的是 the longest, 最高级要三者以上才用; more longer 是双重比较错误。考点: PSLE 爱考 of the two 只能配比较级。"},{"q":"That was by far ___ storm the island had experienced in fifty years.","opts":["worst","the worst","the worse","worse"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"最高级","explain":"by far + 最高级, 五十年里的所有风暴比, 用 the worst, 且最高级前要 the。最迷惑的是 the worse, 比较级只比两个。考点: PSLE 爱考 by far/ever + the + 最高级。"},{"q":"She has been absent from school ___ three days because of a bad cold.","opts":["for","from","since","during"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"介词","explain":"three days 是一段时长, 现在完成时配 for + 时长。最迷惑的是 since, since 后面要接起点(since Monday)不接时长; during 后接名词如 during the holidays, 不接数字时长。考点: PSLE 爱考 for 时段 vs since 时点。"},{"q":"Mrs Lee is very particular ___ punctuality and will not tolerate latecomers.","opts":["on","about","in","for"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"介词搭配","explain":"be particular about = 对某事很讲究/挑剔, 固定搭配。最迷惑的是 on, 中文『在守时方面』容易误选 on/in。考点: PSLE 爱考形容词+介词搭配 particular about / keen on / capable of。"},{"q":"Be careful ___ the hot soup.","opts":["on","in","with","to"],"ans":2,"diff":3,"tag":"介词","explain":"be careful with + 具体东西 = 小心对待热汤, 固定搭配。最迷惑的是 on/in, 中文『对热汤小心』容易乱配介词, 但 careful 只跟 with(东西)或 of(危险)。考点: PSLE 爱考 careful with / afraid of 这类形容词+介词搭配。"},{"q":"If it rains, I ___ at home.","opts":["will stay","staying","stays","stayed"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"条件句","explain":"条件句规则: if从句用现在时, 主句用will+原形, 所以选will stay。最迷惑的是stay, 主句不能也用现在时, 那样两边都没将来的意思。考点: PSLE爱考first conditional主句必带will。"},{"q":"Neither John ___ Mary likes durian.","opts":["and","or","but","nor"],"ans":3,"diff":3,"tag":"neither/nor","explain":"neither固定和nor配对, 表示两者都不喜欢。最迷惑的是or, 它是either的搭档, neither...or是不存在的组合。考点: PSLE爱考连词配对, neither/nor和either/or不能混搭。"},{"q":"She speaks English ___ than her brother.","opts":["good","more well","best","better"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"副词比较","explain":"speaks是动词, 要用副词well的比较级better来修饰。最迷惑的是good, 它是形容词只能修饰名词, 不能修饰动词speak。考点: PSLE爱考形容词副词之分, well的比较级是better不规则。"},{"q":"I would rather ___ tea than coffee.","opts":["to drink","drinking","drink","drinks"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"would rather","explain":"would rather后面直接跟动词原形drink, 这是固定句型。最迷惑的是to drink, 很多同学习惯加to, 但rather后不要to。考点: PSLE爱考would rather+原形, had better也一样不加to。"},{"q":"The book ___ I borrowed is interesting.","opts":["who","whom","which","whose"],"ans":2,"diff":3,"tag":"关系代词","explain":"先行词book是物, 关系代词用which。最迷惑的是who, 它只能指人, book是东西不能用who。考点: PSLE爱考relative pronoun选择, 人用who物用which, that两边通吃但选项里优先对号。"},{"q":"Neither of them ___ here.","opts":["have","are","were","is"],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"主谓陷阱","explain":"neither of them意思是两个都不, 语法上按单数处理, 动词用is。最迷惑的是are, 看到them复数就选are是经典陷阱, 真正的主语是neither。考点: PSLE爱考neither of/either of+复数名词仍配单数动词。"},{"q":"Each of the boys ___ a prize.","opts":["receiving","receives","receive","have"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"主谓陷阱","explain":"each of意思是每一个, 主语核心是each, 单数, 动词加s用receives。最迷惑的是receive, 被the boys复数带偏了, 但of后面的词不是主语。考点: PSLE爱考each of/every one of后动词永远单数。"},{"q":"The news ___ shocking.","opts":["being","are","is","were"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"不可数主谓","explain":"news虽然以s结尾, 但它是不可数名词, 按单数算, 用is。最迷惑的是are, 看到s尾巴就当复数是最常见的坑。考点: PSLE爱考假复数单词, news/mathematics/physics都配单数动词。"},{"q":"Hardly ___ I sat down when the phone rang.","opts":["had","was","did","have"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"倒装","explain":"Hardly...when是固定倒装句型, 表示刚一坐下电话就响, 用过去完成时had提前。最迷惑的是did, 但这个句型固定配had+过去分词, 不用did。考点: PSLE爱考Hardly had...when/No sooner had...than固定倒装。"},{"q":"Not only ___ smart, but also kind.","opts":["he is","was him","is he","he was"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"倒装","explain":"Not only放句首必须倒装, 把is提到he前面, 变成is he。最迷惑的是he is, 正常语序在这里反而错, 句首否定词强制倒装。考点: PSLE爱考Not only/Never/Seldom开头的句子要inversion。"},{"q":"My uncle, who is ___ engineer, teaches at ___ university nearby.","opts":["an / an","a / an","a / a","an / a"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"冠词-球类不加","explain":"engineer 元音音开头用 an; university 虽然 u 开头但发 /ju:/ 辅音音, 用 a。最迷惑的是 an / an, 只看字母不听发音。考点: PSLE 爱考 a university / an hour 这类字母和发音不一致的词。"},{"q":"The Sun rises in ___ east.","opts":["a","/","the","an"],"ans":2,"diff":3,"tag":"冠词-方位the","explain":"东南西北这类方位名词是独一无二的方向, 固定用the: in the east。选「/」(什么都不加)的孩子以为方位词像国家名一样免冠词, 但east前的the是铁规矩。 考点: PSLE爱考独一无二事物加the, 如the sun/the east/the world"},{"q":"It took us nearly ___ hour to find ___ hotel we had booked.","opts":["a / a","an / a","an / the","a / the"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"冠词-h不发音","explain":"hour 的 h 不发音, 用 an; hotel 被 we had booked 限定, 是特指, 用 the。最迷惑的是 an / a, 冠词对了但漏看了后面的定语从句。考点: PSLE 爱考 an hour + 特指 the 双重判断。"},{"q":"He was given ___ one-day pass to the exhibition.","opts":["a","the","/","an"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"冠词-元音音","explain":"one 的发音是 /wʌn/, 辅音音开头, 用 a。最迷惑的是 an, 看见元音字母 o 就选 an, 忘了要听发音。考点: PSLE 爱考 a one-day / a university / an hour 这类发音陷阱。"},{"q":"My brother and ___ went to the park.","opts":["I","me","myself","my"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"代词-主格","explain":"这里是句子的主语(和My brother一起去公园), 主语位置必须用主格I。选「me」的最多, 因为口语常说me and my brother, 但书面语法里主语不能用宾格。 考点: PSLE爱考并列主语选I还是me, 遮住and前面的人单独读一遍就知道"},{"q":"The teacher gave the prize to John and ___.","opts":["me","I","my","myself"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"代词-宾格","explain":"to是介词, 介词后面的代词一律用宾格me。最迷惑的是「I」, 很多孩子被大人教『说I显得有礼貌』带偏了, 其实gave to I读起来就不通。 考点: PSLE爱考介词后接宾格, 删掉John and单独试读是万能验证法"},{"q":"She did the homework by ___.","opts":["her","hers","she","herself"],"ans":3,"diff":3,"tag":"代词-反身","explain":"by oneself是固定搭配表示『独自/自己完成』, she对应的反身代词是herself。选「her」的以为介词后用宾格就行, 但by her意思变成『被她』, 和原意完全不同。 考点: PSLE爱考by+反身代词=独自做, herself/himself/themselves要配对"},{"q":"A friend of ___ is coming to stay with us next week.","opts":["mine","myself","me","my"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"代词-名词性物主","explain":"a friend of mine 是双重所有格固定结构, of 后面用名词性物主代词 mine。最迷惑的是 me, 介词后用宾格的直觉在这里失效, a friend of me 是病句。考点: PSLE 爱考 a friend of mine / a cousin of hers。"},{"q":"The cat licked ___ paws.","opts":["it's","its","itself","it"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"代词-its陷阱","explain":"paws前需要形容词性物主代词, 猫的爪子用its, 不带撇号。最毒的是「it's」, 那是it is的缩写, 意思变成『它是爪子』, 完全讲不通——但长得太像了。 考点: PSLE爱考its(它的)和it's(它是)的撇号陷阱, 拆开读一遍就现形"},{"q":"Everyone should bring ___ own pencil.","opts":["his or her","its","one's","theirs"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"代词-everyone","explain":"everyone 是单数代词, 正式书面语用 his or her 回指。最迷惑的是 theirs, 它是名词性物主代词, 后面不能再接 own pencil; one's 和 everyone 不对应; its 指物。考点: PSLE 爱考 everyone/everybody 按单数处理。"},{"q":"Between you and ___, this is a secret.","opts":["I","myself","me","my"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"代词-between后宾格","explain":"between是介词, 介词后代词必须宾格, between you and me是标准搭配。最坑的是「I」, 因为听起来『高级』, 但between you and I恰恰是最经典的错误说法。 考点: PSLE爱考between you and me, 越像客气话的I越是陷阱"},{"q":"A group of students ___ waiting outside.","opts":["am","have","are","is"],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"主谓-集合主语","explain":"主语核心词是a group(一个团体, 单数), of students只是修饰, 动词跟group走用is。选「are」的被就近的students骗了, 眼睛要盯住真正的主语头。 考点: PSLE爱考a group of/a box of结构, 动词看of前面的量词不看后面"},{"q":"One of the books ___ missing.","opts":["is","were","being","are"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"主谓-one of","explain":"真正的主语是one(一本), of the books只是范围, 单数配is。最迷惑的是「are」, 因为空格紧挨着books, 但books不是主语只是陪衬。 考点: PSLE爱考one of the+复数名词+单数动词, 划掉of短语再选"},{"q":"The number of pupils who failed the test ___ smaller this year than last year.","opts":["are","were","was","have been"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"主谓","explain":"the number of + 复数名词 作主语时是单数(指\"数量\"这一个东西), 所以用 was; a number of + 复数名词才是复数(指\"许多\")。中间的 who failed the test 是插入的定语从句, 专门用来把主语和动词隔开引你选复数。PSLE 高频陷阱。"},{"q":"Scarcely ___ the house when it started raining.","opts":["I left","I had left","did I leave","had I left"],"ans":3,"diff":6,"tag":"倒装-scarcely","explain":"Scarcely放句首必须倒装, 且『前一件事刚做完后一件事就发生』用过去完成时, 所以是had I left。最迷惑的是「I had left」, 时态对了但没倒装, scarcely在句首就必须把had提到主语前面。 考点: PSLE爱考Scarcely/Hardly...when句型, 句首否定词触发倒装+过去完成"},{"q":"The committee ___ divided in their opinions.","opts":["is","was","has","are"],"ans":3,"diff":6,"tag":"集合名词-意义复数","explain":"committee在这里『内部意见分裂』, 强调成员各自不同, 集合名词按复数处理用are, 后面的their也是铁证。最坑的是「is」, 平时committee确实常用单数, 但divided in their opinions说明这次看的是一个个人。 考点: PSLE爱考集合名词两面派, 整体=单数, 内部分歧=复数, 看their抓线索"},{"q":"He demanded that she ___ the report immediately.","opts":["submit","to submit","submits","submitting"],"ans":0,"diff":6,"tag":"虚拟-demand that","explain":"demand/suggest/insist后的that从句用虚拟语气, 动词一律原形submit, 不管主语是she。最迷惑的是「submits」, 按平时第三人称单数加s的习惯选它, 但虚拟从句里这条规则失效。 考点: PSLE高阶爱考demand that+动词原形, 见到demand/insist就把s扔掉"},{"q":"So profound ___ his speech that everyone was moved.","opts":["being","was","had been","is"],"ans":1,"diff":6,"tag":"so...that倒装","explain":"So+形容词放句首触发倒装, be动词提到主语前, 且后文was moved定调过去时, 所以用was。最迷惑的是「is」, 倒装对了但时态错了, 前后半句时态要咬合。 考点: PSLE爱考So...that句首倒装, 先看倒装再对齐后半句时态"},{"q":"She ___ to Japan twice so far, and she hopes to go again next year.","opts":["has been","went","is going","goes"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"现在完成-经历","explain":"twice(两次)说的是到今天为止的人生经历, 用现在完成时has been, been表示去过已回来。最迷惑的是「went」, 过去时只说某一次具体的事, 配不上twice这种累计经历。 考点: PSLE爱考has been to=去过(回来了) vs has gone to=去了(没回来)"},{"q":"I ___ him since last year.","opts":["have known","knew","know","am knowing"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"现在完成-持续","explain":"since last year表示从去年持续到现在, 用现在完成时have known。最坑的是「know」, 以为『现在还认识』就用现在时, 但since一出现必须完成时。另外「am knowing」也错, know不用进行时。 考点: PSLE爱考since/for信号词锁定现在完成时, 见since选have/has+过去分词"},{"q":"By the time we arrived, the movie ___.","opts":["started","starts","has started","had started"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"过去完成","explain":"By the time + 过去时, 说明电影开始发生在『我们到达』之前, 过去的过去要用 had started (past perfect)。最迷惑的是「started」: 它只说过去发生, 分不清先后, 会变成『我们一到电影才开始』。考点: PSLE爱考 by the time + 过去时配 past perfect。"},{"q":"She ___ for two hours before the bus came.","opts":["had been waiting","waits","has waited","is waiting"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"过去完成进行","explain":"公交来之前她已经持续等了两小时, 『过去某点之前一直在做』用 had been waiting (past perfect continuous), for two hours 强调持续。选「has waited」错在: has 是现在完成, 但全句在过去(the bus came), 时间轴对不上。考点: PSLE爱考 for+时长 + before过去时 选过去完成进行。"},{"q":"This time tomorrow, I ___ on the plane.","opts":["will sit","am sitting","will be sitting","sit"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"将来进行","explain":"This time tomorrow 指明天某一刻正在进行的动作, 用 will be sitting (future continuous), 像给未来拍快照。最迷惑的是「will sit」: 它只说会坐, 不能表达『那一刻正坐在飞机上』的进行画面。考点: PSLE爱考 this time tomorrow 定 future continuous。"},{"q":"By next March, he ___ here for ten years.","opts":["worked","will have worked","will work","works"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"将来完成","explain":"By next March 是未来的截止点, 到那时工作满十年, 『未来某点前累计完成』用 will have worked (future perfect)。选「will work」错在: 只说将来会工作, 表达不了『到那时已满十年』的累计感。考点: PSLE爱考 by+将来时间 配 will have + 过去分词。"},{"q":"While I ___ dinner, the phone rang.","opts":["cook","was cooking","am cooking","cooked"],"ans":1,"diff":3,"tag":"过去进行","explain":"While 引导过去正在进行的长动作(做饭), 被短动作(电话响)打断, 长动作用 was cooking (past continuous)。最迷惑的是「cooked」: 两个都用过去时会变成先做完饭电话才响, 丢了『正在做』的背景感。考点: PSLE爱考 while+过去进行 配 when+一般过去。"},{"q":"The train ___ by the time we reach the station.","opts":["has left","leaves","will have left","left"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"将来完成","explain":"By the time we reach 指将来我们到站那一刻, 火车在那之前已开走, 用 will have left (future perfect)。选「has left」错在: 现在完成说的是『现在已走』, 但到站是将来的事, 时间点不符。考点: PSLE爱考 by the time+一般现在(表将来) 配 future perfect。"},{"q":"She said she ___ the book the day before.","opts":["has bought","had bought","bought","buys"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"过去完成-间接引语","explain":"间接引语里主句 said 是过去时, 买书发生在说话之前(the day before), 过去的过去用 had bought。最迷惑的是「bought」: 直接引语可以用过去时, 但转述时要往前退一格, 否则分不清买书在说话前。考点: PSLE爱考间接引语时态后移(backshift)。"},{"q":"I ___ to call you, but I forgot.","opts":["am meaning","mean","have meant","meant"],"ans":3,"diff":3,"tag":"一般过去","explain":"『本来打算但忘了』是过去一件事, 用一般过去 meant, 和 forgot 同一时间线。最迷惑的是「had meant」: 句中没有两个过去动作分先后的需要, meant to do 本身就含『打算了没做成』, 不必用过去完成。考点: PSLE爱考 meant to + but 表过去未实现的打算。"},{"q":"We ___ in Singapore since 2020.","opts":["lived","are living","have lived","live"],"ans":2,"diff":3,"tag":"现在完成-since","explain":"since 2020 表示从过去持续到现在, 用现在完成 have lived。最迷惑的是「lived」: 一般过去表示住过但现在不住了, 和 since 的『一直住到现在』矛盾。考点: PSLE爱考 since+年份 是 present perfect 的信号词。"},{"q":"The students ___ their project by next Friday, so the exhibition can open on time.","opts":["finished","are finishing","finish","will have finished"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"将来完成-deadline","explain":"by Friday 是将来的截止日, 到那天之前会完成项目, 用 will have finished (future perfect)。选「finished」错在: 一般过去表示已经完成了, 但周五还没到, 时间方向反了。考点: PSLE爱考 by+deadline 定 future perfect。"},{"q":"He ___ TV when the earthquake struck.","opts":["has watched","watches","watched","was watching"],"ans":3,"diff":3,"tag":"过去进行-中断","explain":"地震发生(短动作, struck)打断了看电视(长动作), 长动作用过去进行 was watching。最迷惑的是「watched」: 两个一般过去读起来像先看完电视地震才来, 丢了『正在看时被打断』的画面。考点: PSLE爱考 when+短动作 配 past continuous 背景动作。"},{"q":"I wish I ___ harder last semester.","opts":["study","had studied","studied","have studied"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"虚拟-wish过去","explain":"wish + 对过去的后悔, 要比过去再退一格用 had studied (past perfect), last semester 已经过去改不了。最迷惑的是「studied」: wish+过去式是对现在的愿望, 但这里后悔的是上学期, 必须用过去完成。考点: PSLE爱考 wish 后悔过去用 had+过去分词。"},{"q":"If I were you, I ___ accept that offer.","opts":["shall","would","will","can"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"虚拟-条件句2","explain":"If I were you 是第二条件句(与现在事实相反的假设), 主句固定用 would + 动词原形。最迷惑的是「will」: will 用于真实条件句(第一条件), 但『如果我是你』根本不可能, 必须降级成 would。考点: PSLE爱考 If I were you... I would 固定搭配。"},{"q":"She acts as if she ___ the boss, but she is only a trainee.","opts":["is","were","being","be"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"虚拟-as if","explain":"as if 后说与事实相反的情况(她并不是老板), 虚拟语气一律用 were, 不分单复数。最迷惑的是「was」: 口语常听到 she was, 但正式语法和考试里虚拟语气只认 were。考点: PSLE爱考 as if/as though 虚拟用 were。"},{"q":"It is time we ___ home.","opts":["going","have gone","went","go"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"虚拟-it is time","explain":"It is time (that) 后面接过去式 went, 表示『早该回家了』, 是固定虚拟结构, 不是真的过去。最迷惑的是「go」: 按字面『是时候走了』好像该用原形, 但 It is time we 后必须退一格用过去式。考点: PSLE爱考 It is (high) time + 过去式。"},{"q":"They ___ married for 20 years next month.","opts":["will have been","were","had been","are"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"将来完成-持续","explain":"next month 是将来时间点, 到那时结婚满20年, 『将来某点前持续满』用 will have been (future perfect)。最迷惑的是「have been」: 现在完成说『已经满20年』, 但满20年是下个月的事, 还没到。考点: PSLE爱考 for+时长 + next时间 配 future perfect。"},{"q":"The children ___ already ___ their lunch.","opts":["have/eaten","are/eating","has/eaten","had/eaten"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"现在完成-already","explain":"already 配现在完成, children 是复数, 助动词用 have, 所以 have eaten。最迷惑的是「has/eaten」: 时态选对了但主谓不一致, children 不是单数, has 只配第三人称单数。考点: PSLE爱考 already 定现在完成+主谓一致双重陷阱。"},{"q":"I ___ never ___ such a beautiful sunset.","opts":["was/seeing","has/seen","have/seen","am/seeing"],"ans":2,"diff":3,"tag":"现在完成-never","explain":"never 配现在完成表示『至今从未见过』, 主语 I 用 have seen。最迷惑的是「had/seen」: 过去完成要有另一个过去动作作参照点, 这句是感叹到现在为止的经历, 没有参照点就用 have。考点: PSLE爱考 never/ever 是 present perfect 信号词。"},{"q":"We ___ just ___ when it started to rain.","opts":["have/left","are/leaving","had/left","did/leave"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"过去完成-just","explain":"just 表示『刚刚离开』, 而离开发生在下雨(过去时 started)之前, 过去的过去用 had left。最迷惑的是「have/left」: 现在完成不能和过去时间点连用, 全句锚在过去的那场雨, 必须退到 had。考点: PSLE爱考 had just done + when 过去时。"},{"q":"She ___ the piano since she was five.","opts":["has played","plays","played","is playing"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"现在完成-since从句","explain":"since she was five 从五岁持续弹到现在, 用现在完成 has played; since 从句里用过去式是正常的。最迷惑的是「played」: 主句用一般过去就成了『以前弹过现在不弹了』, 和 since 的持续义冲突。考点: PSLE爱考 since+过去时从句 主句配 present perfect。"},{"q":"By the time I reached the hall, the concert ___ and the doors were closed.","opts":["had already started","started","starts","has started"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"过去完成-先于过去","explain":"我到礼堂(过去)时, 音乐会更早就开始了, 过去的过去用过去完成时 had already started。选 started 表达不出先后; has started 是现在完成, 和过去的 reached 打架。考点: By the time + 过去时, 主句用 past perfect。"},{"q":"You ___ finish your homework before playing.","opts":["may","can","might","must"],"ans":3,"diff":3,"tag":"情态-must义务","explain":"must表示义务, 意思是「必须先做完作业才能玩」, 语气强硬没商量。can错在只说「能不能」, 不带任何强制要求, 放这句里就变成「你可以做作业」, 完全丢了规矩的意思。考点: PSLE爱考情态动词强弱, 义务规定用must"},{"q":"You ___ not park here. It is illegal.","opts":["must","would","might","need"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"情态-must not禁止","explain":"must not表示禁止, 「这里不准停车」, 后面It is illegal点明是法律禁止, 语气必须最强。may最迷惑, may not只是「可能不」或「不允许」的弱说法, 撑不起illegal这种硬规定。考点: PSLE爱考禁止类, 看到illegal/against the rules就选must not"},{"q":"He ___ be at home. His car is in the driveway.","opts":["may","must","can","should"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"情态-must推测","explain":"must在这里不是「必须」而是「一定是」, 表示有把握的推测: 车在门口, 他一定在家。may最迷惑, 只表示「可能在家」, 但证据这么明显, 弱弱的may配不上这份把握。考点: PSLE爱考must的第二个身份=肯定推测, 后句必给证据"},{"q":"You ___ see a doctor. That cough sounds bad.","opts":["may","can","would","should"],"ans":3,"diff":3,"tag":"情态-should建议","explain":"should表示建议, 「你该去看医生」, 语气温和是关心不是命令。must最迷惑, 语气太硬变成强制命令, 朋友间提建议不用它, 而且咳嗽严重也只是建议理由不是法规。考点: PSLE爱考建议用should, 命令才用must"},{"q":"She ___ have left already. The door is locked.","opts":["must","should","would","can"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"情态-must have过去推测","explain":"must have + 过去分词表示对过去的肯定推测: 门锁了, 她一定已经走了。should最迷惑, should have left意思是「本该走却没走」, 是责备不是推测, 和门锁着的证据矛盾。考点: PSLE爱考must have done=对过去事情的肯定推断"},{"q":"You ___ not have eaten so much cake.","opts":["should","may","must","can"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"情态-should not have","explain":"should not have + 过去分词表示「本不该做却做了」, 事后责备吃太多蛋糕, 正合语境。must最迷惑, 但must not have done表示「一定没做过」, 是推测不是责备, 意思全反了。考点: PSLE爱考shouldn't have done=事后后悔责备句型"},{"q":"Students ___ hand in their work by Monday.","opts":["can","must","may","might"],"ans":3,"diff":3,"tag":"情态-must要求","explain":"must 表示硬性要求, by Monday 是死线, 老师规定没商量。may/can 只是『可以』, 没有强制意味; might 是『可能』, 更弱。考点: PSLE 爱考截止日期 by + 时间配 must 表强制。"},{"q":"She ___ be the new teacher. She looks very young.","opts":["mustn't","won't","can't","shouldn't"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"情态-can't否定推测","explain":"can't表示否定推测「不可能是」: 她看着太年轻, 不可能是新老师。mustn't最迷惑, 很多孩子以为must的推测否定还用must, 但mustn't只表示「不准」, 推测的否定必须换成can't。考点: PSLE爱考推测否定, must be的反面是can't be不是mustn't be"},{"q":"You ___ hurry — the bus does not leave for another hour.","opts":["can't","oughtn't to","mustn't","needn't"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"情态-needn't","explain":"needn't = 不必, 后半句说巴士还有一小时才开, 所以不用赶。mustn't 是禁止, 『不准赶』不合情理; can't 是不能; oughtn't to 是不该。考点: PSLE 爱考 needn't 不必 vs mustn't 禁止, 靠后半句语境判断。"},{"q":"He ___ to apologize for his rude behaviour.","opts":["need","must","should","ought"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"情态-ought to","explain":"空格后有to, 只有ought能接to, ought to = should表示应该道歉。should最迷惑, 意思完全对但should后面直接跟动词原形, 不能加to, 填进去变should to就错了。考点: PSLE爱考ought to是唯一带to的情态词, 看到to锁定ought"},{"q":"You ___ better hurry or you will miss the bus.","opts":["could","had","should","would"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"情态-had better","explain":"had better是固定短语「最好快点」, 否则误车, 只有had能填。should最迷惑, 意思相近但没有should better这个搭配, 想表达同义得说should hurry。考点: PSLE爱考had better+动词原形, 固定搭配不能拆开换字"},{"q":"I ___ rather stay home than go out in the rain.","opts":["had","could","should","would"],"ans":3,"diff":3,"tag":"情态-would rather","explain":"would rather...than...是固定句型「宁愿在家也不出门」, 只能用would。had最迷惑, 因为有had better这个近亲, 孩子容易串台, 但rather只跟would搭。考点: PSLE爱考would rather配than, 和had better别混成一家"},{"q":"She ___ have arrived by now. The flight was at 6.","opts":["can","mustn't","should","needn't"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"情态-should have预期","explain":"should have + 过去分词表示「按理现在该到了」, 航班6点起飞, 这是合理预期。must最迷惑, must have arrived是「肯定已经到了」, 但说话人其实没把握, 只是推算时间, 语气过头。考点: PSLE爱考should have done表按理该发生的预期"},{"q":"Need I ___ this form?","opts":["filled","filling","to fill","fill"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"情态-need原形","explain":"Need放句首当情态动词用, 后面必须接动词原形fill, 「我需要填这张表吗」。to fill最迷惑, 因为need也能当普通动词接to do, 但那样句子得写成Do I need to fill, 这里Need已提前, 只能配原形。考点: PSLE爱考need双重身份, 情态用法后接原形"},{"q":"You ___ as well take a taxi. The bus is late.","opts":["must","can","should","may"],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"情态-may as well","explain":"may as well是固定短语「不如就」, 公交晚点, 不如打车, 只有may能填。must最迷惑, 看着语气通顺, 但英语里没有must as well这个搭配, 固定短语一个字都不能换。考点: PSLE爱考may as well=不如做某事, 整体记不拆字"},{"q":"He ___ swim across the river when he was young.","opts":["was able to","can","could have","is able to"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"情态-was able to具体","explain":"was able to表示过去的能力, when he was young是过去时间, 只有它时态对。could have最迷惑, could have swum意思是「本可以游但没游」, 表示没发生的事, 和陈述他当年会游泳矛盾。考点: PSLE爱考过去能力用could/was able to, could have done是没做成"},{"q":"Mandarin, Malay and Tamil ___ as official languages in Singapore, along with English.","opts":["is recognised","have recognised","recognise","are recognised"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"被动-一般现在","explain":"三种语言是『被承认』, 要用被动; 主语是三个并列名词, 复数配 are。最迷惑的是 is recognised, 语态对了但主谓不一致; along with English 不计入主语。考点: PSLE 爱考被动+主谓一致双重判断。"},{"q":"The homework ___ before dinner.","opts":["must be finished","must finish","finishing","must finished"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"被动-情态","explain":"作业是被完成的, 情态动词的被动是must be + 过去分词, 所以must be finished。must finished最迷惑, 有过去分词像被动, 但情态动词后不能直接跟分词, 中间必须夹be。考点: PSLE爱考情态被动公式must/can/should+be+done, be不能省"},{"q":"Several houses ___ by the floods before the rescue teams arrived.","opts":["have been destroyed","were destroyed","had been destroyed","destroyed"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"被动-过去","explain":"房子在救援队到达(过去)之前就已经被毁, 过去的过去+被动 = had been destroyed。最迷惑的是 were destroyed, 语态对但分不出先后; have been 是现在完成, 和 arrived 打架。考点: PSLE 爱考 before + 过去时, 主句用过去完成被动。"},{"q":"A new school ___ in our area next year.","opts":["builds","will build","will be built","built"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"被动-将来","explain":"学校是被建的, next year定将来时, 将来被动=will be + 过去分词, 选will be built。will build最迷惑, 将来时对了但是主动语态, 意思变成「学校自己去盖楼」, 主语是物必须被动。考点: PSLE爱考将来被动will be done, 时态和语态两关都要过"},{"q":"The missing wallet ___ to the police station by a passer-by this morning.","opts":["was handed","handed","has handed","is handed"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"被动-过去","explain":"钱包是『被交到』警局, 被动; this morning 已过去, 用 was handed。最迷惑的是 handed, 变成钱包自己交东西; has handed 是主动完成时, 意思反了。考点: PSLE 爱考主语是物+by 某人 = 被动。"},{"q":"These books ___ to the library tomorrow.","opts":["return","returned","will be returned","returning"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"被动-将来","explain":"tomorrow是将来信号词, 书是「被还」, 将来被动 = will be + 过去分词, 选 will be returned。最迷惑的是 returned, 单独用像过去式, 既没有will也没有be, 时态和语态双错。考点: PSLE爱考时间信号词定时态, 被动还要补齐 be。"},{"q":"The letter ___ already ___.","opts":["has/been sent","was/send","is/sending","had/sent"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"被动-现在完成","explain":"already是现在完成时信号词, 完成时被动 = has been + 过去分词, 拆开就是 has...been sent。最迷惑的是 was/sent, 看着通顺, 但 already 强调「已经完成、影响到现在」, 该用 present perfect 不用 past。考点: PSLE爱考 already/just/yet 配 has been done。"},{"q":"The bridge ___ being repaired when we passed.","opts":["is","was","has","had"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"被动-过去进行","explain":"when we passed 是过去的时间点, 桥当时正在被修, 过去进行被动 = was being repaired, 所以填 was。最迷惑的是 is, 后面接 being 结构没错, 但和过去的 when 从句时态打架。考点: PSLE爱考主句从句时态要一致。"},{"q":"She ___ given a prize for her hard work at last month's ceremony.","opts":["is","was","has","had"],"ans":1,"diff":3,"tag":"被动-间接宾语","explain":"奖已经发了, 是过去发生的事, 过去被动 = was + given, 选 was。最迷惑的是 had, 有人以为 had given 是完成时, 但那是主动语态「她给了别人」, 意思全反。考点: PSLE爱考人做主语的被动句, be动词不能丢。"},{"q":"It is only ten o'clock, but all the tickets ___ sold out.","opts":["are being","had been","were being","have been"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"被动-现在完成","explain":"It is only ten o'clock 把全句锚在现在, 票『已经卖光』强调现在的结果, 用现在完成被动 have been sold。最迷惑的是 had been, 过去完成要有更晚的过去参照点, 这里是现在。考点: PSLE 爱考 have been 和 had been 的分界线, 先找句子锚在哪个时间。"},{"q":"The winners ___ at the ceremony next Friday, so do not miss it.","opts":["will be announced","will announce","are announcing","have been announced"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"被动-将来","explain":"获胜者是『被宣布』, next Friday 定将来, 用 will be announced。最迷惑的是 will announce, 变成获胜者自己去宣布; have been announced 是已经宣布了, 和 do not miss it 矛盾。考点: PSLE 爱考将来被动 will be done。"},{"q":"He ___ known to be a generous man.","opts":["has","was being","being","is"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"被动-be known","explain":"be known 是固定被动表达, 「他是出了名的慷慨」是现在的事实, 用 is known。最迷惑的是 has, has known 是主动完成时「他认识...」, 主语变成认识别人的人, 意思错。考点: PSLE爱考 be known to/as/for 固定搭配。"},{"q":"The meeting ___ postponed until Friday.","opts":["is been","has been","was being","has"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"被动-现在完成","explain":"会议「已被推迟」到周五, 强调现在的结果, 现在完成被动 = has been postponed。最迷惑的是 was being, 过去进行被动指「当时正被推迟中」, 推迟是一瞬间的决定, 不能进行中。考点: PSLE爱考推迟取消类动词配 has been。"},{"q":"You will fail ___ you study harder.","opts":["if","because","unless","although"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"连词-unless","explain":"unless = if...not, 「除非你更用功, 否则会不及格」, 逻辑通。最迷惑的是 if, 「如果你更用功就会不及格」意思完全反了, 很多孩子只看结构不读意思就掉坑。考点: PSLE爱考 unless 藏着否定, 翻成「除非」再检查逻辑。"},{"q":"He ran fast ___ he could catch the bus.","opts":["unless","although","so that","because"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"连词-so that目的","explain":"跑得快是为了赶上巴士, 表目的用 so that, 后面常配 could/can。最迷惑的是 because, 「因为能赶上巴士所以跑得快」因果颠倒, 目的和原因方向相反。考点: PSLE爱考 so that + can/could 表目的。"},{"q":"Do not leave your seats ___ the bus has come to a complete stop.","opts":["although","until","while","because"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"连词-until","explain":"『在巴士完全停稳之前不要离座』, 动作持续到某时刻用 until。最迷惑的是 while, 『当巴士停稳时不要离座』逻辑反了。考点: PSLE 爱考 not...until 表『直到...才』。"},{"q":"___ I finish my work, I will join you.","opts":["Once","Unless","Although","Because"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"连词-once","explain":"Once = 一旦...就..., 「一旦做完作业就来找你」, 时间顺承通顺。最迷惑的是 Unless, 「除非我做完否则来找你」意思拧了, 两句是先后关系不是条件否定。考点: PSLE爱考 once 表「一...就」, 从句用现在时代替将来时。"},{"q":"She is ___ kind ___ helpful, so everyone in class likes her.","opts":["neither/nor","both/and","not/but","either/or"],"ans":1,"diff":3,"tag":"连词-both...and","explain":"kind 和 helpful 两个优点都有, 用 both...and。either/or 是二选一, neither/nor 是全否定, 都和后半句『大家都喜欢她』矛盾; not...but 是『不是A而是B』, 两个优点不构成对立。考点: PSLE 爱考成对连词看前后语义。"},{"q":"___ only is he smart, ___ also hardworking.","opts":["Both/and","Not/but","Either/or","Neither/nor"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"连词-not only...but also","explain":"Not only...but also 固定搭配「不但...而且」, 首词 Not 对上题目里的 only, 后半 but 对上 also。最迷惑的是 Both/and, both 后面不能接 only, and 也和句尾 also 不搭。考点: PSLE爱考 not only 放句首, 拿题目已给的 only 和 also 当钥匙。"},{"q":"You can have ___ tea ___ coffee, but not both.","opts":["neither/nor","not/but","either/or","both/and"],"ans":2,"diff":3,"tag":"连词-either...or","explain":"茶或咖啡二选一, 用 either...or。最迷惑的是 both...and, 「两个都要」在 can have 的语境也说得通, 但二选一的口气加上「或者」逻辑, either/or 才是标准答案。考点: PSLE爱考 either...or 选一个、neither...nor 全否定、both...and 全都要。"},{"q":"I like swimming ___ my brother prefers running.","opts":["unless","while","so","because"],"ans":1,"diff":3,"tag":"连词-while对比","explain":"我爱游泳、哥哥爱跑步, 两人对比用 while「而」。最迷惑的是 because, 「因为哥哥爱跑步所以我爱游泳」毫无因果, 硬套就错。考点: PSLE爱考 while 表两人两事对比, 不只是「当...时候」。"},{"q":"___ hard she tried, she could not solve it.","opts":["Unless","However","Although","Because"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"连词-however让步","explain":"However + 形容词/副词 = 无论多么..., 「无论多努力都解不出」, 直接修饰 hard。最迷惑的是 Although, 意思接近但语法不容许 Although hard she tried 这种语序, although 后要接完整句子。考点: PSLE爱考 however + adj/adv + 主语的倒装式让步。"},{"q":"Take an umbrella ___ it rains.","opts":["because","unless","although","in case"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"连词-in case","explain":"in case = 以防万一, 「带伞以防下雨」, 是预防不是原因。最迷惑的是 because, 「因为下雨所以带伞」好像也通, 但句子说的是还没下雨先防着, 不是已经在下。考点: PSLE爱考 in case 表预防, 和 because 用「事情发生没有」区分。"},{"q":"She speaks ___ she were the boss.","opts":["so that","because","as if","although"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"连词-as if","explain":"as if = 好像, 「她说话好像她是老板似的」, 后面配 were 表示假设不是事实。最迷惑的是 so that, 表目的要配 can/could, 这里没有, 且「为了当老板而说话」不通。考点: PSLE爱考 as if + were 表虚拟, she 后接 were 不是错。"},{"q":"I have not seen him ___ he left Singapore.","opts":["until","while","since","because"],"ans":2,"diff":3,"tag":"连词-since","explain":"since + 过去时间点, 主句用现在完成时 have not seen, 「自从他离开就没见过」完全吻合。最迷惑的是 until, 「直到他离开才没见他」逻辑混乱, until 配的是动作的终点不是起点。考点: PSLE爱考 have done + since 黄金组合, 见完成时先找 since。"},{"q":"___ having revised for weeks, Mei Ling still found the paper difficult.","opts":["Despite","However","Although","Even though"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"连词-although","explain":"空格后是 having revised(动名词短语), 不是完整句子, 只能用介词 Despite。最迷惑的是 Although/Even though, 意思对但它们是连词, 后面必须接主语+动词; However 是副词, 不能引导从句。考点: PSLE 爱考 despite/in spite of + 名词或 V-ing vs although + 句子。"},{"q":"I don't suppose you have seen my keys anywhere, ___?","opts":["have you","haven't you","do I","don't I"],"ans":0,"diff":6,"tag":"反问-be肯→否","explain":"I don't suppose/think + 从句, 反问尾巴跟从句走且主句已带否定, 所以用肯定 have you。最迷惑的是 don't I, 看着主语 I 就配 I, 但这类句子的尾巴看从句主语 you。考点: PSLE 顶档反问题 I don't think..., do you? 固定按从句配尾巴。"},{"q":"Mr Tan used to teach at this school, ___?","opts":["wasn't he","didn't he","hadn't he","usedn't he"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"反问-do否→肯","explain":"used to 当一般过去处理, 反问尾巴用 didn't he。最迷惑的是 usedn't he, 现代英语已基本不用; wasn't he 把 used 当成 be 动词是错的。考点: PSLE 爱考 used to 的反问用 did。"},{"q":"Everything has to be cleared from the hall by noon, ___?","opts":["hasn't it","isn't it","doesn't it","doesn't they"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"反问-can","explain":"has to 是实义动词 have to, 不是完成时的助动词 has, 反问要用 does 家族: doesn't it。最迷惑的是 hasn't it, 看到 has 就直接照搬。everything 回指用 it。考点: PSLE 爱考 have to 的尾巴用 do/does/did。"},{"q":"Let's go to the park, ___?","opts":["will we","shall we","do we","can we"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"反问-let's","explain":"Let's开头的建议句是固定搭配, 尾巴一律用shall we, 表示邀请对方一起。选will we错在: Let's句不看主语将来时, 这是死规矩不是推理题。考点: PSLE爱考Let's..., shall we固定句型"},{"q":"You won't tell anyone, ___?","opts":["do you","don't you","will you","won't you"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"反问-won't→will","explain":"won't是否定, 尾巴反过来用肯定will you, 助动词沿用will。最迷惑的是won't you: 前后都否定就重复了, 违反前否后肯规则。考点: PSLE爱考缩写词里藏着的否定(won't=will not)"},{"q":"There is a book on the table, ___?","opts":["are there","isn't there","aren't there","is there"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"反问-there is","explain":"There is句型的尾巴把there当主语用, 肯定句配否定尾巴isn't there。选aren't there错在: 主语a book是单数, 动词必须保持is, 不能换成are。考点: PSLE爱考there be句型反问用there不用it"},{"q":"She has finished her work, ___?","opts":["did she","hasn't she","has she","didn't she"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"反问-has完成","explain":"句子用了现在完成时has finished, 尾巴沿用has变否定hasn't she。最迷惑的是didn't she: finished看着像过去式, 但前面有has坐镇, 是完成时不是过去时。考点: PSLE爱考has+过去分词的尾巴用hasn't不用didn't"},{"q":"Nobody came to the party, ___?","opts":["did they","did he","didn't they","didn't he"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"反问-nobody","explain":"Nobody本身含否定意思, 尾巴要用肯定did they; nobody回指时惯用they。选didn't they错在: 前句已经否定(nobody=没人), 尾巴再否定就双重否定了。考点: PSLE爱考nobody/no one自带否定且代词用they"},{"q":"I am late, ___?","opts":["aren't I","don't I","am I","isn't I"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"反问-I am特殊","explain":"I am的反问是英语特例, 没有amn't I这个词, 一律借用aren't I。选isn't I错在: is配he/she/it, 从来不配I, 纯属生造。考点: PSLE爱考I am..., aren't I?这个不讲理的特殊搭配"},{"q":"Everyone enjoyed the show, ___?","opts":["didn't he","don't they","didn't they","did they"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"反问-everyone","explain":"everyone语法上是单数但反问代词用they, 前句enjoyed是过去时肯定句, 尾巴用didn't they。最迷惑的是didn't he: everyone不指某个男生, 回指必须用they。考点: PSLE爱考everyone/everybody尾巴代词统一用they"},{"q":"She said, \"I am tired.\" → She said that she ___ tired.","opts":["was","has been","is","will be"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"间接引语-am→was","explain":"直接引语变间接引语, 主句said是过去时, 引语里的时态要跟着退一步: am退成was。选is错在: 报告过去说的话, 现在时不退等于没换挡, said和is时态打架。考点: PSLE爱考reported speech时态倒退一格(backshift)"},{"q":"He said, \"I will come.\" → He said he ___ come.","opts":["can","shall","would","will"],"ans":2,"diff":3,"tag":"间接引语-will→would","explain":"said是过去时, 引语里的will要退成would, 这是情态动词的倒退规则。选will错在: 主句已是过去, will原地不动就和said不配套了。考点: PSLE爱考will→would/can→could成对倒退"},{"q":"Tom said, \"I have finished.\" → Tom said he ___ finished.","opts":["having","has","had","have"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"间接引语-have→had","explain":"said过去时带动引语时态后退: have finished(现在完成)退成had finished(过去完成)。选has错在: 主语he本可配has, 但间接引语必须倒退, has没退到位。考点: PSLE爱考现在完成时转述后变past perfect"},{"q":"She asked, \"Do you like coffee?\" → She asked ___ I liked coffee.","opts":["do","if","what","that"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"间接引语-一般疑问","explain":"转述一般疑问句(yes/no问题)要用if或whether来引导, 表示是否。最迷惑的是that: that只转述陈述句, 转述问题就把疑问的味道弄丢了。考点: PSLE爱考yes/no问句转述用if/whether引导"},{"q":"He asked, \"Where do you live?\" → He asked where I ___.","opts":["living","had lived","lived","live"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"间接引语-特殊疑问","explain":"转述特殊疑问句, where后面改用陈述语序, 时态跟asked倒退: live退成lived。选live错在: 语序改对了但时态没退, asked是过去, 引语也要过去。考点: PSLE爱考wh-问句转述要变陈述语序+时态倒退"},{"q":"She told me, \"Don't be late.\" → She told me ___ be late.","opts":["don't","to not","not to","didn't"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"间接引语-祈使否定","explain":"否定祈使句转述的固定公式: told sb not to do, not放在to前面。最迷惑的是to not: 意思能懂但语序错, 标准写法not to才拿分。考点: PSLE爱考Don't...转述成told sb not to do"},{"q":"\"Can you help me?\" she asked. → She asked if I ___ help her.","opts":["will","may","can","could"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"间接引语-can→could","explain":"asked是过去时, 引语里的can倒退成could, 情态动词也要跟着换挡。选can错在: 主句过去时, can不退就和asked不同步了。考点: PSLE爱考间接引语can→could/may→might倒退"},{"q":"He said, \"I saw her yesterday.\" → He said he ___ her the day before.","opts":["had seen","has seen","sees","saw"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"间接引语-saw→had seen","explain":"直接引语里的过去时saw, 转述时再退一格变过去完成had seen, 因为看的动作发生在说之前的之前。最迷惑的是saw: 只退了主句没退引语, yesterday变the day before也提示要双重后退。考点: PSLE爱考simple past转述后变had+过去分词"},{"q":"Mum said, \"Clean your room.\" → Mum told me ___ my room.","opts":["cleaning","to clean","clean","cleaned"],"ans":1,"diff":3,"tag":"间接引语-祈使肯定","explain":"肯定祈使句转述公式: told sb to do sth, 动词前必须加to。选clean错在: 直接照抄原话的动词原形, 忘了转述要套to do的壳。考点: PSLE爱考祈使句转述用tell/ask sb to do"},{"q":"\"I am leaving tomorrow,\" she said. → She said she was leaving ___.","opts":["tomorrow","today","yesterday","the next day"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"间接引语-时间转换","explain":"转述时时间词也要换算: tomorrow从说话那天算, 转述后变the next day/the following day。最迷惑的是tomorrow: 现在转述时那个明天早过了, 不换就时间错乱。考点: PSLE爱考间接引语时间词换算(tomorrow→the next day)"},{"q":"___ of the twins has a completely different hobby.","opts":["Both","All","Each","Every"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"限定-every单数","explain":"只有 each 能接 of, 且 each of 配单数动词 has。最迷惑的是 Every, 意思相近但 every 后面不能接 of; All/Both 配复数动词 have。考点: PSLE 爱考 each of(可以) vs every of(不存在)。"},{"q":"___ of the students have passed the test, but a few need to retake it.","opts":["Much","Each","Every","Most"],"ans":3,"diff":3,"tag":"限定-most of","explain":"Most of + the + 复数名词配复数动词 have, 后半句 a few 也说明不是全部。Each 要配单数 has, 和 have 冲突; Every 不能接 of; Much 只修饰不可数名词。考点: PSLE 爱考 Most/Each/Every/Much 接 of 的合法性和主谓一致。"},{"q":"There is ___ point in arguing with him.","opts":["not","none","any","no"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"限定-no+名词","explain":"固定短语 there is no point in doing something = 做某事没意义, no直接放名词point前面。not最迷惑, 但not是副词, 不能直接修饰名词, 要说not any point才行。考点: PSLE爱考no+名词的固定搭配, no=not any"},{"q":"Hurry up! We have ___ time to waste.","opts":["a little","few","a few","little"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"限定-little否定意","explain":"time是不可数名词, 又要表达「几乎没有时间」的否定意味, 用little。a little最迷惑, 它是肯定意「还有一点」, 和to waste(不能浪费)的语气矛盾。few只配可数名词。考点: PSLE爱考little/few配可数不可数+有无a的褒贬"},{"q":"___ information was given to us.","opts":["Little","Many","A few","Few"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"限定-little不可数","explain":"information是不可数名词, 「几乎没给什么信息」用Little。Few最迷惑, 意思也是「很少」, 但few只能修饰可数复数名词, information永远不可数不加s。考点: PSLE爱考information/advice/news这类不可数名词的限定词"},{"q":"He ate ___ whole cake by himself!","opts":["much","the","an","many"],"ans":1,"diff":3,"tag":"限定-the特指","explain":"whole cake 特指他吃掉的那一整个, 用 the; cake 单数可数, many/much 都不能直接修饰; whole 辅音开头不用 an。考点: PSLE 爱考 the whole + 单数名词。"},{"q":"The fire alarm went ___ in the middle of the lesson and everyone had to evacuate.","opts":["off","on","out","up"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"短语动词-turn off","explain":"go off = (警报)响起, 是固定搭配。最迷惑的是 go on, 是『继续/发生』; go out 是『熄灭』, 和警报响不搭。考点: PSLE 爱考 go off 的多义: 警报响/食物变质/炸弹爆炸。"},{"q":"I need to look ___ this word in the dictionary.","opts":["for","at","into","up"],"ans":3,"diff":3,"tag":"短语动词-look up查找","explain":"look up=在词典里查(单词), 是查字典的专用搭配。look for最迷惑, 意思是「寻找丢失的东西」, 查生词的意思要用look up, in the dictionary就是信号。考点: PSLE爱考look up/look for/look at的区分, 见dictionary选up"},{"q":"She takes ___ her mother in appearance.","opts":["after","on","up","off"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"短语动词-take after像","explain":"take after=长得像(长辈), in appearance(外貌上)是明显信号。take on最迷惑, 意思是「承担/呈现」, 不能表示和妈妈长得像。这类phrasal verb意思和字面无关, 要整个背。考点: PSLE爱考take after表「像家人」, 配mother/father必考"},{"q":"We must carry ___ the experiment carefully.","opts":["off","out","in","on"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"短语动词-carry out执行","explain":"carry out=执行/进行(实验、计划), carry out the experiment是科学课标准搭配。carry on最迷惑, 意思是「继续」, 后面一般接doing或不接宾语, 不和experiment搭配成「做实验」。考点: PSLE爱考carry out+experiment/plan/instructions"},{"q":"He turned ___ the job offer because the pay was low.","opts":["down","on","off","up"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"短语动词-turn down拒绝","explain":"turn down=拒绝(工作、邀请), 后半句because the pay was low说明他不要这份工作。turn off最迷惑, 只表示关电器, 不能拒绝offer。看到offer/invitation+拒绝理由就选down。考点: PSLE爱考turn down拒绝vs turn off关闭"},{"q":"The new club has really taken ___ since it opened — membership has tripled.","opts":["off","up","on","in"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"短语动词-take off起飞","explain":"take off 在这里是『突然走红/迅速发展』, 后半句 membership has tripled 是线索。最迷惑的是 take up(开始学某项活动)和 take on(承担), 都接不上『会员翻三倍』。考点: PSLE 爱考 take off 的引申义, 不只是飞机起飞。"},{"q":"I can't make ___ what the sign says.","opts":["out","in","off","up"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"短语动词-make out辨认","explain":"make out=辨认出、看清(模糊的字或东西), can't make out=看不清招牌写什么。make up最迷惑, 是「编造」, 但这里不是编故事而是看不清, sign(招牌)提示是视觉辨认。考点: PSLE爱考make out辨认vs make up编造, 看语境定"},{"q":"She made ___ a story to avoid punishment.","opts":["out","in","up","off"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"短语动词-make up编造","explain":"make up=编造(故事、借口), 为了逃避惩罚编了个故事, made up a story是固定搭配。make out最迷惑, 是「辨认」, 辨认故事说不通, to avoid punishment说明是撒谎编的。考点: PSLE爱考make up+story/excuse表编造"},{"q":"Please fill ___ this form and return it.","opts":["on","up","in","away"],"ans":2,"diff":3,"tag":"短语动词-fill in填写","explain":"fill in = 填写(表格), fill in the form 是标准说法。最迷惑的是 fill up, 那是『装满(油箱/杯子)』, 不用于表格; fill away/fill on 不存在。考点: PSLE 爱考 fill in + form。"},{"q":"He set ___ on his journey early in the morning.","opts":["in","down","off","up"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"短语动词-set off出发","explain":"set off = 出发、启程, set off on a journey 是固定搭配。最迷惑的是 set up(建立)和 set down(放下/写下), 都和出发无关。考点: PSLE 爱考 set off + journey 表出发。"},{"q":"They called ___ the meeting due to the storm.","opts":["up","off","on","in"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"短语动词-call off取消","explain":"call off=取消(会议、活动), 因为暴风雨把会议取消了, due to the storm是原因信号。call on最迷惑, 意思是「拜访/号召」, 和取消完全不同。想成: call off=cancel。考点: PSLE爱考call off+meeting/match表因故取消"},{"q":"I ran ___ my old teacher at the market.","opts":["off","into","out","on"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"短语动词-run into偶遇","explain":"run into=偶然遇见(人), 在市场碰到老师是巧遇, run into=meet by chance。run out最迷惑, 因为run out of很常见, 但那是「用完」, 后面接的是物不是人。遇到人+地点就是偶遇。考点: PSLE爱考run into偶遇vs run out of用完"},{"q":"She looks ___ to her older sister.","opts":["after","up","into","down"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"短语动词-look up to敬佩","explain":"look up to=敬佩、仰慕(某人), 妹妹敬佩姐姐, 注意句尾已有to, 所以填up。look after最迷惑, 是「照顾」, 但look after后面不加to, 句中的to已经把答案锁定在up。考点: PSLE爱考三词phrasal verb, 看句尾的to选look up to"},{"q":"Don't give ___. Keep trying!","opts":["up","on","off","out"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"短语动词-give up放弃","explain":"give up = 放弃, 后一句 Keep trying! 正好呼应『别放弃』。最迷惑的是 give out(分发/耗尽)和 give off(散发气味), 都接不上鼓励语境; give on 不存在。考点: PSLE 爱考 give up 放弃 vs give out 分发。"},{"q":"He went ___ his notes before the exam.","opts":["up","on","over","off"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"短语动词-go over复习","explain":"go over=温习、复查(笔记), 考试前把笔记过一遍, before the exam是信号。go on最迷惑, 是「继续/发生」, went on his notes说不通。想成: go over=revise。考点: PSLE爱考go over+notes/work表复习检查"},{"q":"We need to cut ___ on our expenses.","opts":["up","out","down","off"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"短语动词-cut down减少","explain":"cut down on=减少(开支、糖分), 是三词固定搭配, on已经在句子里, 填down。cut off最迷惑, 是「切断(水电、通话)」, 不和on连用。看到on our expenses就锁定cut down on。考点: PSLE爱考cut down on+expenses/sugar表削减"},{"q":"She stood ___ for her friend when others bullied him.","opts":["up","in","out","by"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"短语动词-stand up for","explain":"stand up for=挺身维护(某人), 别人欺负朋友时她站出来保护, 句中for是信号, 填up凑成三词短语。stand by最迷惑, 也有「支持某人」的意思, 但stand by后面直接接人不再加for, 句里的for已排除它。考点: PSLE爱考stand up for维护vs stand by支持"},{"q":"A fight broke ___ between the two groups shortly after the match ended.","opts":["up","off","out","down"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"短语动词-break down坏","explain":"break out = (打斗/战争/火灾)突然爆发, 固定搭配。最迷惑的是 break down(机器坏/情绪崩溃)和 break up(分手/解散), 都不能形容打斗爆发。考点: PSLE 爱考 break out 配 fight/fire/war。"},{"q":"He gets ___ well with his classmates.","opts":["along","in","off","up"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"短语动词-get along相处","explain":"get along (well) with = 和某人相处融洽。最迷惑的是 get up(起床)和 get off(下车), 都和相处无关; get in 是进入。考点: PSLE 爱考 get along with + 人表相处好坏。"},{"q":"The second paper was ___ harder than the first, so many pupils ran out of time.","opts":["more","very","too","far"],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"比较级-more","explain":"比较级 harder 前面只能用 far/much/a lot 加强, 不能用 very。最迷惑的是 very, very 只能加强原级(very hard); more harder 是双重比较; too 不和 than 配。考点: PSLE 爱考 much/far + 比较级 vs very + 原级。"},{"q":"The river was ___ shallow for the boat to pass through.","opts":["too","very","enough","so"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"副词-too...to","explain":"too + 形容词 + for sb/sth + to do = 太...以至于不能, 固定结构。最迷惑的是 so, so shallow 后面要接 that 从句不接 for...to; enough 要放在形容词后面。考点: PSLE 爱考 too...for...to 和 so...that 的结构区别。"},{"q":"She speaks English ___ fluently.","opts":["quieter","quietest","quite","quiet"],"ans":2,"diff":3,"tag":"副词-quite修饰","explain":"quite是副词, 修饰fluently, quite fluently意思是说得相当流利。quiet最迷惑, 长得像但意思是安静, 是形容词, 放这里意思和词性都不对。考点: PSLE爱考quite和quiet这对双胞胎, 拼写多个e差很远"},{"q":"Of the three sisters, Mei is ___ at the piano.","opts":["the more skilful","the most skilful","most skilful","more skilful"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"最高级-the","explain":"三者比较用最高级且前面要 the: the most skilful。最迷惑的是 the more skilful, 比较级只用于两者; most skilful 不加 the 在考试里视为不完整。考点: PSLE 爱考 of the three + the + 最高级。"},{"q":"The ___ the weather, the happier I feel.","opts":["best","more good","good","better"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"比较级-the...the","explain":"the...the...是越...越...句型, 两边都要放comparative, good的比较级是better。more good错, good是不规则变化, 直接变better, 不能加more。考点: PSLE爱考the+比较级双联句和good-better-best不规则变化"},{"q":"The ___ you practise, the ___ mistakes you will make.","opts":["more / fewer","most / fewest","more / less","much / few"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"比较级-副词","explain":"the...the... 越...越... 两边都用比较级; mistakes 是可数复数, 用 fewer 不用 less。最迷惑的是 more / less, 前半对了但 less 只修饰不可数名词。考点: PSLE 爱考 the 比较级双联句 + fewer/less 可数不可数。"},{"q":"She would not risk ___ her savings on such a doubtful business plan.","opts":["lose","lost","to lose","losing"],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"不定式-decide+to","explain":"risk 后面固定接动名词 losing, 和 avoid/mind/enjoy 同一阵营。最迷惑的是 to lose, 很多人凭语感加 to, 但 risk to do 是病句。考点: PSLE 爱考 risk/avoid/consider/practise + V-ing。"},{"q":"I look forward to ___ you soon.","opts":["seen","see","saw","seeing"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"动名词-look forward to+ing","explain":"look forward to里的to是preposition介词, 介词后面动词要变ing, 所以是seeing。see最迷惑, 很多人以为to后面接原形, 但这个to不是不定式的to。考点: PSLE爱考look forward to+ing, 是介词陷阱题的老面孔"},{"q":"She stopped ___ when the teacher came in.","opts":["talked","talking","to talk","talk"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"动名词-stop+ing停止做","explain":"stop+ing表示停止正在做的事, 老师进来她停止讲话, 用talking。to talk错, stop to talk是停下来去讲话, 意思刚好相反, 不合情境。考点: PSLE爱考stop doing和stop to do意思相反, 看情境选"},{"q":"He forgot ___ the door, so the burglar simply walked in.","opts":["locked","locking","lock","to lock"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"不定式-forget+to忘记要做","explain":"forget+to表示忘了去做该做的事, 他忘了锁门, 门没锁上, 用to lock。locking错, forget locking是忘了自己锁过门, 门其实锁了, 意思不符。考点: PSLE爱考forget to do和forget doing, 事做没做是分水岭"},{"q":"I suggest ___ early to avoid the traffic.","opts":["left","leave","to leave","leaving"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"动名词-suggest+ing","explain":"suggest后面固定接gerund, suggest leaving表示建议早点出发。to leave错, suggest不接to+动词, 这是和decide相反的一批词, 要分开背。考点: PSLE爱考suggest/recommend+ing, 不接不定式"},{"q":"The teacher does not allow ___ in class, but she lets us drink water.","opts":["to eat","eat","ate","eating"],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"不定式-agree+to","explain":"allow 后面没有宾语时接动名词 eating(allow doing); 有宾语才是 allow sb to do。最迷惑的是 to eat, allow to eat 中间缺了人。考点: PSLE 爱考 allow/permit doing vs allow sb to do。"},{"q":"She can't help ___ whenever she sees a puppy.","opts":["smile","to smile","smiling","smiled"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"动名词-can't help+ing","explain":"can't help+ing是固定搭配, 意思是忍不住做某事, 所以选smiling。to smile最迷惑, help单独用确实接to, 但can't help是整体短语, 规则完全不同。考点: PSLE爱考can't help doing=忍不住, 当整块背下来"},{"q":"Would you mind ___ the window?","opts":["opening","opened","open","to open"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"动名词-mind+ing","explain":"mind后面固定接gerund, Would you mind opening是请人帮忙的礼貌句式。to open错, mind只接ing, 不接不定式, 这是硬性搭配。考点: PSLE爱考Would you mind+ing礼貌请求句型"},{"q":"He pretended ___ asleep when his mother came.","opts":["to be","being","been","be"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"不定式-pretend+to","explain":"pretend后面固定接to+动词, pretend to be asleep表示假装睡着。being错, pretend属于只接infinitive的动词, 不能接ing。考点: PSLE爱考pretend/decide/refuse+to do这批不定式动词"},{"q":"The box of chocolates on the top shelf ___ meant for the guests.","opts":["is","are","were","have"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"主谓-插入短语","explain":"主语是 The box(单数), of chocolates on the top shelf 全是修饰语, 划掉后剩 The box ___ meant, 所以用 is。选 are/were 的同学被离动词最近的 chocolates/shelf 带偏了。考点: PSLE Editing 和语法题最爱在主语和动词之间塞介词短语, 先划掉 of/on/in 引导的修饰语再判断单复数。"},{"q":"My cousin, as well as her two brothers, ___ joining us for dinner tonight.","opts":["was","is","be","are"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"主谓-as well as","explain":"as well as 引导的是附加成分, 不是并列主语, 主语仍然是单数 My cousin, 所以用 is。选 are 的同学把 her two brothers 也算进主语了 — 只有 and 才能把两个名词合成复数主语。考点: PSLE 爱用 as well as / along with / together with / besides 制造假复数, 看到逗号插入语先划掉再看主语。"},{"q":"Neither the coach nor the players ___ satisfied with the referee's decision.","opts":["has","was","is","were"],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"主谓-neither nor就近","explain":"neither...nor 连接的主语按就近原则看最靠近动词的那个, 这里是 the players(复数), 所以用 were。选 was 的同学按前面的 the coach 判断了 — 如果顺序反过来写成 Neither the players nor the coach was..., 才轮到 was。考点: PSLE 故意把单数放前复数放后, 逼你用就近原则而不是数人头。"},{"q":"A number of students ___ absent from school because of the haze yesterday.","opts":["were","has been","was","is"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"主谓-a number of","explain":"a number of = 许多, 中心词是后面的复数名词 students, 动词用复数 were; the number of(数量)才是单数。yesterday 定过去时, 排除 has been/is。考点: PSLE 死磕 a number of(复数)和 the number of(单数)这一对。"},{"q":"She is one of those pupils who ___ never late for lessons.","opts":["was","is","are","has"],"ans":2,"diff":6,"tag":"主谓-one of those who","explain":"who 的先行词是 those pupils(复数), 从句动词用 are; 主句的 She is 已经用过单数了, 从句不能重复。选 is 的同学把先行词误认成 one 了。考点: one of + 复数名词 + who/that + 复数动词, 是 PSLE 拉开 AL1 和 AL3 的经典分水岭题。"},{"q":"Each of the three classes ___ been given a plot in the school garden to look after.","opts":["have","were","having","has"],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"主谓-each of单数","explain":"Each of + 复数名词做主语时中心词是 Each(单数), 用 has been given。选 have 的被 the three classes 带偏; were been given 结构不成立; having 不能单独做谓语。考点: PSLE Editing 高频 — Each/Every/Either/Neither/One of 开头一律当单数。"},{"q":"The team's ___ to finish the project on time impressed the judges.","opts":["determined","determinedly","determining","determination"],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"词形-所有格后接名词","explain":"空格前是所有格 The team's, 后面必须接名词, 所以用 determination(决心)。determined 是形容词, determinedly 是副词, determining 是分词, 都不能被所有格直接修饰。考点: PSLE Editing 每篇必考词形转换, 判断方法是看空格前后 — 冠词或所有格后填名词, be 动词后填形容词, 实义动词后填副词。"},{"q":"Although the instructions were written ___, many pupils still misunderstood them.","opts":["clearer","clearly","clearest","clear"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"词形-副词修饰动词","explain":"修饰的是 were written 这个动作(怎么写的), 要用副词 clearly。clear 是形容词只能修饰名词; clearer 和 clearest 是比较级最高级, 句中没有比较对象。考点: PSLE Editing 常把形容词放在动词后面骗你, 记住修饰动作一律用副词。"},{"q":"We were given very little ___ about the change in the examination format.","opts":["information","informative","informations","informing"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"不可数名词-information","explain":"information 是不可数名词, 永远没有复数 informations, 也不能加 a/an; 空格前的 very little 正好只修饰不可数名词。informative 是形容词, informing 是分词, 都不能做 given 的宾语。考点: PSLE Editing 必考的不可数名词有 information / advice / furniture / luggage / equipment / homework, 一律不加 s。"},{"q":"There were ___ candidates this year, so the queue moved much faster.","opts":["lesser","less","little","fewer"],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"限定-fewer可数","explain":"candidates 是可数名词复数, 用 fewer; less 只修饰不可数名词(less water / less time)。lesser 是'较次要的', little 修饰不可数且不能直接接复数名词。考点: PSLE 反复考 fewer(可数)和 less(不可数)这一对, 先看后面的名词能不能加 s。"},{"q":"After ten years in Singapore, my father is used to ___ in such humid weather.","opts":["working","worked","works","work"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"动词搭配-be used to+ing","explain":"be used to 表示'习惯于', 这里的 to 是介词, 后面接动名词 working; 而 used to do 才是'过去常常做'。选 work 的同学把这两个结构搞混了。考点: PSLE 爱把 used to do 和 be/get used to doing 放进同一题, 先看 to 前面有没有 be 动词。"},{"q":"The workers stopped ___ their lunch when the fire alarm rang.","opts":["eat","eating","to eat","eaten"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"动词搭配-stop+ing","explain":"火警响了, 他们停下的是'正在吃'这个动作, stop doing = 停止做某事; stop to do 是'停下手边的事去做另一件', 那就变成停下来去吃饭, 和火警的语境相反。考点: PSLE 从不直接问规则, 而是给上下文让你判断 stop / remember / forget / try 后面该接 to do 还是 doing。"},{"q":"I clearly remember ___ the door before we left, so someone else must have opened it.","opts":["to lock","lock","locking","locked"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"动词搭配-remember+ing","explain":"后半句说'所以一定是别人打开的', 说明锁门这件事已经做过了, remember doing = 记得做过; remember to do 是'记得要去做'(还没做)。选 to lock 的同学没读后半句的逻辑。考点: PSLE 靠后半句的线索判断动作有没有发生, 这类题不看完整句必错。"},{"q":"While the children were rehearsing on stage, their teacher ___ the costumes backstage.","opts":["is ironing","had ironed","has ironed","was ironing"],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"时态-过去同时进行","explain":"While 从句用了 were rehearsing(过去进行), 表示两件事同时发生, 主句也要用过去进行 was ironing。is ironing 是现在进行, 时态对不上; had ironed / has ironed 表示先后完成, 和'同时'矛盾。考点: PSLE Editing 最爱在一段里混时态, 先找出全段的主时间轴再逐句对齐。"},{"q":"The shop has been closed ___ the owner fell ill last December.","opts":["from","since","for","during"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"完成时-since引导从句","explain":"since 后面可以接一个一般过去时的从句(the owner fell ill), 表示'自从…以来'; for 后面只能接时间长度(for three months); from 不与现在完成时搭配; during 后面接名词不接句子。考点: PSLE 常考 since + 时间点或从句 与 for + 时间段 的区别, 主句必须是完成时。"},{"q":"The government announced that bus fares would ___ by ten cents next month.","opts":["risen","rise","raise","arise"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"易混词-rise不及物","explain":"rise 是不及物动词, 主语自己上升, 票价自己涨用 rise; raise 是及物动词必须带宾语(raise fares 是人去涨价)。空格后面没有宾语, 所以选 rise。arise 是'(问题)出现', 不用于价格; risen 是过去分词, 前面得有 have。考点: PSLE 反复考 rise/raise 和 lie/lay 这两对及物与不及物。"},{"q":"The injured bird ___ motionless on the grass for almost an hour before it flew away.","opts":["lain","laid","lied","lay"],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"易混词-lie过去式lay","explain":"lie(躺)的过去式正好是 lay, 这里描述小鸟躺着不动, 用 lay。laid 是 lay(放置)的过去式且必须带宾语; lied 是 lie(说谎)的过去式; lain 是过去分词, 前面要有 had。考点: PSLE 最爱的动词三胞胎 lie-lay-lain(躺)、lay-laid-laid(放)、lie-lied-lied(说谎)。"},{"q":"The camp taught us how to pitch a tent, how to read a map and how ___ a fire safely.","opts":["build","we built","building","to build"],"ans":3,"diff":6,"tag":"平行结构-how to","explain":"句中三个 how 要长得一模一样: 前面是 how to pitch、how to read, 空格处也必须写成「to build」, 这叫平行结构。选「building」或「we built」都会把这排比打破。考点: PSLE 爱在列举三件事的句子里对最后一件下手, 照着前面两件的样子抄结构就行。"},{"q":"Mount Everest is higher than ___ mountain in the world.","opts":["any other","some other","all other","the other"],"ans":0,"diff":6,"tag":"比较-any other","explain":"比较级把一个成员和同组其他所有成员比, 用 any other + 单数名词。the other 指两者中的另一个; some other 只是『某些别的』不表示全部; all other 后面必须接复数 mountains, 和题干单数 mountain 不合。考点: PSLE 高频模板 higher than any other mountain, than 后名词用单数。"},{"q":"If the referee ___ that foul, our team would still be in the tournament.","opts":["were seeing","had seen","would see","has seen"],"ans":1,"diff":6,"tag":"虚拟-混合条件句","explain":"主句是 would still be(现在的结果), 从句说的却是过去没发生的事, 这是混合虚拟句, 从句要用过去完成 had seen。has seen 是真实完成时不表假设; would see 不能出现在 if 从句里。考点: PSLE 顶档题, 看主句用 would + 原形(现在结果)还是 would have + 过去分词(过去结果), 反推从句时态。"},{"q":"I ___ tell him about the meeting, but he seems to have forgotten completely.","opts":["do","was","did","have"],"ans":2,"diff":6,"tag":"强调-助动词did","explain":"后半句 seems to have forgotten 说明这是过去说过的事, 用 did + 动词原形 tell 表示强调'我确实说了'。do 时态不对; have 后面得跟过去分词 told; was 后面不能直接跟原形。考点: PSLE 用 do/does/did + 原形表强调, 常配 but 引出的转折。"},{"q":"No sooner ___ the ball than the whistle blew for full time.","opts":["did he kick","had he kicked","he had kicked","he did kick"],"ans":1,"diff":6,"tag":"倒装-no sooner than","explain":"No sooner 放句首要部分倒装, 且时态固定为 No sooner had + 主语 + 过去分词 ... than + 一般过去时, 表示'一…就…'。did he kick 用错了助动词; he had kicked 没有倒装。考点: PSLE 顶档倒装三兄弟 No sooner...than / Hardly...when / Scarcely...when, 时态搭配是死的。"},{"q":"This is the neighbour ___ we borrowed the ladder last weekend.","opts":["from whom","from that","from who","from which"],"ans":0,"diff":6,"tag":"关系代词-介词提前","explain":"介词 from 提到关系代词前面时, 后面只能接 whom(指人)或 which(指物), 不能用 who 或 that。先行词是 neighbour(人), 所以是 from whom。考点: PSLE 高分点 — 介词 + whom/which 结构, 记住 that 和 who 永远不能紧跟在介词后面。"},{"q":"___ by the sudden thunder, the toddler burst into tears.","opts":["Frightening","Frighten","Frightened","To frighten"],"ans":2,"diff":6,"tag":"分词-过去分词表被动","explain":"幼儿是'被'雷声吓到, 和 frighten 之间是被动关系, 用过去分词 Frightened。Frightening 是'令人害怕的', 那是形容雷声本身而不是孩子。考点: PSLE 用 -ed(感到…)和 -ing(令人…)这对分词考被动关系, 判断方法是看主语是感受者还是施加者。"},{"q":"You ___ have carried all those books — I had already brought a trolley.","opts":["needn't","can't","won't","mustn't"],"ans":0,"diff":6,"tag":"情态-needn't have过去多余","explain":"needn't have done = 其实没必要做却做了, 正好对应『我已经带了推车』。mustn't have 表达不了这个意思; won't have 时态不合; can't have carried 是『不可能搬过』, 和事实矛盾。考点: PSLE 顶档情态题, 靠后半句语境判断是白费力气。"},{"q":"There is hardly any milk left in the fridge, ___?","opts":["is there","isn't there","are there","was there"],"ans":0,"diff":6,"tag":"反问-hardly准否定","explain":"hardly 本身带否定意义, 整句算否定句, 所以反问部分用肯定形式 is there; 主语 milk 是不可数名词, 对应 is 不用 are。选 isn't there 的同学漏看了 hardly。考点: PSLE 把 hardly / scarcely / seldom / rarely / few / little 一律当否定词处理, 反问用肯定。"},{"q":"\"You may leave once you have finished,\" the invigilator said. → The invigilator said we ___ leave once we had finished.","opts":["can","might","may","must"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"间接引语-may→might","explain":"转述过去说的话, 情态动词要后移: may→might, can→could, will→would。选 may 的同学漏了这一步; must 和 can 都改变了原意。考点: PSLE 间接引语固定考三件事 — 人称变、时态退一步、时间地点词换(tomorrow→the next day)。"}];

// 3. Cloze 单空填 (~40 道)
const CLOZE_QUESTIONS = [{"sentence":"She arrived ___ Singapore last week.","opts":["to","in","at","on"],"ans":1,"diff":3,"explain":"arrive in配大地方, 新加坡是国家所以arrive in Singapore。最迷惑的是at: arrive at配小地点如at the airport。另外arrive绝不配to。考点: PSLE爱考arrive in大地方at小地点"},{"sentence":"I am interested ___ science.","opts":["on","about","in","at"],"ans":2,"diff":3,"explain":"interested in是固定搭配, 对什么感兴趣就in什么。最迷惑的是about: 中文'关于科学很感兴趣'会误选about, 英语只认in。考点: PSLE爱考interested in, 每年都出"},{"sentence":"Don't laugh ___ him!","opts":["with","at","of","to"],"ans":1,"diff":3,"explain":"laugh at somebody是嘲笑某人, 固定词组。最迷惑的是with: laugh with him是跟他一起笑, 意思完全反了, 这里是别嘲笑他。考点: PSLE爱考laugh at表嘲笑"},{"sentence":"We will meet ___ Monday.","opts":["at","in","on","from"],"ans":2,"diff":3,"explain":"星期几前面用on, on Monday雷打不动。最迷惑的是at: at配钟点如at 8 am, 不配星期。口诀: at点on天in月。考点: PSLE爱考星期前用on"},{"sentence":"She is married ___ a doctor.","opts":["of","to","with","at"],"ans":1,"diff":3,"explain":"married to是固定搭配, 嫁给/娶了谁都用to。最迷惑的是with: 中文'和医生结婚'直译就选with, 这是经典中式英语陷阱, 英语只说married to。考点: PSLE爱考married to不用with"},{"sentence":"I came ___ this old photo in the attic.","opts":["on","across","at","through"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"phrasal","explain":"come across是偶然发现、无意中碰到, 正好配旧照片这个情景。最迷惑的是through: come through是熬过去、挺过来, 跟发现照片无关。考点: PSLE爱考phrasal verb, come across=偶遇"},{"sentence":"Please look ___ the children while I go out.","opts":["into","at","for","after"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"phrasal","explain":"look after是照顾, 我出门你照看孩子, 意思吻合。最迷惑的是for: look for是寻找, 孩子没丢不用找。look at是看一眼, 也不对。考点: PSLE爱考look家族词组, after照顾for寻找into调查"},{"sentence":"The fire broke ___ at midnight.","opts":["in","off","down","out"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"phrasal","explain":"break out专指火灾、战争、疾病突然爆发, 半夜起火就是broke out。最迷惑的是down: break down是机器坏掉或人崩溃, 火不会break down。考点: PSLE爱考break out=灾祸爆发"},{"sentence":"He gave ___ smoking last year.","opts":["out","up","in","off"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"phrasal","explain":"give up是戒掉、放弃, 戒烟就是give up smoking。最迷惑的是in: give in是让步投降, 对烟让步反而是继续抽, 意思拧了。考点: PSLE爱考give up+动名词表戒除"},{"sentence":"They put ___ the meeting to next week.","opts":["out","off","in","down"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"phrasal","explain":"put off是推迟, 会议挪到下周正是推迟。最迷惑的是out: put out是扑灭火, 会议不能扑灭。put down是放下或写下, 也不搭。考点: PSLE爱考put off=postpone推迟"},{"sentence":"Despite ___ tired, he kept working.","opts":["was","being a","to be","being"],"ans":3,"diff":5,"explain":"Despite是介词, 后面只能接名词或动名词, 所以用being。最迷惑的是to be: 介词后不能接to do不定式, 这是硬规矩。was更不行, 介词后没动词原形句。考点: PSLE爱考despite+V-ing结构"},{"sentence":"___ hearing the fire alarm, the pupils were dismissed from the hall immediately.","opts":["At","By","In","Upon"],"ans":3,"diff":5,"explain":"upon + V-ing 表示'一…就…', Upon hearing = On hearing = As soon as they heard。at/by/in 都不能直接接 hearing 构成这个意思。考点: PSLE 爱考 upon/on + 动名词表'随即发生'。"},{"sentence":"She was so engrossed ___ the book.","opts":["at","on","with","in"],"ans":3,"diff":5,"explain":"engrossed in是固定搭配, 全神贯注沉浸在书里。最迷惑的是with: 中文'被书迷住'像被动会想选with, 但engrossed只配in, 跟absorbed in同款。考点: PSLE爱考engrossed/absorbed in表入迷"},{"sentence":"I prefer reading ___ watching TV.","opts":["more","to","than","rather"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"explain":"prefer 的固定句型是 prefer + 前者 + to + 后者, 整句就是 prefer reading to watching TV, 这里的「to」是介词不是不定式。最迷惑的是「than」: 看到比较就想用than, 但prefer不配than, 只配to。考点: PSLE爱考prefer...to...不用than"},{"sentence":"He had no choice ___ to apologize.","opts":["rather","but","then","than"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"explain":"have no choice but to do是固定句型, 别无选择只好道歉。最迷惑的是than: 长得像比较句就选than, 但这个词组里定死用but, but后接to do。考点: PSLE爱考no choice but to do"},{"sentence":"After working tirelessly for ten hours under the scorching sun, the construction workers were ___ exhausted.","opts":["slightly","hardly","barely","utterly"],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"context-vocab","explain":"utterly 意思是'彻底地', 烈日下干了十小时, 累到极点, utterly exhausted 是固定强化搭配。slightly 程度太轻, hardly 和 barely 都是'几乎不', 意思正好反了。考点: 程度副词要和语境强度匹配。"},{"sentence":"Although the storm warning was issued early, many residents ___ to evacuate, hoping the typhoon would change course.","opts":["agreed","hurried","accepted","refused"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"context-vocab","explain":"refused「拒绝」才通: 后半句说居民盼台风改道, 说明他们不肯撤离。although提示前后转折, 警报早发但没人走。agreed最迷惑, 同意撤离的话就跟「盼台风转向」矛盾了。考点: PSLE爱考although转折逻辑, 空格要和后半句心态一致。"},{"sentence":"The teacher reminded the class that ___ a complete sentence requires both a subject and a verb.","opts":["constructs","constructing","constructed","construct"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"context-grammar","explain":"that从句里空格是主语, 动词当主语要用gerund(动名词), 所以constructing对, 「造一个完整句子需要主谓」。construct最迷惑, 原形动词不能直接当主语, 后面已有requires这个真动词。考点: PSLE爱考动名词作主语, 一句只能有一个主要动词。"},{"sentence":"By the time the firefighters arrived, the entire building ___ to the ground.","opts":["had burned","was burning","burned","has burned"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"context-grammar-pluperfect","explain":"By the time是past perfect信号词: 消防员到之前, 楼已经烧光, 更早发生的动作用had burned。was burning最迷惑, 进行时表示「正在烧」, 但句意是烧完塌了(to the ground), 动作已结束。考点: PSLE爱考by the time + 过去时, 主句配had + p.p.。"},{"sentence":"Despite ___ the fastest runner in the school, Ahmad lost the race because he tripped over a stone.","opts":["is","been","to be","being"],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"context-grammar-despite","explain":"Despite是preposition, 后面只能接noun或gerund, 所以用being。been最迷惑, 它是过去分词, 前面必须有have/has/had才成立, 不能单独跟在despite后。考点: PSLE爱考despite/in spite of + V-ing, although才接完整句子。"},{"sentence":"The librarian, ___ patience with the noisy children was wearing thin, finally asked them to leave.","opts":["whose","whom","who","which"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"context-grammar-whose","explain":"空格后的patience是名词, 表示「图书管理员的耐心」, 名词前表所属要用whose。who最迷惑, 它做从句主语, 但这里主语是patience, 不缺主语, 缺的是「谁的」。考点: PSLE爱考关系代词, 空格后紧跟名词就选whose。"},{"sentence":"If I ___ harder for the test, I would not have failed it.","opts":["have studied","study","had studied","studied"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"context-grammar-conditional3","explain":"主句是would not have failed, 这是third conditional(对过去的假设), if从句必须配had studied, 「当初要是多用功就不会挂」。studied最迷惑, 它是second conditional的搭配, 假设现在而不是过去。考点: PSLE爱考would have + p.p.反推if从句用had + p.p.。"},{"sentence":"The detective examined the crime scene ___, looking for any clue that might have been overlooked.","opts":["meticulously","randomly","barely","quickly"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"context-vocab-adv","explain":"meticulously「一丝不苟地」和后半句「找任何可能被漏掉的线索」完美呼应, 侦探查案就该细致。quickly最迷惑, 查得快不等于查得细, 和「不放过线索」的语境对不上。考点: PSLE爱考副词与语境呼应, 先读完整句再选。"},{"sentence":"The phenomenon, ___ scientists had long theorized about, was finally observed in the laboratory.","opts":["which","whom","what","that"],"ans":0,"diff":6,"tag":"context-relative-clause","explain":"从句被两个逗号夹住, 是non-defining relative clause, 只能用which, 补充说明phenomenon。that最迷惑, 平时它能代物, 但有逗号的非限定从句里that被禁用, 这是铁规。考点: PSLE爱考逗号+关系代词, 见逗号排除that。"},{"sentence":"Had the government ___ stricter measures earlier, the outbreak could have been contained.","opts":["implementing","implement","to implement","implemented"],"ans":3,"diff":6,"tag":"context-subjunctive-inversion","explain":"Had the government...是倒装的third conditional, 等于If the government had implemented, had后面接过去分词implemented。implement最迷惑, 看到had像该接原形, 但这个had是助动词, 必须配p.p.。考点: PSLE爱考Had + 主语 + p.p.的省略if倒装句。"},{"sentence":"The CEO was ___ criticized for her decision that she eventually resigned from her position.","opts":["very severely","such severely","so severely","too severely"],"ans":2,"diff":6,"tag":"context-so...that","explain":"后面有that she resigned, 是so...that句型「批评得如此严厉以至于辞职」, 修饰副词severely用so。such severely最迷惑, such只能配名词(such a harsh critic), 不能直接接副词。考点: PSLE爱考so+adj/adv+that与such+名词+that的区分。"},{"sentence":"The teacher asked us to pay ___ to her explanation.","opts":["notice","mind","focus","attention"],"ans":3,"diff":3,"tag":"collocation-pay attention","explain":"pay attention to是固定搭配「注意听」, pay只能配attention, 这是collocation死规矩。notice最迷惑, take notice of也表注意, 但动词是take不是pay, 混搭就错。考点: PSLE爱考动词+名词固定搭配, 记词组要连动词一起背。"},{"sentence":"He always takes ___ in his work.","opts":["priding","pride","proud","proudly"],"ans":1,"diff":3,"tag":"collocation-take pride","explain":"take pride in是固定搭配「以...为荣」, take后面要接noun, pride是名词形式。proud最迷惑, 它是adjective, 该用在be proud of里, 跟take不搭。考点: PSLE爱考同根词选词性, 看前面动词定名词还是形容词。"},{"sentence":"She made a good ___ on her new teacher.","opts":["idea","impression","opinion","expression"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"collocation-make impression","explain":"make an impression on是固定搭配「给...留下印象」, 对新老师留下好印象用impression。expression最迷惑, 长得像但意思是「表情/表达」, make a good expression不成立。考点: PSLE爱考形近词impression/expression, 靠搭配make...on辨认。"},{"sentence":"We need to make a ___ about where to eat.","opts":["deciding","decisive","decision","decide"],"ans":2,"diff":3,"tag":"collocation-make decision","explain":"make a decision是固定搭配「做决定」, 冠词a后面必须接noun, decision是名词。decide最迷惑, 意思对但它是verb, a后面不能放动词原形。考点: PSLE爱考make/take + 名词搭配, 见冠词就选名词形式。"},{"sentence":"He took ___ of the opportunity to travel.","opts":["benefit","use","profit","advantage"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"collocation-take advantage","explain":"take advantage of是固定词组「利用(机会)」, 三个词绑死不能换。benefit最迷惑, 意思也和好处相关, 但搭配是benefit from, 不跟take...of连用。考点: PSLE爱考三件套短语take advantage of, 整组背不拆开。"},{"sentence":"The news came as a great ___ to everyone.","opts":["shocking","shock","shocked","shocks"],"ans":1,"diff":3,"tag":"collocation-come as shock","explain":"come as a shock是固定表达「令人震惊」, a后面接noun, shock作名词。shocking最迷惑, 它是adjective, a shocking后面还得再加名词才完整, 单放句尾就错。考点: PSLE爱考a/an后接名词, 同根词看词性下手。"},{"sentence":"She bears a strong ___ to her mother.","opts":["resemblance","resembling","resemble","resembled"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"collocation-bear resemblance","explain":"bear a strong resemblance to 是固定搭配'长得很像', a strong 后面必须接名词, resemblance 是名词形式。resemble 是动词, resembling/resembled 是分词, 都不能被 a strong 修饰。考点: PSLE 爱考同根词选词性, 冠词+形容词后面一定是名词。"},{"sentence":"He made an ___ to help the old woman.","opts":["affect","effect","effort","afford"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"collocation-make effort","explain":"make an effort是固定搭配「努力」, an提示元音开头名词, effort正好。effect最迷惑, 拼写像但意思是「效果」, make an effect to help不通。考点: PSLE爱考形近词effort/effect/affect, 用搭配make an effort to锁答案。"},{"sentence":"The company suffered heavy ___ last year.","opts":["losses","losing","lost","lose"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"collocation-suffer losses","explain":"suffer losses是固定搭配「蒙受损失」, heavy后面要接noun, 商业亏损常用复数losses。lost最迷惑, 它是动词过去式或形容词, 不能当heavy修饰的名词。考点: PSLE爱考lose/loss/lost三兄弟, 形容词后面选名词loss(es)。"},{"sentence":"Please do me a ___ and close the window.","opts":["good","favour","help","kind"],"ans":1,"diff":3,"tag":"collocation-do favour","explain":"do someone a favour是固定搭配「帮个忙」, favour是名词配do。help最迷惑, 意思全对, 但英语只说do me a favour或give me some help, do me a help不存在。考点: PSLE爱考favour/help的动词搭配差异, 按词组整套记。"},{"sentence":"The students were told to keep ___ during the test.","opts":["silence","quietly","silently","quiet"],"ans":3,"diff":3,"tag":"collocation-keep quiet","explain":"keep quiet是固定搭配「保持安静」, keep后接adjective作补语, quiet是形容词。quietly最迷惑, 副词修饰动作, 但keep在这里是linking verb, 要接形容词描述状态。考点: PSLE爱考linking verb(keep/stay/remain)后用形容词不用副词。"},{"sentence":"She takes after her father in many ___.","opts":["sides","parts","things","ways"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"collocation-in many ways","explain":"in many ways是固定表达「在许多方面」, 说她像爸爸的地方很多。things最迷惑, 中文直译「很多事情」好像通, 但英语谈相似点只用ways, in many things不地道。考点: PSLE爱考固定短语in many ways, 别用中文直译选词。"},{"sentence":"I have no ___ but to agree with him.","opts":["choose","choice","chose","chosen"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"collocation-have no choice","explain":"have no choice but to是固定句型「别无选择只能」, no后面接noun, choice是名词。choose最迷惑, 它是verb, no后面不能直接放动词原形。考点: PSLE爱考choice/choose词性区分, no/the/a后面一律选名词。"},{"sentence":"He lost his ___ and shouted at the waiter.","opts":["temper","mood","anger","feeling"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"collocation-lose temper","explain":"lose one's temper是固定搭配「发脾气」, 后面冲服务员大吼正是发火。anger最迷惑, 意思也是怒气, 但lose his anger反而像「消气」, 搭配错意思也反。考点: PSLE爱考idiom原装搭配lose one's temper, 换近义词就丢分。"},{"sentence":"We caught a ___ of the famous actor at the airport.","opts":["view","glance","look","glimpse"],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"collocation-catch glimpse","explain":"catch a glimpse of 是固定搭配'瞥见一眼'。glance 是主动扫一眼, 配 take/cast(take a glance at); look 配 take/have; view 不与 catch a 连用。考点: glimpse/glance 这对形近词的动词搭配。"},{"sentence":"The heavy rain ___ havoc on the crops.","opts":["made","gave","wreaked","did"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"collocation-wreak havoc","explain":"wreak havoc 是固定搭配'造成严重破坏'。make/do/give 都不能和 havoc 组成这个意思。考点: 整组背 wreak havoc on。"},{"sentence":"Nobody at the table knew each other, so she broke the ___ by telling a joke.","opts":["cold","quiet","ice","air"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"collocation-break the ice","explain":"break the ice 是习语'打破陌生/尴尬气氛', 前半句说大家互不相识, 讲笑话就是暖场。air/quiet/cold 都不与 break the 组成这个意思。考点: idiom 整体意思, 不能逐字直译。"},{"sentence":"He has a good ___ of humour.","opts":["feeling","meaning","taste","sense"],"ans":3,"diff":3,"tag":"collocation-sense of humour","explain":"a sense of humour是固定搭配「幽默感」, sense表示对某种东西的感知力。最迷惑的是feeling: feeling是情绪感受, 不和of humour搭配, 英语里只说sense of humour。考点: PSLE爱考sense of搭配(sense of humour/direction/responsibility)"},{"sentence":"The students must hand ___ their essays by Friday.","opts":["off","up","out","in"],"ans":3,"diff":3,"tag":"collocation-hand in提交","explain":"hand in是phrasal verb「上交」, 交作业给老师就用hand in。最迷惑的是hand up: 举手是put up your hand, hand up不是交东西的意思, 别被「向上交」的中文思维骗了。考点: PSLE爱考phrasal verb, hand in交/hand out发/hand over移交要分清"},{"sentence":"She kept an ___ on the children while they played.","opts":["look","eye","watch","attention"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"collocation-keep eye on","explain":"keep an eye on是习语「照看、留意」, 妈妈看着玩耍的孩子就是这个词组。最迷惑的是watch: keep watch要说keep watch on(不加an), 空格前有an, 只能填eye。考点: PSLE爱考idiom里的冠词细节, an后面跟的词是关键线索"},{"sentence":"The weather was cold. ___, we decided to go hiking.","opts":["Nevertheless","Unless","Since","Because"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"connector-nevertheless","explain":"前句天冷, 后句照样去远足, 意思相反转折, Nevertheless「尽管如此」正合适。最迷惑的是Because: 天冷不是去远足的原因, 逻辑反了; 而且Because不能单独放句首带逗号这样用。考点: PSLE爱考connector逻辑方向, 先判断两句是顺着说还是对着说"},{"sentence":"He studied hard. ___, he failed the exam.","opts":["Furthermore","Therefore","Moreover","However"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"connector-however","explain":"努力学习却考砸, 前后结果出乎意料, However表转折最对。最迷惑的是Therefore: 它表因果「所以」, 用了就变成努力所以不及格, 逻辑完全反了。考点: PSLE爱考However和Therefore对换设陷阱, 抓句意方向再选"},{"sentence":"She was tired. ___, she continued working.","opts":["Thus","Therefore","Nonetheless","Hence"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"connector-nonetheless","explain":"很累却继续工作, 转折关系, Nonetheless=nevertheless「尽管如此」。最迷惑的是Therefore: 累了「所以」继续工作说不通, 因果词放转折句就是错。考点: PSLE爱考Nonetheless这类高级转折词, 记住它和However是一家"},{"sentence":"The road was flooded. ___, we took a detour.","opts":["Nevertheless","However","Moreover","Therefore"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"connector-therefore","explain":"路淹了「所以」绕道走, 前因后果, Therefore正确。最迷惑的是Nevertheless: 它表转折, 用了就成「路淹了但我们还是绕道」, 绕道明明是被逼的结果不是对着干。考点: PSLE爱考因果connector, 问自己后句是不是前句导致的"},{"sentence":"He is smart. ___, he is also hardworking.","opts":["However","Nevertheless","Therefore","Moreover"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"connector-moreover","explain":"聪明「而且」还勤奋, 两个优点往上叠加, Moreover表递进。最迷惑的是However: also已经提示是补充不是转折, 两句都是夸人, 方向一致不能用转折词。考点: PSLE爱考递进词Moreover/Furthermore, 看到also就找加法词"},{"sentence":"The food was delicious. ___, the service was excellent.","opts":["However","Nevertheless","Furthermore","Instead"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"connector-furthermore","explain":"菜好吃「而且」服务也棒, 两句都在夸, Furthermore表递进补充。最迷惑的是However: 好吃和服务好不矛盾, 没有转折; Instead更错, 没有替代关系。考点: PSLE爱考connector, 先判断两句是同方向(加法)还是反方向(转折)"},{"sentence":"She did not study. ___, she did not pass.","opts":["Nevertheless","Moreover","However","Consequently"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"connector-consequently","explain":"没学习「结果」没及格, 标准因果, Consequently=as a result。最迷惑的是However: 不学习和不及格顺理成章, 一点不意外, 转折词放这就是逻辑错误。考点: PSLE爱考Consequently这类结果词, 和Therefore/Hence是一家"},{"sentence":"He was not invited. ___, he went to the party.","opts":["Furthermore","Therefore","Nevertheless","Moreover"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"connector-nevertheless","explain":"没被邀请「却还是」去了派对, 出乎意料的转折, Nevertheless正确。最迷惑的是Therefore: 没被邀请「所以」去派对完全讲不通, 因果方向反了。考点: PSLE爱考转折connector, 后句和前句唱反调就选Nevertheless家族"},{"sentence":"The show was cancelled ___ the heavy rain.","opts":["due to","however","despite of","although"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"connector-due to","explain":"due to+名词表原因「由于大雨」, 空格后是名词短语the heavy rain, 语法意思都对。最迷惑的是despite of: 这是经典陷阱, despite后面直接加名词, 根本没有despite of这个说法, 而且转折意思也不对。考点: PSLE爱考due to/because of接名词, despite of是永远的错误选项"},{"sentence":"___ his wealth, he lives a simple life.","opts":["Despite","Because","Although","Since"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"connector-despite+名词","explain":"Despite+名词「尽管有钱却过得简朴」, 空格后his wealth是名词短语, 只有Despite能直接带名词。最迷惑的是Although: 意思也是转折, 但Although后面必须接完整句子(主语+动词), 不能接名词短语。考点: PSLE爱考Despite+名词 vs Although+句子的结构区别"},{"sentence":"He was ill. ___, he stayed home.","opts":["However","Hence","Nevertheless","Moreover"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"connector-hence","explain":"生病「因此」待在家, 因果关系, Hence=therefore「所以」。最迷惑的是However: 生病待在家理所当然, 没有意外转折, 用However逻辑就断了。考点: PSLE爱考Hence/Thus/Therefore三胞胎, 都是因果词可互换"},{"sentence":"The project was difficult. ___, we managed to finish it.","opts":["Therefore","Hence","Consequently","Nonetheless"],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"connector-nonetheless","explain":"项目很难「但我们还是」完成了, managed暗示克服困难, Nonetheless表转折。最迷惑的是Therefore: 难「所以」完成说不通, 另外三个全是因果词, 只有Nonetheless是转折。考点: PSLE爱考排除法, 三个选项同类时答案往往是落单的那个"},{"sentence":"She enjoys reading. ___, she loves writing stories.","opts":["Nevertheless","However","In addition","Therefore"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"connector-in addition","explain":"爱读书「另外」也爱写故事, 两个爱好叠加, In addition表递进。最迷惑的是However: 读和写是好朋友不是对头, 没有转折; 看到后句和前句同方向就用加法词。考点: PSLE爱考In addition/Moreover/Furthermore递进三件套"},{"sentence":"He is not only smart ___ also kind.","opts":["and","but","or","yet"],"ans":1,"diff":3,"tag":"connector-not only but also","explain":"not only...but also是固定关联词组「不但…而且」, 中间只能填but。最迷惑的是and: 单独看smart and kind没错, 但前面出现了not only, 就必须配套用but also, 拆散词组就丢分。考点: PSLE爱考not only...but also配对连词, 见到前半必接后半"},{"sentence":"I want to go; ___, I have no time.","opts":["furthermore","however","moreover","therefore"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"connector-semicolon however","explain":"想去「但是」没时间, 分号加逗号中间放转折副词however, 意思结构都对。最迷惑的是therefore: 想去「所以」没时间讲不通, 前后是愿望和现实的冲突, 必须转折。考点: PSLE爱考分号+connector+逗号的标点结构, however最常驻"},{"sentence":"___ the fact that he was sick, he came to school.","opts":["Despite","Since","Because","Due to"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"connector-despite the fact","explain":"Despite the fact that+句子「尽管他病了」, 这是despite带从句的唯一方式。最迷惑的是Due to: 后面接the fact that语法也通, 但「因为生病所以来上学」逻辑不通, 带病上学是转折。考点: PSLE爱考Despite the fact that整串结构, 先过语法再过逻辑"},{"sentence":"She arrived late ___ of the traffic jam.","opts":["despite","because","in spite","although"],"ans":1,"diff":3,"tag":"connector-because of","explain":"because of+名词「因为塞车」, 空格后有of, 只有because能和of组队表原因。最迷惑的是in spite: in spite of语法上也成立, 但意思变成「尽管塞车她还是迟到了」, 塞车明明是迟到的原因不是被克服的困难。考点: PSLE爱考because of vs in spite of, 语法都对时拼逻辑"},{"sentence":"He worked hard ___ that he could earn more money.","opts":["because","despite","so","although"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"connector-so that","explain":"so that表目的「为了能多赚钱」而拼命工作, so...that前有could更是目的从句标志。最迷惑的是because: 空格后已有that, because that不是英语说法; 而且赚钱是目的不是原因。考点: PSLE爱考so that目的从句, 空格后的that是解题钥匙"},{"sentence":"We waited for an hour. ___, the bus did not come.","opts":["Still","Moreover","Furthermore","Therefore"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"connector-still","explain":"等了一小时「可是」车还是没来, Still放句首表「尽管如此、还是」, 是转折。最迷惑的是Therefore: 等了一小时「所以」车不来? 车来不来不由你等多久决定, 因果不成立, 只能转折。考点: PSLE爱考Still当转折connector用, 别只记它「仍然」的副词义"},{"sentence":"___ to popular belief, bats are not blind.","opts":["Contrary","Despite","Although","However"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"connector-contrary to","explain":"Contrary to popular belief 是固定搭配, 意思是「和大家想的相反」, 只有 Contrary 能配 to。最迷惑的 Despite 后面直接接名词, 不带 to, 而且意思是「尽管」不是「相反」。考点: PSLE爱考固定搭配介词, contrary to 要整块背下来。"},{"sentence":"By the time she ___ home, her parents had already gone to bed.","opts":["reached","reaches","reaching","has reached"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"tense-context-past perfect","explain":"By the time 后面用 simple past (reached), 主句用 past perfect (had gone), 表示她到家前父母已睡了。最迷惑的 reaches 是现在式, 和后半句 had already gone 的过去时间对不上。考点: PSLE爱考 by the time + past 搭配 had done 的时态组合。"},{"sentence":"She ___ in this school since 2020.","opts":["teaches","taught","has taught","is teaching"],"ans":2,"diff":3,"tag":"tense-context-present perfect since","explain":"since 2020 表示从2020年一直教到现在, 动作延续到今天, 要用 present perfect: has taught。最迷惑的 taught 是 simple past, 意思是过去教过、现在不教了, 和 since 矛盾。考点: PSLE爱考 since/for + 时间段 定 present perfect。"},{"sentence":"The children ___ when the teacher walked in.","opts":["have talked","talk","talked","were talking"],"ans":3,"diff":3,"tag":"tense-context-past continuous","explain":"老师走进来那一刻, 孩子们「正在」讲话, 长动作被短动作打断, 用 past continuous: were talking。最迷惑的 talked 只说他们讲过话, 表达不出「当时正在进行、被撞见」的画面。考点: PSLE爱考 when + walked in 打断进行中动作, 选 was/were doing。"},{"sentence":"If it ___ tomorrow, we will cancel the picnic.","opts":["will rain","raining","rains","rained"],"ans":2,"diff":3,"tag":"tense-context-conditional 1","explain":"这是 first conditional: if 从句用 simple present (rains), 主句才用 will。虽然说的是明天, if 后面也不能加 will。最迷惑的 will rain 就是掉进这个坑, if 从句禁用 will。考点: PSLE爱考条件句 If + present, main clause + will 的公式。"},{"sentence":"By the time the guests arrived, Mother ___ all the dishes.","opts":["prepares","prepared","had prepared","has prepared"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"tense-context-past perfect after","explain":"客人到达(过去)之前, 妈妈就已经把菜都做好了 —— 更早发生的那件事用过去完成时「had prepared」。选「prepared」的把两件事说成同时发生, 而 By the time 这个结构恰恰要求前一件已经完成; 「has prepared」是现在完成时, 和过去的 arrived 对不上。PSLE 陷阱: By the time + 过去时从句, 主句必须用过去完成时, 这里不能省。"},{"sentence":"When she reached the front door, she realised that she ___ her keys at the office.","opts":["has left","leaves","is leaving","had left"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"tense-context-past perfect result","explain":"realised 是过去时, 钥匙落在办公室是比'意识到'更早的过去, 用过去完成时 had left。has left 是现在完成, 和过去的 realised 不同框; leaves/is leaving 时态全错。考点: 过去的过去用 had + p.p.。"},{"sentence":"I ___ this book yet. Can I keep it longer?","opts":["did not finish","do not finish","am not finishing","have not finished"],"ans":3,"diff":3,"tag":"tense-context-present perfect yet","explain":"yet 配否定句, 表示到现在还没读完, 而且还想继续借, 影响延续到当下, 用 present perfect: have not finished。最迷惑的 did not finish 是过去式, 说的是过去某次没读完, 和 yet 不搭。考点: PSLE爱考 yet/already/just 信号词定 present perfect。"},{"sentence":"While she ___ the dishes, she heard a loud crash.","opts":["was washing","has washed","is washing","washed"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"tense-context-while past cont","explain":"While 引导正在进行的长动作(洗碗), 中途被巨响打断, 用 past continuous: was washing。最迷惑的 is washing 时态是现在, 但 heard 已锁定整句在过去, 前后要一致。考点: PSLE爱考 while + was/were doing 搭配 simple past 的打断句型。"},{"sentence":"He promised that he ___ help us move house.","opts":["shall","would","can","will"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"tense-context-reported future","explain":"主句 promised 是过去式, 宾语从句要跟着退一步, will 变 would, 这叫 reported speech 时态后移。最迷惑的 will 就是没退时态, 主句过去从句不能停在将来式。考点: PSLE爱考 said/promised/told 后从句 will→would 的时态一致。"},{"sentence":"By next year, they ___ married for 25 years.","opts":["will have been","have been","were","are"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"tense-context-future perfect","explain":"By next year 表示「到明年为止」将满25年, 用 future perfect: will have been。最迷惑的 have been 只说到「现在」为止, 缺了 will, 够不到明年那个时间点。考点: PSLE爱考 by + 将来时间 定 will have + p.p.。"},{"sentence":"Before I ___ you, I had never eaten durian.","opts":["met","had met","meet","have met"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"tense-context-before past","explain":"Before I met you: 从句用 simple past, 主句「从没吃过榴莲」是更早的经历, 已用了 had never eaten。最迷惑的 had met 把 past perfect 放错位置, 一句里更早的动作才用 had, 从句这边只需 met。考点: PSLE爱考 before/after 句中 had + p.p. 该放哪半句。"},{"sentence":"The concert ___ already ___ by the time we arrived.","opts":["is/starting","has/started","was/starting","had/started"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"tense-context-past perfect already","explain":"我们到场之前音乐会已开始, 更早的动作用 past perfect: had already started, already 插在 had 和 started 中间。最迷惑的 has/started 是 present perfect, 但 by the time we arrived 锁定全句在过去, has 不能用。考点: PSLE爱考 by the time + arrived 搭配 had + p.p.。"},{"sentence":"Don't call me at 8 pm. I ___ dinner then.","opts":["have","will be having","had","have had"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"tense-context-future continuous","explain":"晚上 8 点这个将来时刻我会'正在'吃饭, 用 future continuous: will be having。have/had/have had 都表达不出'将来某一刻正在进行'。考点: 将来某时刻正在做的事选 will be + doing。"},{"sentence":"She ___ English since she was five years old.","opts":["learned","has been learning","learns","is learning"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"tense-context-present perfect continuous","explain":"since she was five 表示从五岁一直学到现在还在学, 用 present perfect continuous: has been learning。最迷惑的 learned 是过去式, 意思是学过但停了, 和 since 的「延续到现在」冲突。考点: PSLE爱考 since + 过去时间点 定 has been doing/has done。"},{"sentence":"The letter ___ yesterday but I haven't read it yet.","opts":["had arrived","has arrived","arrives","arrived"],"ans":3,"diff":3,"tag":"tense-context-simple past yesterday","explain":"yesterday 是明确的过去时间, 信到达用 simple past: arrived。最迷惑的 has arrived 是 present perfect, 它不能和 yesterday 这种具体过去时间连用, 这是铁规则。考点: PSLE爱考 yesterday/last week 与 present perfect 不能同框。"},{"sentence":"I ___ to Paris before, so I know the way around.","opts":["had been","went","have been","go"],"ans":2,"diff":3,"tag":"tense-context-present perfect experience","explain":"before 在这里指「以前去过」, 是到现在为止的人生经历, 用 present perfect: have been, 所以现在才认路。最迷惑的 went 是过去式, 需要具体过去时间配合, 而且接不上后半句「现在认路」的效果。考点: PSLE爱考 have been to 表经历, before/ever 是信号词。"},{"sentence":"The ___ student was praised by the principal for his excellent results.","opts":["diligent","lazy","careless","naughty"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"vocab-diligent","explain":"被校长表扬、成绩优秀, 只有 diligent(勤奋的)是正面词, 和句意匹配。最迷惑的 careless(粗心的)是负面词, 粗心的学生不会考出 excellent results, 逻辑不通。考点: PSLE爱考形容词褒贬要和句子结果一致, 先判断句子是夸还是批。"},{"sentence":"Despite the ___ weather, the hikers pressed on.","opts":["warm","pleasant","harsh","mild"],"ans":2,"diff":3,"tag":"vocab-harsh","explain":"Despite 表示「尽管」, 后面的天气必须是坏的, 徒步者才需要「咬牙前进」(pressed on), 所以选 harsh(恶劣的)。最迷惑的 pleasant 是好天气, 好天气不需要 despite 来转折。考点: PSLE爱考 despite/although 转折词决定空格选反方向的词。"},{"sentence":"The old man walked with a ___ pace due to his injured leg.","opts":["swift","brisk","sluggish","rapid"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-sluggish","explain":"腿受伤了, 走路自然慢, sluggish 意思是缓慢无力的, 和 injured leg 因果吻合。最迷惑的 brisk 是轻快的, 恰恰相反, 伤腿的人快不起来。考点: PSLE爱考 due to 因果线索, 空格要和原因逻辑一致, brisk/swift/rapid 全是快, 排除。"},{"sentence":"She spoke in a ___ voice so as not to wake the baby.","opts":["hushed","shrill","harsh","loud"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-hushed","explain":"为了不吵醒宝宝, 说话要压低声音, hushed 意思是轻声的, 正好呼应 so as not to wake。最迷惑的 shrill 是尖锐刺耳的, 一喊宝宝立刻醒, 和目的完全相反。考点: PSLE爱考 so as to/in order to 目的句, 空格必须服务这个目的。"},{"sentence":"The ___ sunset painted the sky in shades of orange and pink.","opts":["ordinary","dull","plain","magnificent"],"ans":3,"diff":3,"tag":"vocab-magnificent","explain":"magnificent对: 橙粉相间的晚霞是壮丽美景, 要选褒义形容词「壮丽的」。最迷惑的dull错: dull是「暗淡无趣」, 和后面painted the sky in shades of orange and pink的绚烂画面矛盾。考点: PSLE爱考形容词感情色彩要和句子画面一致, 先看后半句描写再选词。"},{"sentence":"His sigh of relief was ___ even from the back row of the hall when the results were announced.","opts":["invisible","silent","inaudible","audible"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-audible","explain":"even from the back row 说明后排都听得到, 所以是 audible(听得见的)。inaudible/silent 和'后排都听到'矛盾, invisible 是看不见, 和声音无关。考点: 用 even from... 这种程度线索反推形容词。"},{"sentence":"The crowd erupted in ___ applause after the performance.","opts":["thunderous","polite","soft","scattered"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-thunderous","explain":"thunderous对: 表演精彩后全场erupted(爆发), 掌声要像打雷一样响, thunderous applause是固定搭配。最迷惑的polite错: polite applause是礼貌性稀拉掌声, 跟erupted的热烈气氛不搭。考点: PSLE爱考collocation固定搭配, thunderous applause=雷鸣般的掌声要整组背。"},{"sentence":"She received a ___ welcome from her relatives.","opts":["warm","lukewarm","cold","cool"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"vocab-warm welcome","explain":"warm对: 亲戚见面当然热情, warm welcome=热情欢迎, 是最常见搭配。最迷惑的lukewarm错: lukewarm是「不冷不热、冷淡」, 用在welcome上表示不情愿, 和relatives的亲情语境不符。考点: PSLE爱考warm welcome这类高频搭配, warm在这里指态度热情不是温度。"},{"sentence":"The detective examined the crime scene ___ for clues.","opts":["carelessly","casually","hastily","meticulously"],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-meticulously","explain":"meticulously对: 侦探找线索必须一丝不苟, meticulously=极其仔细地, 和examined for clues逻辑一致。最迷惑的hastily错: hastily是匆忙地, 匆忙检查会漏掉clues, 和侦探身份矛盾。考点: PSLE爱考副词修饰动词要合职业逻辑, 看到detective+clues就选careful类词。"},{"sentence":"His ___ behaviour in class earned him a detention.","opts":["polite","disruptive","respectful","exemplary"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-disruptive","explain":"disruptive对: 被罚detention说明他捣乱, disruptive=扰乱课堂的, 因果才通。最迷惑的exemplary错: exemplary是「模范的」, 模范行为只会被表扬不会被留堂。考点: PSLE爱考因果逻辑推断, 先看结果earned him a detention再倒推空格是贬义词。"},{"sentence":"The ___ child refused to share his toys with anyone.","opts":["selfish","kind","thoughtful","generous"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"vocab-selfish","explain":"selfish对: 不肯和任何人分享玩具就是自私, selfish和refused to share直接对应。最迷惑的generous错: generous是慷慨大方, 大方的孩子恰恰乐意分享, 意思正好相反。考点: PSLE爱考人物性格词与行为描写配对, 空格后的行为就是答案的定义。"},{"sentence":"She was ___ to hear that she had won the scholarship.","opts":["elated","indifferent","dismayed","annoyed"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-elated","explain":"elated对: 赢得奖学金是大喜事, elated=欣喜若狂, 情绪与好消息匹配。最迷惑的dismayed错: dismayed是「惊愕沮丧」, 用于坏消息, 和won the scholarship的喜讯矛盾。考点: PSLE爱考情绪词正负判断, 先定事件好坏再选emotion word, elated是高频褒义词。"},{"sentence":"The explorers faced ___ challenges in the jungle.","opts":["formidable","easy","minor","trivial"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-formidable","explain":"formidable对: 丛林探险艰险重重, formidable=令人生畏的、艰巨的, 和explorers闯jungle的语境相符。最迷惑的minor错: minor是「轻微的」, 丛林里的挑战不会是小事, 削弱了句子想强调的困难。考点: PSLE爱考formidable challenges这类高级搭配, 认得它能和difficult互换。"},{"sentence":"He made a ___ effort to finish the race despite his injury.","opts":["feeble","valiant","half-hearted","lazy"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-valiant","explain":"valiant对: 带伤仍坚持完赛是英勇之举, valiant effort=顽强的努力, 和despite his injury呼应。最迷惑的feeble错: feeble是「无力的」, 无力的努力撑不到终点, 和finish the race矛盾。考点: PSLE爱考despite这类让步信号词, 前后要形成反差, 伤病+完赛=勇敢。"},{"sentence":"The teacher's ___ explanation helped us understand the concept.","opts":["unclear","vague","lucid","confusing"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-lucid","explain":"lucid对: 能让大家听懂的讲解必然清晰, lucid=清楚易懂的, 和helped us understand因果相扣。最迷惑的vague错: vague是「含糊的」, 含糊的解释只会让人更糊涂, 与结果矛盾。考点: PSLE爱考结果句倒推词义, helped us understand锁定褒义, lucid=clear要记牢。"},{"sentence":"She cast a ___ look at the broken vase.","opts":["satisfied","guilty","happy","proud"],"ans":1,"diff":3,"tag":"vocab-guilty","explain":"guilty对: 花瓶打碎了, 她心虚地看一眼, guilty look=心虚愧疚的眼神, 合情合理。最迷惑的proud错: proud是骄傲, 没人会为打碎花瓶自豪, 情绪和broken vase的事故不符。考点: PSLE爱考cast a look+情绪形容词, 看物件状态(broken)判断人物心情。"},{"sentence":"The ___ silence in the hall was broken by a sudden sneeze.","opts":["noisy","moderate","deafening","loud"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-deafening silence","explain":"deafening对: deafening silence是固定表达「震耳欲聋的寂静」, 故意用矛盾修辞形容极度安静, 才会被一个喷嚏打破。最迷惑的loud错: silence本身没声音, loud silence不是英文惯用搭配, 是中式直译陷阱。考点: PSLE爱考deafening silence这类idiom式搭配, 整组背不拆开理解。"},{"sentence":"He accepted the criticism with ___ and promised to improve.","opts":["anger","grace","resentment","hostility"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-with grace","explain":"grace对: 后半句promised to improve说明他虚心接受, with grace=大度地、有风度地, 前后一致。最迷惑的resentment错: resentment是怨恨, 心怀怨恨的人不会承诺改进, 和and后的内容矛盾。考点: PSLE爱考and连接的前后情绪要同向, accept criticism with grace是加分表达。"},{"sentence":"The news of his promotion spread like ___.","opts":["wind","water","wildfire","ice"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-spread like wildfire","explain":"wildfire对: spread like wildfire是固定idiom「像野火般迅速传开」, 专形容消息传得快。最迷惑的wind错: 风虽然快, 但英文习惯用wildfire不用wind, 这是搭配不是自由造句。最迷惑处就在wind看似合理。考点: PSLE爱考idiom原样搭配, news spread like wildfire整句背下。"},{"sentence":"She was ___ by her friend's sudden outburst.","opts":["taken aback","pleased","amused","delighted"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-taken aback","explain":"taken aback对: 朋友突然发飙(sudden outburst)让人吃惊, be taken aback=大吃一惊, 情境吻合。最迷惑的amused错: amused是觉得好笑, 别人对你发火不好笑, 情绪方向错了。考点: PSLE爱考phrasal verb情绪短语, taken aback=surprised, 看到sudden就找吃惊类词。"},{"sentence":"She is fond ___ singing.","opts":["at","in","to","of"],"ans":3,"diff":3,"tag":"prep-fond of","explain":"of对: be fond of是固定搭配「喜爱」, fond后面只能接of, 再接V-ing。最迷惑的in错: interested才配in, fond不配in, 这是两组搭配混淆的经典陷阱。考点: PSLE爱考adjective+preposition固定搭配, fond of/interested in要分开记死。"},{"sentence":"He is capable ___ solving difficult problems.","opts":["of","in","to","at"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"prep-capable of","explain":"of对: be capable of doing是固定搭配「有能力做某事」, capable只跟of。最迷惑的at错: good at里才用at, capable at是错误混搭, 考的就是你别串组。考点: PSLE爱考capable of vs good at, 两个都表「擅长/能做」但介词不同, 成对记。"},{"sentence":"She apologized ___ her rude behaviour.","opts":["of","about","to","for"],"ans":3,"diff":3,"tag":"prep-apologize for","explain":"for对: apologize for sth是固定搭配「为某事道歉」, 道歉的原因用for引出。最迷惑的to错: to接的是道歉对象(apologize to him), 这里接的是行为behaviour, 该用for。考点: PSLE爱考apologize to sb for sth双介词结构, 对人用to对事用for。"},{"sentence":"I am looking forward ___ meeting you.","opts":["for","in","to","at"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"prep-look forward to","explain":"to对: look forward to是固定短语「期待」, 这个to是preposition, 所以后面接meeting不是meet。最迷惑的for错: 很多人想「期待for某事」, 但英文里forward只搭to, for是中式思维陷阱。考点: PSLE爱考look forward to+V-ing, to后接动名词是必考陷阱。"},{"sentence":"He insisted ___ paying for dinner.","opts":["in","at","on","for"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"prep-insist on","explain":"on对: insist on doing是固定搭配「坚持要做」, insist后只能接on。最迷惑的in错: persist in才用in, insist用on, 两个「坚持」介词不同最易混。考点: PSLE爱考insist on vs persist in, 意思相近介词不同的verb+preposition要成对背。"},{"sentence":"She blamed him ___ the accident.","opts":["for","on","at","to"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"prep-blame for","explain":"for对: blame sb for sth是固定搭配「因某事责怪某人」, 原因用for。最迷惑的on错: blame sth on sb(把事怪到人头上)也存在, 但那是blame+事+on+人; 这里blame后先接him, 只能用for接原因。考点: PSLE爱考blame的两种句型, blame sb for sth / blame sth on sb别搞反。"},{"sentence":"The teacher was pleased ___ our performance.","opts":["with","of","to","for"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"prep-pleased with","explain":"with对: be pleased with是固定搭配「对…满意」, 对某人表现满意用with。最迷惑的at错: pleased at偶见于对某消息高兴, 但对performance这类成果, 标准搭配是with, 考试按pleased with判。考点: PSLE爱考satisfied/pleased with, 表「对成果满意」一律with。"},{"sentence":"He suffers ___ a rare disease.","opts":["in","from","by","of"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"prep-suffer from","explain":"from对: suffer from是固定搭配「患病、受…折磨」, 接疾病只能用from。最迷惑的of错: 中文「死于/患于」让人想选of, 但英文die of存在, suffer却只搭from, 别类推。考点: PSLE爱考suffer from+疾病, 看到disease/illness直接锁from。"},{"sentence":"She is allergic ___ peanuts.","opts":["from","to","with","of"],"ans":1,"diff":3,"tag":"prep-allergic to","explain":"to对: be allergic to是固定搭配「对…过敏」, allergic后面只能接to。最迷惑的from错: 中文说「对花生过敏」像「来自花生的反应」, 有人误选from, 但英文固定用to。考点: PSLE爱考allergic to/similar to这类adj+to搭配, 过敏一律to。"},{"sentence":"I am grateful ___ you ___ your help.","opts":["for/to","to/for","with/for","at/of"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"prep-grateful to...for","explain":"grateful的固定搭配是 grateful to 人 for 事: 感谢的对象用to, 感谢的原因用for, 连起来就是 grateful to you for your help, 所以填「to/for」。最迷惑的是「for/to」, 它把两个介词调了个个儿, 变成『因为你而感谢帮助』, 逻辑不通。考点: PSLE爱考『人用to、事用for』的双介词搭配, 类似的还有 thank you for。"},{"sentence":"He is accustomed ___ waking up early.","opts":["with","to","at","of"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"prep-accustomed to","explain":"be accustomed to 是固定搭配, 意思是\"习惯于\", 这个to是preposition, 后面接waking这种-ing形式。最迷惑的是of, 因为很多形容词配of(如fond of), 但accustomed只认to。考点: PSLE爱考 accustomed to / used to + V-ing, 别把to当infinitive写成wake。"},{"sentence":"She succeeded ___ passing the exam.","opts":["at","in","of","on"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"prep-succeed in","explain":"succeed in doing sth 是固定搭配, \"成功做成某事\"只能用in。最迷惑的是at, 因为 good at 太熟了, 孩子容易照搬, 但succeed不跟at配。考点: PSLE爱考动词固定介词, succeed in 和 good at 要分开记, 不能混用。"},{"sentence":"The book consists ___ ten chapters.","opts":["in","from","of","with"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"prep-consist of","explain":"consist of 是固定搭配, 意思是\"由...组成\", 书由十章组成只能用of。最迷惑的是from, 因为中文\"由...而来\"让人想到from, 但consist from是错的。考点: PSLE爱考组成类短语, consist of = be made up of, 且consist不用被动。"},{"sentence":"He congratulated her ___ her achievement.","opts":["on","at","with","to"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"prep-congratulate on","explain":"congratulate sb on sth 是固定搭配。at/to/with 都不能接在 congratulated her 后面引出所祝贺的事。考点: congratulate on / praise for / thank for 分开记。"},{"sentence":"She is addicted ___ her phone.","opts":["of","to","with","on"],"ans":1,"diff":3,"tag":"prep-addicted to","explain":"be addicted to 是固定搭配, \"沉迷于\"只能用to, 这个to是preposition。最迷惑的是on, 因为中文说\"沉迷在手机上\", 直译会选on, 但英语不这么搭。考点: PSLE爱考带to的形容词短语, addicted to / devoted to / used to 是一家人。"},{"sentence":"They objected ___ the new proposal.","opts":["at","for","on","to"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"prep-object to","explain":"object to 是固定搭配, \"反对\"某事必须加to, object是不及物动词, 不能直接接宾语。最迷惑的是on, 因为\"在提案上有意见\"的中文思路会带偏, 但英语只认object to。考点: PSLE爱考object to / agree to, to后接名词或V-ing。"},{"sentence":"He divided the cake ___ six pieces.","opts":["into","for","in","to"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"prep-divide into","explain":"divide...into 是固定搭配, 把整体切成几份用into, 强调\"变成\"新的状态。最迷惑的是in, 看着只差两个字母, 但in表示位置不表示变化, divide in six pieces是错的。考点: PSLE爱考divide into / cut into / turn into, \"变成\"类都用into。"},{"sentence":"She prevented him ___ making a mistake.","opts":["for","to","of","from"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"prep-prevent from","explain":"prevent sb from doing sth 是固定搭配, \"阻止某人做某事\"只能用from, 表示\"使远离\"。最迷惑的是to, 孩子容易按\"阻止他去做\"翻译成to make, 方向正好反了。考点: PSLE爱考prevent/stop/discourage sb from + V-ing, 阻拦类动词全家用from。"},{"sentence":"I am tired ___ doing the same thing every day.","opts":["about","from","of","with"],"ans":2,"diff":3,"tag":"prep-tired of","explain":"be tired of 表示\"厌倦、烦了\", 每天做同样的事让人厌倦, 用of。最迷惑的是from, 因为 tired from 也存在, 但那是\"因劳累而疲惫\"(如tired from running), 这里是心理上的烦。考点: PSLE爱考tired of(厌倦) vs tired from(累), 看语境选介词。"},{"sentence":"He reminds me ___ my grandfather.","opts":["to","about","with","of"],"ans":3,"diff":3,"tag":"prep-remind of","explain":"remind sb of sb/sth 是固定搭配, \"让我想起\"某人用of。最迷惑的是about, 因为 remind me about the meeting(提醒某事)也对, 但\"像谁、让人想起谁\"只能用of。考点: PSLE爱考remind of(想起) vs remind about(提醒做事), 两个意思两个介词。"},{"sentence":"The teacher ___ to mark the essay because it was handed in late.","opts":["rejected","refused","disapproved","denied"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-synonym","explain":"refuse to do 是'拒绝做某事'的标准结构。reject/deny/disapprove 后面都不能直接接 to + 动词原形(reject 接名词, deny 接名词或 V-ing, disapprove 接 of)。考点: 拒绝家族里只有 refuse 和 decline 能接 to do, 本题考的是语法接法。"},{"sentence":"Doctors warned that the patient's body might ___ the transplanted kidney.","opts":["refuse","deny","decline","reject"],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-synonym","explain":"身体对移植器官的'排斥'只能用 reject, 这是医学固定用语。refuse 是人主动不做, deny 是否认, decline 是婉拒邀请, 都不能用于器官。考点: reject 的宾语是'被排斥的东西', 不限于提案和申请。"},{"sentence":"Sarah ___ the kind offer, saying she already had plans.","opts":["declined","denied","disagreed","disapproved"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-synonym","explain":"decline an offer 是'婉拒邀请/提议'的标准搭配。deny 是否认事实, disagree 是不及物动词要接 with, disapprove 要接 of, 三个都不能直接带 the kind offer 这个宾语。考点: 拒绝家族看宾语和接法。"},{"sentence":"The suspect ___ all knowledge of the incident.","opts":["rejected","denied","refused","declined"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-synonym","explain":"denied = 否认某事真实; 其他都是拒绝做/接受"},{"sentence":"The little girl gazed ___ at the puppy in the window.","opts":["barely","sharply","longingly","quickly"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-synonym","explain":"longingly = 渴望地 (看到喜欢的东西); quickly 速度; barely 几乎不; sharply 锋利"},{"sentence":"The students ___ when the bell signalled the end of the test.","opts":["sulked","frowned","rejoiced","wept"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-synonym","explain":"考试结束是解脱, rejoiced = 欢欣鼓舞。wept 哭、frowned 皱眉、sulked 生闷气全是负面反应, 和'考完了'的轻松不符。考点: 先判断事件好坏再选情绪动词。"},{"sentence":"Despite the heavy rain, the marathon runners ___ on towards the finish line.","opts":["persevered","retreated","hesitated","wavered"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-synonym","explain":"persevered = 坚持不懈 (常配 on); wavered 动摇; hesitated 犹豫; retreated 撤退"},{"sentence":"My grandmother always speaks ___ about her childhood in the kampong.","opts":["rudely","fondly","briefly","silently"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-synonym","explain":"fondly = 深情地 (回忆童年正面情感); rudely 粗鲁; briefly 简短; silently 不说话 (矛盾)"},{"sentence":"The dog wagged its tail ___ when its owner came home.","opts":["sluggishly","reluctantly","enthusiastically","clumsily"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-synonym","explain":"enthusiastically = 兴奋地 (狗见主人); 其他都是负面/慢"},{"sentence":"The chef ___ tasted the soup before serving it to the customers.","opts":["rudely","noisily","recklessly","cautiously"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-synonym","explain":"cautiously = 小心地 (尝汤要谨慎); recklessly 鲁莽; 其他不合适"},{"sentence":"You must ___ a decision quickly before the deadline.","opts":["take","have","do","make"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-collocation","explain":"make a decision 是固定搭配, 不能用 do/take/have. 同类: make a choice/promise/mistake"},{"sentence":"She made a great ___ to complete the project on time.","opts":["effort","effect","affect","afford"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-collocation","explain":"make an effort 是固定搭配'努力'。effect 是效果, affect 是动词影响, afford 是负担得起, 都不能放在 made a great 后面。考点: effort/effect/affect 形近词靠搭配锁定。"},{"sentence":"The team ___ home the trophy from the inter-school competition.","opts":["took","did","made","won"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-collocation","explain":"take home the trophy = 把奖杯带回家(赢得奖杯)。won 不能接 home(won the trophy 可以, won home 不成立); made/did 都不搭。考点: 看空格后面的 home 这个词, 它决定了动词只能是 took/brought。"},{"sentence":"You should ___ your homework before watching TV.","opts":["do","have","take","make"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"vocab-collocation","explain":"do homework 是固定 (与 make 不同); make 用于\"创造\"含义 (make a cake)"},{"sentence":"Please ___ a deep breath and try to calm down.","opts":["take","do","have","make"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-collocation","explain":"take a breath = 呼吸 (固定); take a look, take a seat 同类"},{"sentence":"The students ___ their best to finish the project on time.","opts":["did","took","made","gave"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-collocation","explain":"do one's best = 尽全力, 固定搭配。make/take/give 都不能和 one's best 组成这个意思(give one's best 是'致以问候', 和尽力无关)。考点: do/make 搭配, do one's best 和 try one's best 都对, 但本题选项里只有 do 成立。"},{"sentence":"I always ___ the bus to school every morning.","opts":["take","do","drive","make"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-collocation","explain":"take the bus/train/MRT = 坐 (固定); ride a bike 才对; ride the bus 较少用"},{"sentence":"Please ___ attention to the safety instructions before boarding.","opts":["give","take","pay","make"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-collocation","explain":"pay attention = 注意 (固定); pay a visit/compliment 同类"},{"sentence":"The new policy will ___ effect from next Monday.","opts":["do","have","take","make"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-collocation","explain":"take effect = 生效 (固定 - 法律/政策用语); 其他不能搭 effect"},{"sentence":"My father ___ a successful business for over 20 years.","opts":["has played","has made","has done","has run"],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-collocation","explain":"run a business = 经营生意, 固定搭配。do business 后面不能接 a successful business, make/play 都不搭。考点: run 作'经营'讲, run a business/shop/company 整组记。"},{"sentence":"___ the heavy rain, we managed to finish the football match.","opts":["Despite","Although","Because of","In addition to"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-connector","explain":"Despite + 名词/动名词 (heavy rain 是名词); Although 后跟句子 (Although it rained heavily); Because of 表示因为"},{"sentence":"___ it was raining heavily, we managed to finish the match.","opts":["In spite","Despite","Because of","Although"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-connector","explain":"Although + 完整句子; Despite 后只能跟名词/动名词. In spite 必须有 of (In spite of)"},{"sentence":"The class was cancelled ___ the teacher's sudden illness.","opts":["therefore","due to","despite","although"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-connector","explain":"due to + 名词原因 (illness 是名词); despite 表让步; although 跟句子; therefore 表结果"},{"sentence":"She studied very hard; ___, she did well in the exam.","opts":["despite","although","meanwhile","therefore"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-connector","explain":"therefore = 因此 (前因后果); 用分号后表结论. despite 让步; meanwhile 同时"},{"sentence":"___ I was tired, I had to finish my homework before sleeping.","opts":["Despite","Because","Although","When"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-connector","explain":"Although + 完整句 (表让步); Despite 不能后跟句子; Because 表原因 (但这里逻辑是让步)"},{"sentence":"You can either take the bus ___ walk to school.","opts":["or","and","nor","but"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"vocab-connector","explain":"either...or 是配对 (固定); either...and/but/nor 都错"},{"sentence":"Neither John ___ his brother enjoys reading novels.","opts":["or","but","and","nor"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-connector","explain":"neither...nor 是配对 (固定); 跟 or 是错配; 主谓一致看 nor 后名词 (brother 单数 → enjoys)"},{"sentence":"Not only ___ but he also helps with chores at home.","opts":["he does study hard","does he study hard","he hardly studies","he studies hard"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-connector","explain":"Not only 开头需要倒装 (does he study) 不是 he studies; \"Not only does X, but X also\" 是固定结构"},{"sentence":"The coach was determined to win the championship this year. ___, the team practised every day after school.","opts":["Although","As a result","In addition","However"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-connector","explain":"前句教练决心夺冠, 后句天天训练, 是前因后果, 用 As a result。However 是转折(决心夺冠和苦练不矛盾), Although 后面要接从句不能带逗号独立用, In addition 是递进但前句不是同类并列的事实。考点: 结果词前面必须找得到原因。"},{"sentence":"I want to be a doctor; ___, my sister wants to be an engineer.","opts":["therefore","however","because","despite"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-connector","explain":"however = 然而 (对比, 我想 vs 她想); therefore 因此; 用分号 + however + 逗号"},{"sentence":"The fire ___ at midnight, destroying the entire warehouse.","opts":["broke down","broke in","broke out","broke up"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-phrasal","explain":"break out = 突然爆发 (fire/war/disease 必搭); break up 分手; break down 故障; break in 闯入"},{"sentence":"My car ___ on the way home, and I had to take a taxi.","opts":["broke up","broke out","broke in","broke down"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-phrasal","explain":"break down = 故障 (机器/车); 其他都不合"},{"sentence":"Please ___ the children while I go to the supermarket.","opts":["look after","look for","look at","look up"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-phrasal","explain":"look after = 照顾 (take care of); look for 寻找; look up 查找 (信息); look at 看"},{"sentence":"I can't find my keys. Help me ___ them.","opts":["look at","look up","look for","look after"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-phrasal","explain":"look for = 寻找 (东西不见了); 区别: look after 照顾人; look up 查找资料"},{"sentence":"Don't ___, you can finish this puzzle if you try harder.","opts":["give away","give off","give out","give up"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-phrasal","explain":"give up = 放弃, 鼓励别人坚持就是 don't give up。give off 是散发(气味), give out 是分发/耗尽, give away 是送掉/泄露, 都不合。考点: give 家族短语动词。"},{"sentence":"The teacher will ___ the worksheets at the start of class.","opts":["hand down","hand in","hand out","hand over"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-phrasal","explain":"hand out = 发放; hand in 上交 (homework); hand over 移交权力; hand down 传给下一代"},{"sentence":"Please ___ your homework by Friday.","opts":["hand out","hand down","hand off","hand in"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-phrasal","explain":"hand in = 上交 (作业/试卷); 反义 hand out 发放"},{"sentence":"The plane ___ at 8 am sharp.","opts":["took off","took over","took out","took up"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-phrasal","explain":"take off = 起飞 (飞机); take up 培养爱好; take out 取出; take over 接管"},{"sentence":"I have ___ a new hobby — learning the violin.","opts":["taken over","taken out","taken off","taken up"],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-phrasal","explain":"take up = 开始 (爱好/工作); take off 起飞; take over 接管"},{"sentence":"The meeting was ___ to next week due to the typhoon.","opts":["put down","put up","put off","put out"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-phrasal","explain":"put off = 推迟 (postpone); put up 张贴/容忍; put out 熄灭; put down 放下"},{"sentence":"Singapore is famous ___ its hawker food.","opts":["with","of","about","for"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-prep","explain":"famous for = 因…而出名 (固定); famous with 错; famous of 错"},{"sentence":"I am proud ___ my younger sister for winning the prize.","opts":["of","about","with","for"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-prep","explain":"proud of = 因…而骄傲 (固定); proud with/for 错"},{"sentence":"She is interested ___ studying Mandarin.","opts":["in","at","about","on"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-prep","explain":"interested in + 动名词 (固定); interested at/on/about 错"},{"sentence":"My brother is good ___ playing chess.","opts":["in","at","on","for"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-prep","explain":"good at = 擅长 (skill); good in/on/for 错. 区别: good for health 是另一个意思 (有益于)"},{"sentence":"The book is similar ___ the one I borrowed last week.","opts":["from","with","as","to"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-prep","explain":"similar to = 类似于 (固定); different from; same as. 不要混"},{"sentence":"The teacher accused him ___ cheating during the exam.","opts":["with","about","of","for"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-prep","explain":"accuse sb of sth/doing = 指控 (固定); accuse for 错"},{"sentence":"My grandmother suffers ___ arthritis.","opts":["at","with","of","from"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-prep","explain":"suffer from = 患…病 (固定); suffer of/with 错"},{"sentence":"The success depends ___ how much effort you put in.","opts":["on","with","to","of"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-prep","explain":"depend on = 依赖于 (固定); depend of/with 错"},{"sentence":"The cake consists ___ flour, eggs and sugar.","opts":["from","of","with","in"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-prep","explain":"consist of = 由…组成 (固定, 不用被动); 区别: be composed of; be made of/from"},{"sentence":"I apologise ___ being late to class.","opts":["about","of","to","for"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-prep","explain":"apologise for + ing (固定); apologise to + 人; 别混 — apologise to him for being late"},{"sentence":"I have two pens. One is blue and the ___ is red.","opts":["another","any other","others","other"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-another-other","explain":"the other = 两个中的另一个 (确指); another = 还有一个 (再加, 不确指). 真考 17 题孩子写 another 错"},{"sentence":"There are three apples on the table. One is mine, and the ___ two belong to my sister.","opts":["others","another","other","any"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-another-other","explain":"the other + 复数 = 其余的 (剩下都是); another 后只能跟单数; others 是代词不接名词"},{"sentence":"Would you like ___ cup of tea?","opts":["the other","another","other","others"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-another-other","explain":"another + 单数 = 再一个 (不确指); other 后必须有名词复数 或 the other; 这里是 polite offer 用 another"},{"sentence":"___ I see a stray dog, I feel sorry for it.","opts":["Whenever","Although","Until","Unless"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-when-whenever","explain":"每次看到流浪狗都难过, 用 Whenever(每当)。Unless(除非)、Until(直到)逻辑不通, Although(尽管)前后没有转折。考点: whenever 表'每一次', 本题靠排除另外三个逻辑词锁定。"},{"sentence":"___ the bell rings, students rush out of the classroom.","opts":["Until","Where","Whenever","Unless"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-when-whenever","explain":"铃一响就冲出去是每次都发生的规律, 用 Whenever。Where 是地点, Until 是'直到…才', Unless 是'除非', 三个逻辑都不通。考点: whenever = every time that。"},{"sentence":"___ we visit grandma, she always cooks our favourite food.","opts":["Whereas","Whenever","Wherever","Unless"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-when-whenever","explain":"每次去看外婆她都做饭, 用 Whenever 配 always。Whereas 是对比'然而', Wherever 是'无论哪里', Unless 是'除非', 都不合。考点: whenever + always 表习惯。"},{"sentence":"I ___ the children playing in the park for an hour.","opts":["looked","noticed","saw","watched"],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-saw-watched","explain":"watch = 持续观看 (for an hour 持续动作); saw = 一瞬间看到; look at = 朝某方向看. 真考 20 题孩子写 saw 错"},{"sentence":"As I ___ the ripples form on the water, I felt peaceful.","opts":["watched","viewed","looked","glanced"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-saw-watched","explain":"watch = 持续注视一个过程(涟漪慢慢形成)。looked/glanced 都要接 at 才能带宾语, viewed 是'观看/查看(文件、风景)', 不和'涟漪形成'这个动态过程搭配。考点: 看 watch/see/look 的接法和持续性。"},{"sentence":"Dad ___ TV every evening after dinner.","opts":["notices","watches","looks","sees"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-saw-watched","explain":"watch TV 是固定搭配 (持续观看节目); see TV 错"},{"sentence":"The current was ___ strong that I struggled to swim back.","opts":["very","quite","too","so"],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-so-too","explain":"so + adj + that = 如此...以致 (结构固定); too + adj + to + 动 (不能跟 that); 真考 23 题孩子写 too 错"},{"sentence":"The film was ___ boring that we all fell asleep.","opts":["very","so","too","really"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-so-too","explain":"so...that = 结果状语从句; too...that 不存在; too...to 才对"},{"sentence":"The bag is ___ heavy for me to carry.","opts":["enough","so","very","too"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-so-too","explain":"too + adj + (for sb) + to + 动 = 太...而不能 (结构); so 后跟 that 从句"},{"sentence":"I always tell ___ to stay calm during exams.","opts":["myself","my","me","mine"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-reflexive","explain":"主语 I 和宾语是同一个人, 必须用反身代词 myself。me 不能在主语是 I 时作宾语指自己, mine 是物主代词, my 后面要接名词。考点: 主宾同人用 -self。"},{"sentence":"She made the cake all by ___.","opts":["she","her","herself","hers"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-reflexive","explain":"by + 反身代词 = 独自. by herself = 她自己 (没人帮); by her 是 \"由她\" 不同意"},{"sentence":"The children got ___ dressed before going to school.","opts":["their","them","they","themselves"],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-reflexive","explain":"主语 children = 复数, 反身 themselves; dress oneself = 给自己穿衣 (动作返回主语)"},{"sentence":"I was so angry that I could not stop ___ from yelling.","opts":["I","me","myself","mine"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-reflexive","explain":"stop + oneself + from = 阻止自己 (反身); 主语 I, 宾语 myself"},{"sentence":"The lifeguard pulled the drowning child to ___.","opts":["ground","land","dry","safety"],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-collocation-safety","explain":"pull/bring/get sb to safety = 救出脱险 (固定搭配, \"safety\" 抽象名词); pull to ground 不对; 真考 30 题孩子写 ground 错"},{"sentence":"Despite the heavy traffic, we arrived ___ on time.","opts":["too","just","very","quite"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-collocation","explain":"just on time = 刚好准时 (固定); very on time 不自然"},{"sentence":"The river was ___ across the village, bringing fresh water.","opts":["flows","flow","flowing","flowed"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-word-form","explain":"was + V-ing = 过去进行 (河流持续流动). 真考 16 题孩子写 Across 错 (Across 是 prep 不是动词形式, 应该用 ing) "},{"sentence":"The dog was ___ in the river before its owner rescued it.","opts":["drowned","drowning","drowns","drown"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-word-form","explain":"was + V-ing 表示过去正在进行(正在溺水), 所以用 drowning。drowned 是过去式/过去分词, 和 was 连用会变成被动; drown/drowns 不能跟在 was 后面。考点: 过去进行时 was/were + V-ing。"},{"sentence":"The witness gave a ___ account of the accident, mentioning the colour of the car, the time and even the driver's jacket.","opts":["lengthy","detailed","confusing","truthful"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"context-vocab-evidence","explain":"空格后面列举了车的颜色、时间、连夹克都记得 — 这就是'细节丰富'的证据, 所以选 detailed。lengthy 只说篇幅长不说细; truthful 讲的是真假, 句中没有真假线索; confusing 与举例的清晰程度矛盾。考点: PSLE 完形的正确答案一定能在空格前后找到具体证据, 不能凭第一感觉选。"},{"sentence":"The new library was equipped with thousands of books and a quiet reading room; ___, hardly any pupils went there after the first week.","opts":["fortunately","similarly","surprisingly","accordingly"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"context-connector-contrast","explain":"前半句说条件很好, 后半句说几乎没人去, 这是出乎意料的反差, 用 surprisingly。fortunately 语气正面与'没人去'矛盾; similarly 表示相似不是反差; accordingly 表因果, 但条件好不会导致没人去。考点: PSLE 完形的连接词题先判断前后两句是顺还是逆, 再挑具体的词。"},{"sentence":"Every player trained hard for the finals; ___, an unexpected injury to the captain cost the team the trophy.","opts":["meanwhile","nevertheless","furthermore","consequently"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"context-connector-concession","explain":"前句是刻苦训练, 后句是丢掉奖杯, 属于转折, 用 nevertheless。furthermore 是递进; meanwhile 是同时发生; consequently 是因果, 但'努力训练'不会导致'队长受伤丢冠'。考点: PSLE 只考四类连接词 — 转折、递进、因果、时间, 每题先给两句话贴上关系标签再选。"},{"sentence":"The MRT breakdown lasted only twenty minutes; ___, thousands of commuters were late for work that morning.","opts":["by then","in turn","as such","even so"],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"context-connector-even so","explain":"前句说只坏了二十分钟(时间很短), 后句说几千人迟到(后果很大), 是让步转折, 用 even so(即便如此)。as such 是'就其本身而言'; in turn 是'依次/反过来'; by then 是'到那时'。考点: PSLE 完形里的短连接词组最容易被忽略, even so / all the same / at the same time 都表让步。"},{"sentence":"Sarah checked the timetable twice, packed her bag the night before and set two alarms; ___, she still managed to miss the coach.","opts":["predictably","accordingly","deliberately","remarkably"],"ans":3,"diff":6,"tag":"context-attitude-adverb","explain":"她做了三重准备却还是没赶上车, 这是令人意外的结果, 用 remarkably。predictably(不出所料)与充分准备矛盾; accordingly(因此)表因果, 准备充分不会导致误车; deliberately(故意地)句中没有任何依据。考点: PSLE 完形后段常考'作者态度副词', 必须把整句的因果读完再选。"},{"sentence":"The letter had no stamp, no return address and a name spelt three different ways; the officer therefore treated it with considerable ___.","opts":["suspicion","confidence","enthusiasm","gratitude"],"ans":0,"diff":6,"tag":"context-inference-noun","explain":"没有邮票、没有回邮地址、名字还拼了三种写法, 全是可疑的证据, 所以是 suspicion(怀疑)。confidence / enthusiasm / gratitude 都是正面情绪, 与这些疑点矛盾。考点: PSLE 完形和阅读理解共用一个技巧 — 把空格前罗列的细节当成证据链, 答案必须是这些细节共同指向的那一个。"},{"sentence":"The old man accepted the award ___, insisting that his team deserved far more credit than he did.","opts":["loudly","humbly","angrily","proudly"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"context-manner-adverb","explain":"后半句说他坚持功劳属于团队, 这是谦逊的表现, 用 humbly。proudly 与'把功劳让给别人'矛盾; angrily 和 loudly 在句中找不到任何依据。考点: PSLE 完形爱在空格后用分词短语给出人物态度的证据, 先读逗号后面那半句再回来选。"},{"sentence":"The nurse spoke to the frightened child in a ___ voice until he stopped crying.","opts":["soothing","shrill","hoarse","stern"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"context-adj-result","explain":"结果是孩子不哭了, 说明护士的声音是安抚性的, 用 soothing。shrill(尖利)、stern(严厉)、hoarse(沙哑)都不可能让受惊的孩子平静下来。考点: PSLE 完形的形容词题, 用结果分句(until he stopped crying)反推前面该填什么。"},{"sentence":"The instructions on the packet were so ___ that even the adults could not work out how to assemble the shelf.","opts":["plain","vague","simple","brief"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"context-adj-so-that","explain":"连大人都装不出来, 说明说明书含糊不清, 用 vague。brief 只是'简短', 简短未必看不懂; plain 和 simple 都是'简单明了', 与'看不懂'正好相反。考点: PSLE 完形的 so...that 结构里, that 后面的结果分句就是选词的唯一证据。"},{"sentence":"Winning the inter-school championship gave the young goalkeeper the ___ he needed to try out for the national squad.","opts":["experience","permission","confidence","reputation"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"context-abstract-noun","explain":"赢了比赛带来的是去参加国家队选拔的'信心', 用 confidence。experience 靠一场比赛谈不上; permission 选拔不需要谁批准; reputation 是名声, 不能直接促使人去试训。考点: PSLE 完形考抽象名词时先问'这件事给了他什么', 答案必须能解释后面那个动作。"},{"sentence":"The principal ___ the rumour at the assembly, stating clearly that no teacher would be leaving at the end of the year.","opts":["declined","denied","rejected","refused"],"ans":1,"diff":6,"tag":"vocab-deny-refuse-reject","explain":"deny 是'否认某件事是真的', 正好对应在朝会上澄清谣言。refuse 和 decline 是拒绝邀请或请求, reject 是驳回提案或申请, 三者的宾语都不能是一个'传闻'。考点: PSLE 反复考 deny / refuse / reject / decline 这个拒绝家族, 关键看宾语是'说法'还是'请求'。"},{"sentence":"After three rounds of talks the union finally ___ to the management's offer, ending the two-week strike.","opts":["admitted","agreed","approved","accepted"],"ans":1,"diff":6,"tag":"vocab-agree to搭配","explain":"空格后面是介词 to, 四个词里只有 agree to sth 这个搭配成立。accept 和 approve 是及物动词直接跟宾语(accepted the offer), admit 是承认。考点: PSLE 完形常把'意思相近但介词不同'的动词放在一起考, 先看空格后面有没有介词。"},{"sentence":"Despite mounting evidence, the accused man ___ his innocence right up to the final day of the trial.","opts":["maintained","remained","obtained","contained"],"ans":0,"diff":6,"tag":"vocab-maintain innocence","explain":"maintain one's innocence 是固定说法, 意思是'坚称自己无罪'。remain 是不及物动词不能带宾语; contain 是'包含'; obtain 是'获得', 都讲不通。考点: PSLE 高档完形喜欢用形近词组当干扰项(maintain / remain / contain / obtain), 靠搭配和及物性排除。"},{"sentence":"The village had relied on the river for generations, so the discovery that the factory upstream had been ___ waste into it caused an immediate uproar.","opts":["distributing","dispersing","disposing","discharging"],"ans":3,"diff":6,"tag":"vocab-discharge waste","explain":"discharge waste into a river 是'向河里排放废物'的标准说法。dispose 必须接 of(dispose of waste), 这里后面没有 of; disperse 是'驱散(人群)'; distribute 是'分发'。考点: PSLE 顶档完形用形近的高级动词做干扰, 先检查它要求的介词对不对。"},{"sentence":"The coach ___ us that the match had been postponed because the field was waterlogged.","opts":["told","said","talked","spoke"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-say-tell-speak-talk","explain":"tell 后面直接跟人再跟 that 从句(told us that); say 不能直接跟人(要写成 said to us); speak 和 talk 后面接 to sb, 也不能接 that 从句。考点: PSLE Editing 和完形都爱考 say / tell / speak / talk 的搭配, 判断方法就是看空格后面紧跟的是不是'人'。"},{"sentence":"The scientists published two reports last year; the ___ one has already been translated into six languages.","opts":["last","later","latest","latter"],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-former-latter","explain":"两者之中的'后一个'用 the latter(对应 the former)。later 是'较晚的时间'; last 是一系列里的最后一个(要三个以上); latest 是'最新的'。句中明确只有 two reports, 所以用 latter。考点: PSLE 常考 former / latter 这一对, 触发条件是前文刚好提到两样东西。"},{"sentence":"The volunteers ___ no effort to clear the beach before the coastal clean-up ended at noon.","opts":["kept","saved","spared","held"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-spare no effort","explain":"spare no effort 是固定搭配, 意思是'不遗余力'。save / keep / hold 都不能和 no effort 组成这个意思。考点: PSLE 完形的固定搭配题只能靠积累, 同一族的还有 make an effort / take pains / go to great lengths。"},{"sentence":"The two sisters had not spoken for months, but they finally ___ after their grandmother's birthday dinner.","opts":["made for","made up","made out","made off"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-phrasal-make up和好","explain":"make up 在这里是'和好', 对应前半句'几个月没说话'。make out 是'辨认出'; make off 是'逃走'; make for 是'走向/有助于'。考点: PSLE 完形常考同一动词配不同小品词, 靠前半句的人物关系锁定意思。"},{"sentence":"By the time the ambulance ___ the scene, the passers-by had already carried the injured cyclist to the pavement.","opts":["reached","had reached","reaches","has reached"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"tense-context-两个过去","explain":"主句用了 had carried(过去完成)表示更早发生, By the time 从句就用一般过去 reached 作为参照点。选 had reached 会让两件事都变成'更早', 逻辑就乱了。考点: PSLE 完形考'过去的过去' — 先发生的用 had done, 后发生的用一般过去, 两个不能同时用过去完成。"},{"sentence":"The museum ___ its collection for over a century before the fire of 1974 destroyed almost every exhibit.","opts":["has been building","had been building","was building","is building"],"ans":1,"diff":6,"tag":"tense-context-过去完成进行","explain":"for over a century 是持续到 1974 年大火这个过去时间点为止, 用过去完成进行 had been building。has been building 会一直持续到现在, 但藏品已经烧毁了; was building 表达不出'持续了一百多年'。考点: PSLE 顶档时态题, 看到 for + 时间段 + before + 过去事件, 就用 had been doing。"},{"sentence":"Not until the last guest had gone home ___ how exhausted she really was.","opts":["she did realise","did she realise","she realised","realised she"],"ans":1,"diff":6,"tag":"context-倒装-not until","explain":"Not until 放在句首时主句要部分倒装, 写成 did + 主语 + 动词原形。其余三个要么没倒装要么语序错。考点: PSLE 顶档考的句首否定倒装 — Not until / Never / Seldom / Little 开头, 主句必须倒装, 从句照常。"},{"sentence":"The sudden ___ of the star player was a heavy blow to a team that had just reached the semi-finals.","opts":["withdrawing","withdraw","withdrawal","withdrawn"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"词形-名词withdrawal","explain":"空格前是 The sudden(冠词加形容词), 需要一个名词, withdrawal(退出)才是名词形式。withdraw 是动词原形; withdrawn 是过去分词; withdrawing 是动名词, 不能被 The sudden 这样修饰。考点: PSLE Editing 每篇有两三个词形题, 定位方法是先判断空格该是名词、动词、形容词还是副词。"},{"sentence":"The referee awarded the goal ___ the loud protests of the visiting supporters.","opts":["instead of","in spite of","because of","on top of"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"context-prep-让步","explain":"抗议声很大但进球仍然算数, 属于让步关系, 用 in spite of(尽管)。because of 表原因(抗议不会导致进球有效); instead of 是'代替'; on top of 是'除…之外'。考点: PSLE 完形里 despite 和 in spite of 后面只能接名词或动名词, 绝不能接完整句子。"},{"sentence":"The hall was packed ___ parents by seven o'clock, and latecomers had to stand along the back wall.","opts":["by","in","with","of"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"context-prep-packed with","explain":"be packed with = 挤满了, 固定介词是 with(同族的还有 be filled with / be crowded with)。by 表示施动者(被谁打包); of 和 in 都不与 packed 搭配。考点: PSLE Editing 的高频错点 — 表示'充满'的动词后面统一跟 with。"},{"sentence":"In a letter to the school principal, the most appropriate way to sign off is \"___\" rather than a casual ending.","opts":["Lots of love","Yours sincerely","Cheers for now","See you around"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"situational-正式收尾","explain":"写给校长属于正式信, 收尾用 Yours sincerely(知道对方姓名)或 Yours faithfully(不知道姓名)。其余三个都是朋友之间的随意语气, 用在正式信里会被扣格式分。考点: PSLE Situational Writing 的 purpose / audience / tone 三要素, 收信人身份直接决定用词的正式程度。"},{"sentence":"Since you are writing to invite a busy guest speaker, the opening should read \"___\" instead of a blunt demand.","opts":["Come and give a talk to our class","We would be honoured if you could","You have to come and speak to us","We are telling you to come along"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"situational-邀请语气","explain":"邀请忙碌的嘉宾要用委婉的请求语气 We would be honoured if you could; 其余三句是命令或平铺直叙, 对长辈或校外嘉宾都不礼貌。考点: PSLE Situational Writing 评分先看语气是否匹配收信人身份, 邀请信必须出现请求而不是要求。"},{"sentence":"When writing a report about a lost wallet, the most suitable opening sentence is \"___\"","opts":["My wallet is gone and I am really very upset.","I am writing to report the loss of my wallet.","Somebody must have taken the wallet that I own.","I lost my wallet and want you to find it right now."],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"situational-报告开头","explain":"正式报告第一句要交代写作目的, I am writing to report... 是标准句式。其余三句分别在抒发情绪、指责别人、下命令, 都不符合报告的语域。考点: PSLE Situational Writing 第一段必须点明 purpose, 阅卷老师第一眼就找这句。"},{"sentence":"Your friend has just failed an important test. The most suitable thing to write in your message is \"___\"","opts":["Do not be too hard on yourself; there will be another chance.","That is what happens when a person does not prepare properly.","I did tell you that this test was going to be extremely hard.","You should have listened to me and studied much harder before."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"situational-安慰语气","explain":"朋友刚失利, 该写的是安慰和鼓励; 其余三句都在事后指责, 语气与场景不合。考点: PSLE Situational Writing 会给定情境和收信人, 内容点写得再全, 语气错了照样拿不到高分。"}];

// ============= v19.4: SST (Synthesis & Transformation) 题库 =============
// PSLE Paper 2 Section C: 5 题 × 2 分 = 10 分
// 格式: 给原句 + 转换要求, 选正确的转换结果 (MCQ 化 — app 内可自动判分)
const SST_QUESTIONS = [{"q":"\"I am going to the market,\" said Mum.","rule":"Rewrite in reported speech.","opts":["Mum said that she was going to the market.","Mum said that I am going to the market.","Mum said she will go to the market.","Mum said that she is going to the market."],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"sst-direct-indirect","explain":"直接引语变间接语三处必改: I→she, am going→was going(时态退一步)。「she was going」这项两处都到位, 判分点就在时态后移。「she is going」那项人称改对了却没退时态, 转述过去说的话必须用过去时。考点: PSLE爱考reported speech的时态后移加人称转换。"},{"q":"\"We will visit you tomorrow,\" they promised.","rule":"Rewrite in reported speech.","opts":["They promised that they would visit us the next day.","They promise that they will visit us tomorrow.","They promised that they would visit us tomorrow.","They promised that we will visit you tomorrow."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-direct-indirect","explain":"三处齐变: will→would, tomorrow→the next day, you→us。「would visit us the next day」这项三点全中。「would visit me the next day」那项最迷惑, 时态和时间词都对了, us偷偷变成me, 人称漏改照样扣分。考点: PSLE爱考tomorrow→the next day的时间词转换。"},{"q":"\"Do you like ice cream?\" she asked me.","rule":"Rewrite in reported speech.","opts":["She asked me that I liked ice cream.","She asked me if I liked ice cream.","She asked me do I like ice cream.","She asked me whether do I like ice cream."],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-direct-indirect-question","explain":"yes/no问句转述要用if或whether引出, 而且改成陈述语序: 「if I liked ice cream」, like还要退成liked。「whether do I like ice cream」那项最坑, whether后面还留着疑问语序, 转述后不能再倒装。考点: PSLE爱考间接问句一律用陈述语序。"},{"q":"\"Don't run in the corridor,\" the teacher told us.","rule":"Rewrite in reported speech.","opts":["The teacher told us don't run in the corridor.","The teacher said us not to run in the corridor.","The teacher told us not to run in the corridor.","The teacher told us to not run in the corridor."],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-direct-indirect-imperative","explain":"否定命令转述有固定公式: told加人加not to加动词原形, 「told us not to run」正好踩中判分点。「to not run」那项语序错, not必须放在to前面; 「told us don't run」那项直接照抄祈使句也不行。考点: PSLE爱考not to do的否定祈使句转述。"},{"q":"\"Where did you put my keys?\" Dad asked.","rule":"Rewrite in reported speech.","opts":["Dad asked where I had put his keys.","Dad asked me where I put my keys.","Dad asked where did I put his keys.","Dad asked that where did I put his keys."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-direct-indirect-wh","explain":"wh-问句转述三步走: 陈述语序加时态退一步(did put→had put)加my→his。「where I had put his keys」三步齐全。「where did I put his keys」那项最迷惑, 只改了人称, 却留着疑问语序。考点: PSLE爱考wh-question转述要去掉did改成had done。"},{"q":"Mum told me not to stay up late.","rule":"Rewrite in direct speech.","opts":["\"Don't stay up late,\" Mum told me.","\"You must not stay up late,\" Mum told me.","\"I told you not to stay up late,\" Mum said.","\"Don't stay up late,\" Mum said to her."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-indirect-direct","explain":"not to stay还原成祈使句「Don't stay up late」, 转述动词told me原样保留, 听话人不能动。「Mum said to her」那项最坑, 句子看着通顺, 但原句是told me, 听话人是我不是她, 人称一错就丢分。考点: PSLE爱考间接转直接时人称要还原回对话现场。"},{"q":"\"I have already eaten,\" he said.","rule":"Rewrite in reported speech.","opts":["He said that I had already eaten.","He said that he already ate.","He said that he has already eaten.","He said that he had already eaten."],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-indirect-direct","explain":"现在完成 have eaten 转述要退成过去完成 had eaten, I 变 he, 「he had already eaten」两处都到位。「he has already eaten」人称对了时态没退; 「I had already eaten」时态退了人称没改, 读起来像他在说我; 「he already ate」是一般过去, 没退够。考点: PSLE 爱考 present perfect 转述变 past perfect。"},{"q":"\"Can you help me?\" she asked him.","rule":"Rewrite in reported speech.","opts":["She asked him could he help her.","She asked him if he could help her.","She asked him that he could help her.","She asked him if he can help me."],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-indirect-direct-question","explain":"yes/no 问句转述用 if 引出, 改陈述语序, can 退成 could, me 变 her, 「if he could help her」四处全中。「could he help her」留着疑问语序; 「if he can help me」时态和人称都没动; 「that he could help her」yes/no 问句不能用 that 引导。考点: PSLE 爱考 can→could 加人称还原。"},{"q":"\"I have been waiting for an hour,\" he complained.","rule":"Rewrite in reported speech.","opts":["He complains that he had been waiting for an hour.","He complained that I have been waiting for an hour.","He complained that he had been waiting for an hour.","He complained he has been waiting for an hour."],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-direct-indirect-perfect","explain":"现在完成进行时转述要退成过去完成进行时: have been waiting→「had been waiting」, I同时变he。「he has been waiting」那项最迷惑, 人称改对了, has却没退成had, 时态没后移就扣分。考点: PSLE爱考have been doing转述变had been doing。"},{"q":"\"Please close the door,\" the teacher said to Ali.","rule":"Rewrite in reported speech.","opts":["The teacher told Ali please close the door.","The teacher asked Ali close the door.","The teacher said Ali to close the door.","The teacher asked Ali to close the door."],"ans":3,"diff":3,"tag":"sst-direct-indirect-polite","explain":"带please的礼貌请求, 转述动词用asked, 结构是asked加人加to do, 「asked Ali to close the door」踩中判分点。「said Ali to close」那项最坑, said后面不能直接接人, 要么said to Ali, 要么换成told或asked。考点: PSLE爱考please请求句用ask sb to do转述。"},{"q":"The dog chased the cat.","rule":"Rewrite in the passive voice.","opts":["The dog was chased by the cat.","The cat has been chased by the dog.","The cat is chased by the dog.","The cat was chased by the dog."],"ans":3,"diff":3,"tag":"sst-active-passive","explain":"原句chased是过去式, 被动就得是「was chased by the dog」, 宾语cat挪到主语位, 时态一步不许变。「has been chased」那项最迷惑, 时态凭空升级成完成时。考点: PSLE爱考被动语态时态必须与原句一致。"},{"q":"Someone stole my bicycle yesterday.","rule":"Rewrite in the passive voice.","opts":["My bicycle has been stolen yesterday.","My bicycle is stolen yesterday.","Someone was stolen my bicycle.","My bicycle was stolen yesterday."],"ans":3,"diff":3,"tag":"sst-active-passive-agent","explain":"yesterday锁死过去式, 只能是「was stolen」; someone是无名氏, by someone可以省掉不写。「has been stolen yesterday」那项最坑, 完成时不能跟明确的过去时间词同框。考点: PSLE爱考yesterday直接排除present perfect。"},{"q":"The students are cleaning the classroom now.","rule":"Rewrite in the passive voice.","opts":["The classroom was being cleaned now.","The classroom is cleaned by the students now.","The classroom has been cleaned now.","The classroom is being cleaned by the students now."],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-active-passive-continuous","explain":"现在进行时的被动是固定搭配「is being cleaned」, now保留在句尾。「is cleaned by the students」那项最迷惑, 那是一般现在时, 丢了正在进行的意思, 跟now对不上。考点: PSLE爱考进行时被动写成is being done。"},{"q":"They will announce the results next week.","rule":"Rewrite in the passive voice.","opts":["The results are announced next week.","The results will announce next week.","The results will be announced next week.","The results would be announced next week."],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-active-passive-future","explain":"将来时被动公式是will加be加过去分词, 即「will be announced」, 时态跟着原句的will走。「would be announced」那项最坑, 偷偷降成过去将来, 原句根本没有这个语境。考点: PSLE爱考will be done的将来被动。"},{"q":"The cake was baked by my grandmother.","rule":"Rewrite in the active voice.","opts":["My grandmother has baked the cake.","My grandmother was baking the cake.","My grandmother baked the cake.","The cake baked my grandmother."],"ans":2,"diff":3,"tag":"sst-passive-active","explain":"was baked还原成主动就是过去式「baked the cake」, grandmother回到主语位置。「was baking the cake」那项最迷惑, 进行时是自己加的, 原句只是简单过去。考点: PSLE爱考被动转主动只换语态不换时态。"},{"q":"You must complete the assignment by Friday.","rule":"Rewrite in the passive voice.","opts":["You must be completed the assignment.","The assignment must be completed by Friday.","The assignment is completed by Friday.","The assignment must complete by Friday."],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-active-passive-modal","explain":"情态动词的被动公式是must加be加过去分词, 「must be completed」少一个be都不行。「must complete by Friday」那项最坑, 缺了be变成主动形式, 作业自己完成自己, 语法崩了。考点: PSLE爱考modal加be加done的被动结构。"},{"q":"The children have eaten all the cookies.","rule":"Rewrite in the passive voice.","opts":["All the cookies were eaten by the children.","All the cookies has been eaten by the children.","All the cookies had been eaten.","All the cookies have been eaten by the children."],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-active-passive-perfect","explain":"现在完成时被动是have/has been加过去分词, 主语cookies是复数, 所以用「have been eaten」。「has been eaten by the children」那项主谓不一致; 「were eaten」那项语法本身没错, 但把完成时改成过去时, 时态就不忠实原句了。考点: PSLE爱考完成时被动的have/has选择。"},{"q":"People speak English all over the world.","rule":"Rewrite in the passive voice.","opts":["English is spoken all over the world.","English has been spoken all over the world.","English was spoken all over the world.","English speaks all over the world."],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"sst-active-passive-general","explain":"讲普遍事实用一般现在时被动「is spoken」, people泛指做主语可以整个省掉。「has been spoken」那项最坑, 看着高级, 但原句说的是习惯性事实, 不该换成完成时。考点: PSLE爱考general truth用一般现在时被动。"},{"q":"The letter was written by Sarah.","rule":"Rewrite in the active voice.","opts":["Sarah wrote the letter.","Sarah writes the letter.","Sarah has written the letter.","Sarah was writing the letter."],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"sst-passive-active","explain":"was written还原成主动就是过去式「wrote the letter」, Sarah做主语, 干净利落。「has written the letter」那项最迷惑, 时态升级成完成时, 语态转换只换语态不换时态。考点: PSLE爱考语态转换时时态原封不动。"},{"q":"They are going to build a new mall here.","rule":"Rewrite in the passive voice.","opts":["A new mall is going to be built here.","A new mall is built here.","A new mall was going to be built here.","A new mall will going to be built here."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-active-passive-going to","explain":"be going to的被动只改后半段: going to后面加be加过去分词, 写成「is going to be built」, here留在句尾。「will going to be built」那项最坑, will和going to两个将来结构叠在一起, 不能混用。考点: PSLE爱考going to结构的被动只动后半段。"},{"q":"Study hard or you will fail.","rule":"Rewrite using \"If\".","opts":["If you fail, you will study hard.","If you study hard, you will fail.","If you do not study hard, you will fail.","If you do not fail, study hard."],"ans":2,"diff":3,"tag":"sst-if","explain":"祈使句加or的意思是不照做就有坏结果, 改写成If要反着说: 「If you do not study hard」再接原后果will fail。「If you study hard, you will fail」那项最迷惑, 照抄命令却没加否定, 逻辑正好颠倒。考点: PSLE爱考祈使句加or改If时要补上否定。"},{"q":"If you do not hurry, you will miss the bus.","rule":"Rewrite using \"Unless\".","opts":["Unless you do not hurry, you will miss the bus.","Unless you hurry, you will not miss the bus.","Unless you hurry, you will miss the bus.","Unless you miss the bus, you will hurry."],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-unless","explain":"Unless本身就等于if not, 所以原句的do not hurry要写成肯定的「Unless you hurry」, 主句照抄。「Unless you do not hurry」那项最坑, unless后面又放not, 双重否定把意思弄反。考点: PSLE爱考Unless等于If not, 后面不能再加not。"},{"q":"Unless she apologizes, I will not forgive her.","rule":"Rewrite using \"If\".","opts":["If she does not apologize, I will not forgive her.","If she does not apologize, I will forgive her.","If she apologizes, I will not forgive her.","If I do not forgive her, she will apologize."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-unless-to-if","explain":"Unless she apologizes拆开就是「If she does not apologize」, 主句「I will not forgive her」一个字都别动。那项写成「I will forgive her」的最迷惑, 前半句拆对了, 后半句却把not forgive改成forgive, 结果整个反了。考点: PSLE爱考Unless转If只改条件句, 主句原样保留。"},{"q":"Bring an umbrella or you will get wet.","rule":"Rewrite using \"Unless\".","opts":["Unless you bring an umbrella, you will not get wet.","Unless you get wet, bring an umbrella.","Unless you do not bring an umbrella, you will get wet.","Unless you bring an umbrella, you will get wet."],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-unless","explain":"带伞是不淋湿的条件, 「Unless you bring an umbrella」正好表达不带就湿, 后果照抄will get wet。那项写成「Unless you do not bring an umbrella」的最坑, unless已含否定还加do not, 变成带了伞反而淋湿。考点: PSLE爱考Unless句内不能再放not。"},{"q":"If it does not rain, we will have a barbecue.","rule":"Rewrite using \"Unless\".","opts":["Unless it does not rain, we will have a barbecue.","Unless we have a barbecue, it will not rain.","Unless it rains, we will not have a barbecue.","Unless it rains, we will have a barbecue."],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-if-to-unless","explain":"If it does not rain等于「Unless it rains」, 动词回到肯定形式, 主句we will have a barbecue照搬。那项写成「we will not have a barbecue」的最迷惑, 前半漂亮, 后半偷偷加了not, 烧烤泡汤。考点: PSLE爱考If not转Unless只改条件句不动主句。"},{"q":"You cannot enter unless you have a ticket.","rule":"Rewrite using \"If\".","opts":["If you cannot enter, you do not have a ticket.","If you do not enter, you have a ticket.","If you do not have a ticket, you cannot enter.","If you have a ticket, you cannot enter."],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-unless-to-if","explain":"unless等于if not, 所以unless you have a ticket要展开成「If you do not have a ticket」, 主句cannot enter原样保留。那项写成「If you have a ticket, you cannot enter」的丢了否定, 意思变成有票反而进不去, 正好说反。考点: PSLE爱考unless和if not互换只改条件句。"},{"q":"Work harder or you will not get promoted.","rule":"Rewrite using \"If\".","opts":["If you get promoted, work harder.","If you work harder, you will not get promoted.","If you do not work harder, you will not get promoted.","If you do not get promoted, work harder."],"ans":2,"diff":3,"tag":"sst-if","explain":"祈使句加or是警告, 改If要给命令补否定: 「If you do not work harder」再接原后果will not get promoted。那项写成「If you work harder, you will not get promoted」的漏了do not, 变成越努力越不升职, 逻辑颠倒。考点: PSLE爱考or前的命令改成if否定条件, 主句照抄。"},{"q":"If she does not practise daily, she will not improve.","rule":"Rewrite using \"Unless\".","opts":["Unless she improves, she will not practise.","Unless she practises daily, she will not improve.","Unless she does not practise daily, she will improve.","Unless she practises, she will improve."],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-if-to-unless","explain":"if...not直接换成unless, 动词回到肯定的「Unless she practises daily」, 主句will not improve不动。那项写成「Unless she does not practise daily」的双重否定, unless自带not, 不能再否定一次。考点: PSLE爱考unless后必须用肯定动词, 双重否定必错。"},{"q":"Unless you leave now, you will be late.","rule":"Rewrite using \"If\".","opts":["If you do not leave, you will not be late.","If you are late, leave now.","If you do not leave now, you will be late.","If you leave now, you will be late."],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-unless-to-if","explain":"unless换成if not: unless you leave now要写成「If you do not leave now」, 主句you will be late照抄。那项写成「If you leave now, you will be late」的只换了词没补not, 变成走了反而迟到, 意思反了。考点: PSLE爱考unless转if要补出do not, 条件与结果关系不能变。"},{"q":"Be quiet or the teacher will punish you.","rule":"Rewrite using \"Unless\".","opts":["Unless the teacher punishes you, be quiet.","Unless you are not quiet, the teacher will punish you.","Unless you are quiet, the teacher will punish you.","Unless you are quiet, the teacher will not punish you."],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-unless","explain":"命令Be quiet的反面是不安静, 写成「Unless you are quiet」就等于如果你不安静, 后面接原后果老师会罚你。那项写成「Unless you are not quiet」的加了not, 双重否定意思拧了。考点: PSLE爱考unless从句里动词保持肯定形式。"},{"q":"The box was too heavy for me to carry.","rule":"Rewrite using \"so...that\".","opts":["The box was so heavy that I carried it.","The box is so heavy that I could not carry.","The box was so heavy that I could not carry it.","The box was so heavy that I can carry it."],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-too-to-so-that","explain":"too...to换so...that, 否定要显式写出来, 而且that从句必须完整: 「so heavy that I could not carry it」, 句尾的it不能少。那项写成「that I can carry it」的丢了not还把could换成can, 变成重到搬得动, 意思相反。考点: PSLE爱考so...that后补could not加宾语it。"},{"q":"She is so kind that everyone likes her.","rule":"Rewrite using \"such\".","opts":["She is such kind that everyone likes her.","She is such a kind person that everyone likes her.","Such kind she is that everyone likes her.","She is such a kind that everyone likes her."],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-so-to-such","explain":"so加形容词换成such时必须补一个名词: 「such a kind person」, 因为such修饰的是名词短语, 不是光秃秃的形容词。那项写成「such kind that」的让such直接接形容词, 那是so的用法。考点: PSLE爱考so加形容词对应such加冠词加形容词加名词。"},{"q":"He ran so fast that no one could catch him.","rule":"Rewrite using \"too...to\".","opts":["He ran too fast for anyone to catch.","He was too fast for anyone catching him.","He ran too fast for anyone to catch him.","He ran too fast that no one could catch."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-so-to-too","explain":"too...to 结构里, 如果不定式的宾语就是主句主语本人, 必须省略 —— 写成 for anyone to catch him 里的 him 是多余的, 这是全国最高频的失分点之一。for anyone 不能省(它交代了\"谁去抓\"); too...that 不是合法搭配。"},{"q":"The boy is too short to reach the shelf.","rule":"Rewrite using \"not...enough\".","opts":["The boy is not enough tall to reach the shelf.","The boy is not tall enough to reach the shelf.","The boy is not short enough to reach the shelf.","The boy is enough short to reach the shelf."],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-too-to-enough","explain":"too short是矮到够不着, 换成not...enough就要换反义词: 「not tall enough」, 不够高才对得上。那项写成「not short enough」的照抄了short, 意思变成不够矮, 跟够不着货架完全对不上。考点: PSLE爱考too加形容词转not加反义词加enough。"},{"q":"She is not old enough to drive.","rule":"Rewrite using \"too...to\".","opts":["She is not too old to drive.","She is too old to drive.","She is too enough to drive.","She is too young to drive."],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-enough-to-too","explain":"not old enough是年纪不够大, 换too要用反义词: 「too young to drive」, 太小所以不能开车。那项写成「too old to drive」的照抄old, 变成太老不能开, 年龄方向整个反了。考点: PSLE爱考enough转too必须换成反义形容词。"},{"q":"It was such a boring movie that we left early.","rule":"Rewrite using \"so...that\".","opts":["The movie so boring was that we left.","The movie was so boring that we left early.","It was so a boring movie that we left.","The movie was so boring such that we left early."],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-such-to-so","explain":"such加名词转so要把名词提到主语位: 「The movie was so boring that」, so后面只跟形容词。那项写成「so boring such that」的把两个结构叠着用, 一句话只能选一个, 混用必错。考点: PSLE爱考such加名词与so加形容词的互换。"},{"q":"The water is too cold for swimming.","rule":"Rewrite using \"so...that\".","opts":["The water is so cold that we can swim.","The water is so cold that it is too cold.","The water is so cold for swimming.","The water is so cold that we cannot swim in it."],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-too-to-so-that","explain":"too cold for swimming是冷到没法游, 转so...that要把结果写成完整否定句「so cold that we cannot swim in it」, cannot和句尾的in it都不能省。那项写成「that we can swim」的丢了not, 变成冷到能游泳, 因果荒唐。考点: PSLE爱考too自带否定, 转so...that必须补cannot。"},{"q":"He spoke so softly that I could not hear him.","rule":"Rewrite using \"too...to\".","opts":["He spoke too softly for me to hear.","He spoke too softly that I could not hear.","He spoke too softly to hear him.","He was too soft for me to hear."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-so-to-too","explain":"so softly that I could not hear him换too...to, 否定收进too里, 听的人用for me引出: 「too softly for me to hear」, 句尾不再加him。那项写成「too softly to hear him」的漏了for me, 读起来像他自己听不见自己, 对象丢了。考点: PSLE爱考too...to用for sb标明谁做不到。"},{"q":"The question was too difficult for us to answer.","rule":"Rewrite using \"so...that\".","opts":["The question was so difficult that we could not answer it.","The question was so difficult to answer.","The question so difficult that we could not answer.","The question was so difficult that we answer it."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-too-to-so-that","explain":"too...to转so...that, that后面要写完整句: 「so difficult that we could not answer it」, could not和宾语it都得补齐。那项写成「that we answer it」的没有not, 变成难到我们答出来了, 前后矛盾。考点: PSLE爱考so...that从句补could not加代词宾语。"},{"q":"It was such a heavy bag that she could not lift it.","rule":"Rewrite using \"too...to\".","opts":["The bag was too heavy that she lifted it.","The bag was too heavy for her to lift.","It was too a heavy bag for her.","She was too heavy to lift the bag."],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-such-to-too","explain":"such a heavy bag she could not lift转too, 否定藏进too里: 「too heavy for her to lift」, to后面不再重复it。那项写成「too heavy that she lifted it」的把too和that混搭, too...to结构里不能出现that从句。考点: PSLE爱考too...to句尾不加宾语it也不接that从句。"},{"q":"She sings so well that she won the competition.","rule":"Rewrite using \"such\".","opts":["She sings such well that she won.","Such well she sings that she won.","She is such a good singer that she won the competition.","She is such good at singing that she won."],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-so-to-such","explain":"so加副词转such要变词性: 动词sing变名词singer, 副词well变形容词good, 合起来是「such a good singer」。那项写成「sings such well」的让such直接带副词, such只能修饰名词短语。考点: PSLE爱考so加副词转such时动词变名词、副词变形容词。"},{"q":"The child is not strong enough to move the table.","rule":"Rewrite using \"too...to\".","opts":["The child is too enough to move the table.","The child is too strong to move the table.","The child is too not strong to move.","The child is too weak to move the table."],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-enough-to-too","explain":"not strong enough是力气不够, 转too要换反义词: 「too weak to move the table」, 太弱所以搬不动。那项写成「too strong to move」的照抄strong, 变成太壮反而搬不动, 完全讲不通。考点: PSLE爱考enough转too要换反义形容词, 方向别搞反。"},{"q":"The soup was so hot that I burned my tongue.","rule":"Rewrite using \"such\".","opts":["It was such hot soup that I burned my tongue.","The soup was such hot that I burned.","It was such a hot soup that I burned my tongue.","Such hot soup that I burned my tongue."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-so-to-such","explain":"so加形容词转such要带上名词, 但soup是不可数名词, 前面不加冠词, 所以「such hot soup」才是标准写法, 判分点就在这个冠词上。那项写成「such a hot soup」的多了一个a, 不可数名词不能用a。考点: PSLE爱考such后面加不加冠词, 先看名词可不可数。"},{"q":"He is too tired to continue studying.","rule":"Rewrite using \"so...that\".","opts":["He is so tired that he can continue studying.","He is so tired to continue studying.","He is so tired that he cannot continue studying.","He so tired that he cannot continue."],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-too-to-so-that","explain":"too tired to continue转so...that, 要补出完整结果句「so tired that he cannot continue studying」, 否定必须明写出来。那项写成「that he can continue studying」的丢了not, 变成累到还能接着学, 因果反了。考点: PSLE爱考too自带否定, 转so...that要显式加cannot。"},{"q":"The room is big enough for ten people.","rule":"Rewrite using \"so...that\".","opts":["The room is so big that it can fit ten people.","The room is so big that ten people is enough.","The room is so big enough for ten.","The room so big that ten people fit."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-enough-to-so","explain":"big enough for ten people是肯定意思, 转so...that结果句就用can: 「so big that it can fit ten people」。那项写成「that ten people is enough」的错两处, 一是从句里又塞enough两种句型叠用, 二是ten people要配are不是is。考点: PSLE爱考enough转so...that用can表示做得到。"},{"q":"Although he was tired, he finished his homework.","rule":"Rewrite using \"Despite\".","opts":["Despite tired, he finished his homework.","Despite his tiredness, he not finished.","Despite being tired, he finished his homework.","Despite he was tired, he finished his homework."],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-although-despite","explain":"Although加句子转Despite要变短语, Despite是介词只吃名词或V-ing, 所以写「Despite being tired」。那项写成「Despite he was tired」的直接跟了完整主谓句, 介词后面不能有主语加动词。考点: PSLE爱考Despite接名词或being加形容词, 不接句子。"},{"q":"Despite the rain, we went for a walk.","rule":"Rewrite using \"Although\".","opts":["Although despite the rain, we walked.","Although it was raining, we went for a walk.","Although the rain, we went for a walk.","Although it rained, we did not walk."],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-despite-although","explain":"Despite加名词转Although要补出完整主谓: 「Although it was raining」, 天气句还得补上主语it。那项写成「Although the rain」的直接接名词没有动词, 那是Despite的接法, 两者用法正好互补。考点: PSLE爱考Although接完整句, Despite接名词短语。"},{"q":"She is smart but lazy.","rule":"Rewrite using \"Although\".","opts":["Although smart but lazy.","Although she is smart, but she is lazy.","Although she is smart, she is lazy.","Although she is smart and lazy."],"ans":2,"diff":3,"tag":"sst-but-although","explain":"but表转折, 换Although要把让步放前面: 「Although she is smart, she is lazy」, 惊讶点是聪明却懒。那项写成「Although she is lazy, she is smart」的把两个形容词对调, 强调重点整个反了。考点: PSLE爱考but转Although时转折方向不能变。"},{"q":"In spite of his age, he is still very active.","rule":"Rewrite using \"Although\".","opts":["Although he is old, he is still very active.","Although in spite of his age, he is active.","Although he is active, he is old.","Although his age, he is very active."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-in spite-although","explain":"In spite of his age转Although要把名词展开成句子, his age指他年纪大, 写成「Although he is old」。那项写成「Although his age」的只接了名词没有动词, Although必须带完整主谓结构。考点: PSLE爱考名词短语转Although从句要自己补出形容词句。"},{"q":"Although the food was expensive, we ordered it.","rule":"Rewrite using \"In spite of\".","opts":["In spite of expensive, we ordered it.","In spite although expensive, we ordered.","In spite of the food was expensive, we ordered.","In spite of the expensive food, we ordered it."],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-although-in spite","explain":"Although句子转In spite of短语, 要把the food was expensive压缩成名词短语「the expensive food」, 形容词挪到名词前面。那项写成「In spite of the food was expensive」的照抄完整句, 介词短语后不能接主谓句。考点: PSLE爱考In spite of加形容词加名词的压缩改写。"},{"q":"Despite studying hard, she failed the test.","rule":"Rewrite using \"Although\".","opts":["Although despite studying hard, she failed.","Although she studied hard, she failed the test.","Although she failed, she studied hard.","Although studying hard, she failed."],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-despite-although","explain":"Although后面必须接完整句子, 「Although she studied hard」主谓齐全, 前后意思也没颠倒。那项写成「Although despite studying hard」的最迷惑, Although和despite都是虽然, 挤在一起等于说了两遍, 只能二选一。考点: PSLE爱考Although接句子, Despite接名词或V-ing, 两者不同框。"},{"q":"He is rich but unhappy.","rule":"Rewrite using \"Despite\".","opts":["Despite rich, he is unhappy.","Despite his rich, he is unhappy.","Despite being rich, he is unhappy.","Despite he is rich, he is unhappy."],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-but-despite","explain":"Despite是介词, 后面只能接名词或V-ing, 所以形容词rich要包装成「Despite being rich」。那项写成「Despite he is rich」的看着通顺, 但介词后不能接完整句子, 那是Although的地盘。考点: PSLE爱考Despite加being加形容词, but句变Despite句必带being。"},{"q":"Although she was nervous, she gave an excellent speech.","rule":"Rewrite using \"In spite of\".","opts":["In spite of she was nervous, she gave a speech.","In spite of nervous, she gave a speech.","In spite of her nervousness, she gave an excellent speech.","In spite of her speech, she was nervous."],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-although-in spite","explain":"In spite of和Despite一样是介词, 后接名词, 所以形容词nervous要变名词: 「In spite of her nervousness」, 加her更完整。那项写成「In spite of she was nervous」的塞进了完整主谓句, 介词后不能带句子, 直接扣分。考点: PSLE爱考nervous变nervousness这类词形转换要背熟。"},{"q":"Despite the heavy traffic, he arrived on time.","rule":"Rewrite using \"Even though\".","opts":["Even though the traffic was heavy, he arrived on time.","Even though the heavy traffic, he arrived.","Even though he arrived, the traffic was heavy.","Even though despite heavy traffic, he arrived."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-despite-even though","explain":"Even though是连词, 后面要接完整句子, 名词短语得展开成「the traffic was heavy」, be动词要自己补出来。那项写成「Even though the heavy traffic」的照抄名词短语, 没有动词was, 句子残缺。考点: PSLE爱考Despite加名词改Even though加句子, 记得补be动词。"},{"q":"She is young but very responsible.","rule":"Rewrite using \"Despite\".","opts":["Despite young, she is responsible.","Despite she is young, she is responsible.","Despite her responsible, she is young.","Despite her young age, she is very responsible."],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-but-despite","explain":"Despite后面接名词短语, 「Despite her young age」把形容词young包进名词age里, 转换最地道。那项写成「Despite she is young」的接了完整句子, 介词despite后面绝不能有主语加动词。考点: PSLE爱考young改成her young age这种形容词转名词短语的包装术。"},{"q":"He is smart. He is also hardworking.","rule":"Combine using \"Not only...but also\".","opts":["He is not only smart but also hardworking.","He is not only smart and also hardworking.","He is not only smart but hardworking also.","Not only he is smart but also hardworking."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-not only but also","explain":"not only和but also要放在对称位置, 后面各跟一个形容词: 「not only smart but also hardworking」, 结构工整。那项写成「not only smart and also hardworking」的用and替了but, 这是固定搭配, not only只配but also。考点: PSLE爱考关联连词固定配对, 一个字都不能换。"},{"q":"She can sing. She can also dance.","rule":"Combine using \"Both...and\".","opts":["She can both sing and also dance.","She can both sing and dance.","She both can sing and dance.","Both she can sing and dance."],"ans":1,"diff":3,"tag":"sst-both and","explain":"both...and连接的两样要对称, 都放在情态动词can后面: 「can both sing and dance」, sing和dance都是动词原形。那项写成「both sing and also dance」的多塞了一个also, both...and本身已表示两者都, also纯属画蛇添足。考点: PSLE爱考both...and的平行结构, and后面不加also。"},{"q":"Tom did not come. Jerry did not come.","rule":"Combine using \"Neither...nor\".","opts":["Neither Tom nor Jerry came.","Neither Tom or Jerry came.","Neither Tom nor Jerry did not come.","Neither Tom and Jerry came."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-neither nor","explain":"neither...nor本身就是否定, 动词用肯定式就够了: 「Neither Tom nor Jerry came」, 意思是两人都没来。那项写成「nor Jerry did not come」的又加一次否定, 双重否定反而变成两人都来了, 意思整个反。考点: PSLE爱考neither...nor自带否定, 动词绝不能再用not。"},{"q":"You can have tea. You can have coffee.","rule":"Combine using \"Either...or\".","opts":["You can have either tea or coffee.","You can have either tea nor coffee.","Either you can have tea or coffee.","You can have either tea and coffee."],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"sst-either or","explain":"either...or连接的是两个选项, 都放在have后面: 「have either tea or coffee」, tea和coffee对称, 位置最工整。那项写成「can either have tea or coffee」的把either提前, 连起来的变成have tea和coffee, 两边不对称。考点: PSLE爱考either...or要紧贴两个并列词的正前方。"},{"q":"She plays the piano. She also plays the violin.","rule":"Combine using \"Not only...but also\".","opts":["She not only plays piano but also the violin.","She plays not only the piano but also the violin.","Not only she plays piano but also violin.","She plays not only piano and also violin."],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-not only but also","explain":"not only和but also各接一个名词短语, 冠词the都保留: 「not only the piano but also the violin」, 结构平衡。那项写成「not only plays piano but also the violin」的前面接动词后面接名词, 词性不对称还丢了the。考点: PSLE爱考平行结构, not only后是什么词性but also后就得是什么。"},{"q":"The movie was not funny. It was not interesting either.","rule":"Combine using \"Neither...nor\".","opts":["The movie neither was funny nor interesting.","The movie was neither funny nor interesting.","The movie was neither funny or interesting.","Neither the movie was funny nor interesting."],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-neither nor","explain":"neither...nor放在was后面, 对称连接两个形容词: 「neither funny nor interesting」, 位置正确。那项写成「neither funny or interesting」的用or代替nor, neither的固定搭档只有nor, neither配or是经典陷阱。考点: PSLE爱考neither配nor不配or, 看到neither先找nor。"},{"q":"He can fix the car. His brother can fix the car.","rule":"Combine using \"Both...and\".","opts":["Both he and his brother can fix the car.","Both him and his brother can fix the car.","Both he or his brother can fix the car.","He both and his brother can fix the car."],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"sst-both and","explain":"both...and连接两个主语时要用主格: 「Both he and his brother」, 后面动词can不变。那项写成「Both him and his brother」的用了宾格him, 口语常这么说, 但做主语必须用主格, PSLE按书面语法判。考点: PSLE爱考并列主语用主格, 不是宾格。"},{"q":"You must leave now. Otherwise, you will be late.","rule":"Combine using \"Either...or\".","opts":["You either leave now or will be late.","Either leave now or late.","Either you leave now or you will be late.","Either you leave now and you will be late."],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-either or","explain":"either...or要连两个完整分句才对称: 「Either you leave now or you will be late」, 要么现在走要么迟到, 逻辑通。那项写成「You either leave now or will be late」的把主语提前, or后面只剩will be late没有主语, 两边不对称。考点: PSLE爱考otherwise句改Either...or, 两边各留一个完整分句最稳。"},{"q":"She did not eat the cake. She did not eat the pie.","rule":"Combine using \"Neither...nor\".","opts":["She neither ate the cake nor the pie.","Neither she ate cake nor pie.","She ate neither cake or pie.","She ate neither the cake nor the pie."],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-neither nor","explain":"判分点在 neither…nor 要对称卡住两个宾语——「She ate neither the cake nor the pie」把动词 ate 提到外面只写一次, neither 后是 the cake, nor 后是 the pie, 两边都是名词, 冠词也齐。最迷惑的是「She neither ate the cake nor the pie」: neither 后接动词 ate, nor 后接名词, 前后词性不对称。「She ate neither cake or pie」更直接, neither 只能配 nor 不能配 or。考点: PSLE 爱考 neither…nor 紧贴并列成分, 动词放外面只写一次。"},{"q":"He is talented. He is also humble.","rule":"Combine using \"Not only...but also\".","opts":["He is not only talented but also humble.","He not only is talented but also humble.","Not only is he talented but also humble.","He is not only talented and humble."],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"sst-not only but also","explain":"判分点是 not only…but also 要对称连接两个形容词, talented 和 humble 都挂在同一个 is 后面, 所以「He is not only talented but also humble」结构最工整。最迷惑的是「Not only is he talented but also humble」: 倒装本身是高级用法, 但后半截没补 he is, 前后不完整。「He is not only talented and humble」把 but also 换成 and, 关联词配错。考点: not only…but also 必须成对且平行, 小学阶段别碰倒装, 老实放在 be 动词后最安全。"},{"q":"The chef had prepared the meal before the guests arrived.","rule":"Rewrite in passive voice.","opts":["The meal had prepared by the chef before the guests arrived.","The meal had been prepared by the chef before the guests arrived.","The meal has been prepared by the chef before the guests arrived.","The meal was prepared by the chef before the guests arrived."],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-passive","explain":"原句 had prepared 是过去完成, 被动要写 had been + 过去分词, 「The meal had been prepared」时态和结构都对上。「The meal was prepared」把过去完成降级成一般过去, 丢了'更早发生'的意思; 「The meal had prepared」缺 been 变回主动; 「has been prepared」用现在完成, 和后面的 arrived 对不上。"},{"q":"They are repairing the road outside our school.","rule":"Rewrite in passive voice.","opts":["The road outside our school has been repaired.","The road outside our school is repaired.","The road outside our school is being repaired.","The road outside our school was being repaired."],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-passive","explain":"现在进行 are repairing 变被动是 is being + 过去分词, 「The road outside our school is being repaired」保住了'正在进行'。「The road outside our school is repaired」漏了 being 变成一般现在; 「has been repaired」是现在完成(已经修完); 「was being repaired」时间跑到了过去。being 绝不能省。"},{"q":"The teacher will mark the exam papers this weekend.","rule":"Rewrite in passive voice.","opts":["The exam papers will marked by the teacher this weekend.","The exam papers are marked by the teacher this weekend.","The exam papers will be marked by the teacher this weekend.","The exam papers will have been marked by the teacher this weekend."],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-passive","explain":"will + 动词原形变被动是 will be + 过去分词, 「The exam papers will be marked by the teacher」对。「The exam papers will marked」漏了 be, 光有过去分词撑不起被动; 「will have been marked」变成将来完成, 语义成了'到那时已改完'; 「are marked by the teacher this weekend」把将来改成现在时, 和 this weekend 打架。"},{"q":"Someone has stolen my bicycle from the bicycle stand.","rule":"Rewrite in passive voice.","opts":["My bicycle has been stolen from the bicycle stand.","My bicycle is stolen from the bicycle stand.","My bicycle had been stolen from the bicycle stand.","My bicycle was stolen from the bicycle stand."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-passive","explain":"现在完成 has stolen 变被动是 has been + 过去分词, 「My bicycle has been stolen」保留了'到现在还没找回'。「My bicycle was stolen」降成一般过去只讲事发那一刻; 「My bicycle is stolen」是现在时; 「had been stolen」是过去完成, 句里没有更早的参照点。someone 作主语改被动就直接删掉施动者, 时态原样保留, PSLE 高频陷阱。"},{"q":"The children must complete their homework before bedtime.","rule":"Rewrite in passive voice.","opts":["Their homework must completed by the children before bedtime.","Their homework must be completed by the children before bedtime.","Their homework must to be completed by the children before bedtime.","Their homework must has been completed by the children before bedtime."],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-passive","explain":"情态动词后面变被动是 must be + 过去分词, 「Their homework must be completed by the children」对。「Their homework must completed」漏了 be; 「must has been completed」在情态动词后塞 has, 语法不成立; 「must to be completed」多了 to, 情态动词后面永远不加 to。"},{"q":"\"I have finished my homework,\" Mary told her mother.","rule":"Rewrite in indirect speech.","opts":["Mary told her mother that I had finished my homework.","Mary told her mother that she has finished her homework.","Mary told her mother she finished her homework.","Mary told her mother that she had finished her homework."],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-indirect","explain":"间接引语要时态后退: 现在完成 have finished 退成过去完成, my 跟着 Mary 变 her, 所以「she had finished her homework」对。「she has finished her homework」时态没退; 「she finished her homework」跳成一般过去, 丢了'已完成'这层; 「I had finished my homework」人称没改, 读起来变成 Mary 在转述自己。"},{"q":"\"Will you help me with this exercise?\" Lisa asked her brother.","rule":"Rewrite in indirect speech.","opts":["Lisa asked her brother that he would help her with this exercise.","Lisa asked her brother if he will help her with this exercise.","Lisa asked her brother would he help her with that exercise.","Lisa asked her brother if he would help her with that exercise."],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-indirect","explain":"yes/no 问句转述要用 if 或 whether 引导并改陈述语序, 同时 will 退成 would、this 变 that、me 变 her, 「if he would help her with that exercise」三样全中。「if he will help her with this exercise」时态和 this 都没动; 「that he would help her」用 that 引导 yes/no 问句是错的; 「would he help her with that exercise」保留了疑问语序。"},{"q":"\"What time does the show start?\" the boy asked.","rule":"Rewrite in indirect speech.","opts":["The boy asked what time the show started.","The boy asked what time did the show start.","The boy asked that what time the show started.","The boy asked what time does the show start."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-indirect","explain":"Wh- 问句间接化要拆掉助动词 does、改成陈述语序、时态后退, 所以「what time the show started」对。「what time did the show start」保留了助动词和疑问语序; 「what time does the show start」时态没变; 「that what time the show started」在疑问词前多加 that, 两个引导词撞车。"},{"q":"\"You must wear your school uniform tomorrow,\" the teacher said to us.","rule":"Rewrite in indirect speech.","opts":["The teacher told us that we must wear our school uniform tomorrow.","The teacher told us that we had to wear our school uniform the next day.","The teacher said to us that we had to wear our school uniform tomorrow.","The teacher told us that we have to wear our school uniform the next day."],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-indirect","explain":"转述三件事同时做: must 退成 had to(也可保留 must)、said to 换成 told、tomorrow 换成 the next day, 「told us that we had to wear our school uniform the next day」全做到了。「that we must wear our school uniform tomorrow」时间词没换; 「The teacher said to us that…」该用 told 且 tomorrow 没换; 「we have to wear … the next day」have to 没退成 had to。"},{"q":"\"Don't touch the wet paint,\" the painter warned them.","rule":"Rewrite in indirect speech.","opts":["The painter warned them that they don't touch the wet paint.","The painter warned them to not touch the wet paint.","The painter warned them not to touch the wet paint.","The painter warned them don't touch the wet paint."],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-indirect","explain":"否定祈使句转述用 warned + 人 + not to + 动词原形, not 必须放在 to 前面, 「warned them not to touch the wet paint」对。「warned them don't touch」把原句的祈使形式整个搬了过来; 「that they don't touch」加了 that 从句, 结构不对; 「to not touch」是分裂不定式, PSLE 判错。"},{"q":"The food was delicious. It was very expensive.","rule":"Combine using \"Although\".","opts":["Although the food was delicious, but it was very expensive.","Although that the food was delicious, it was very expensive.","Although the food was delicious, it was very expensive.","Although the food being delicious, it was very expensive."],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-although","explain":"Although 是连词, 后面要跟主语加动词的完整从句, 「Although the food was delicious, it was very expensive」对。「Although the food being delicious」用了 -ing, 连词后面不能接分词短语; 「Although that the food was delicious」多了一个 that。 另加一个: 「Although the food was delicious, but it was very expensive」把 although 和 but 同时用了, 英语里这两个连词只能留一个。"},{"q":"It was raining heavily. We continued our football match.","rule":"Combine using \"Despite\".","opts":["Despite the heavy rain, we continued our football match.","Despite raining heavily, we continued our football match.","Despite of the heavy rain, we continued our football match.","Despite it was raining heavily, we continued our football match."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-despite","explain":"Despite 是介词, 后面只能接名词短语, 所以要把'下大雨'名词化成「Despite the heavy rain」。「Despite it was raining heavily」后面跟了完整句子, 那是 Although 的活; 「Despite of the heavy rain」多了 of, 带 of 的是 in spite of; 「Despite raining heavily」缺主语, 读起来像我们在下雨。考点: despite 接名词、although 接句子。"},{"q":"He is rich. He is not happy.","rule":"Combine using \"Although\".","opts":["Although he is rich, but he is not happy.","Despite he is rich, he is not happy.","Although he is rich, however he is not happy.","Although he is rich, he is not happy."],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-although","explain":"Although 后面要跟完整从句, 「Although he is rich, he is not happy」主谓齐全。「Despite he is rich」用介词接了句子; 「Although he is rich, but he is not happy」是中式的'虽然…但是…', 英语里 although 和 but 只能留一个。 另加一个: 「Although he is rich, however he is not happy」把 although 和 however 叠在一起, 同样是连词冗余。"},{"q":"Tom worked hard. He failed the exam.","rule":"Combine using \"Despite\".","opts":["Despite of working hard, Tom failed the exam.","Despite Tom worked hard, he failed the exam.","Despite working hard, Tom failed the exam.","Despite he worked hard, Tom failed the exam."],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-despite","explain":"Despite 后接动名词时, 这个动作的执行者必须和主句主语一致, 「Despite working hard, Tom failed the exam」里努力的和考砸的都是 Tom。「Despite he worked hard」和「Despite Tom worked hard」都在介词后面塞了完整句子; 「Despite of working hard」多了 of。"},{"q":"The weather was bad. The event was a success.","rule":"Combine using \"In spite of\".","opts":["In spite of the bad weather, the event was a success.","In spite of the weather was bad, the event was a success.","In spite the bad weather, the event was a success.","In spite of that the weather was bad, the event was a success."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-in spite of","explain":"In spite of 是三个词的固定介词短语, 后面接名词, 所以把 the weather was bad 名词化成「In spite of the bad weather」。「In spite the bad weather」漏了 of; 「In spite of that the weather was bad」多了 that 还带从句; 「In spite of the weather was bad」介词后面直接跟了句子。in spite of 必带 of, despite 绝不带 of。"},{"q":"The box is too heavy. I cannot lift it.","rule":"Combine using \"so...that\".","opts":["The box is so heavy that I cannot lift it.","The box is such heavy that I cannot lift it.","The box is so heavy so that I cannot lift it.","The box is too heavy that I cannot lift it."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-so that","explain":"so + 形容词 + that 是固定框架, 「The box is so heavy that I cannot lift it」对。「so heavy so that I cannot lift it」多了一个 so, that 前面不用再加; 「too heavy that I cannot lift it」把 too 和 that 拼在一起, too 只能配 to; 「such heavy that」用错词, such 后面要跟名词。"},{"q":"It was a difficult question. Nobody could answer it.","rule":"Combine using \"such...that\".","opts":["It was such difficult question that nobody could answer it.","It was so difficult question that nobody could answer it.","It was such a difficult question and nobody could answer it.","It was such a difficult question that nobody could answer it."],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-such that","explain":"such + a/an + 形容词 + 名词 + that 是完整模板, 「It was such a difficult question that nobody could answer it」对。「It was so difficult question」用 so 直接修饰名词短语是错的; 「It was such difficult question」漏了 a, question 是可数单数必须带冠词; 「such a difficult question and nobody could answer it」用 and 丢掉了结果关系。"},{"q":"She runs very fast. She always wins the race.","rule":"Combine using \"so...that\".","opts":["She runs such fast that she always wins the race.","She runs so fast that she always wins the race.","She runs so fast and always wins the race.","She runs so fast that she always win the race."],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-so that","explain":"so 也可以修饰副词, 「She runs so fast that she always wins the race」里 fast 是副词, 后面接 that 结果从句。「She runs so fast and always wins the race」用 and 只是并列, 没有因果; 「that she always win the race」主谓不一致, 该用 wins; 「She runs such fast」用错词, such 不能修饰副词。"},{"q":"The film was boring. We all fell asleep.","rule":"Combine using \"so...that\".","opts":["The film was so boring, so we all fell asleep.","The film was so a boring one that we all fell asleep.","The film was so boring that we all fell asleep.","The film was such boring that we all fell asleep."],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-so that","explain":"so + 形容词 + that 的标准写法是「The film was so boring that we all fell asleep」。「The film was such boring that…」用 such 直接接形容词是错的; 「The film was so boring, so we all fell asleep」两个 so 重复, 结果只需交代一次。 另加一个: 「The film was so a boring one that…」在 so 后面塞了冠词, so 只能直接接形容词或副词。"},{"q":"The puzzle was easy. Even my little brother solved it.","rule":"Combine using \"such...that\".","opts":["It was so easy puzzle that even my little brother solved it.","It was such easy puzzle that even my little brother solved it.","It was such a easy puzzle that even my little brother solved it.","It was such an easy puzzle that even my little brother solved it."],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-such that","explain":"such 后面的冠词看读音: easy 以元音音素开头, 所以「It was such an easy puzzle that…」对。「It was such easy puzzle」漏了冠词; 「It was so easy puzzle」用 so 修饰名词短语; 「It was such a easy puzzle」冠词选错, 元音音素前要用 an。冠词按后面单词的读音定, 不看拼写。"},{"q":"John is a teacher. His wallet was stolen.","rule":"Combine using \"whose\".","opts":["John, whose wallet was stolen, is a teacher.","John who his wallet was stolen, is a teacher.","The teacher John, whose wallet was stolen.","John whose wallet was stolen, is a teacher."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-relative-whose","explain":"whose 直接顶替 his, 而且 John 是唯一确定的人, 非限定从句要前后各一个逗号, 「John, whose wallet was stolen, is a teacher」对。「John whose wallet was stolen, is a teacher」漏了左逗号; 「John who his wallet was stolen」用了 who 又留着 his, 所有格重复; 「The teacher John, whose wallet was stolen」没有主句谓语, 句子没写完。🎯 孩子真题卷 D34 题错的就是这型!"},{"q":"I met a girl. Her father is a doctor.","rule":"Combine using \"whose\".","opts":["I met a girl whose her father is a doctor.","I met a girl, who father is a doctor.","I met a girl who her father is a doctor.","I met a girl whose father is a doctor."],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-relative-whose","explain":"whose 已经等于 her, 后面直接接名词, 而且这里在交代'哪个女孩', 属于限定从句不加逗号, 「I met a girl whose father is a doctor」对。「who her father is a doctor」who 后面又冒出 her; 「whose her father is a doctor」所有格写了两遍; 「I met a girl, who father is a doctor」既加了逗号又丢了所有格关系代词。"},{"q":"The book is on the table. Its cover is red.","rule":"Combine using \"whose\".","opts":["The book whose the cover is red is on the table.","The book whose cover is red is on the table.","The book whose its cover is red is on the table.","The book which cover is red is on the table."],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-relative-whose","explain":"whose 不只代人, 也能代物的 its, 而且要区分'哪一本书', 属于限定从句不加逗号, 「The book whose cover is red is on the table」对。「whose the cover is red」在 whose 后又加冠词; 「which cover is red」which 不能当所有格; 「whose its cover is red」whose 和 its 重复。whose 后面直接跟名词, 一个都不能多。"},{"q":"My friend lost her cat. The cat's collar is red.","rule":"Combine using \"whose\".","opts":["My friend lost her cat, which collar is red.","My friend lost her cat whose the collar is red.","My friend lost her cat whose its collar is red.","My friend lost her cat whose collar is red."],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-relative-whose","explain":"whose 也能代替 the cat's 这种物的所有格, 后面直接接名词 collar, 限定从句不加逗号, 「her cat whose collar is red」对。「whose its collar」所有格写了两遍; 「whose the collar」whose 后不能再加冠词; 「which collar is red」which 不能当所有格。考点: whose 后面直接跟名词, 一个都不能多。"},{"q":"The student got an award. His project won the competition.","rule":"Combine using \"whose\".","opts":["The student whose project won the competition got an award.","The student got an award whose his project won the competition.","The student, whose project won the competition got an award.","The student which project won the competition got an award."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-relative-whose","explain":"这里靠从句区分'哪一个学生', 属于限定从句, 一个逗号都不加, 「The student whose project won the competition got an award」对。「The student, whose project won the competition got an award」只加了左逗号没封口; 「which project won the competition」which 不能指人; 「got an award whose his project won」语序乱了还多出 his。"},{"q":"I borrowed a book from the library. The book was very interesting.","rule":"Combine using \"which\".","opts":["The book which I borrowed from the library was very interesting.","I borrowed a book from the library which was very interesting.","The book whom I borrowed from the library was very interesting.","The book what I borrowed from the library was very interesting."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-relative-which","explain":"限定从句交代'哪一本书', 用 which 引导并紧贴被修饰的名词, 「The book which I borrowed from the library was very interesting」对。「The book what I borrowed」用 what 引导定语从句是错的; 「The book whom I borrowed」whom 只能指人; 「a book from the library which was very interesting」把从句甩到 library 后面, 分不清有趣的是书还是图书馆。"},{"q":"The car was very expensive. It was parked outside the house.","rule":"Combine using \"which\".","opts":["The car who was parked outside the house was very expensive.","The car which it was parked outside the house was very expensive.","The car which was parked outside the house was very expensive.","The car which parked outside the house was very expensive."],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-relative-which","explain":"原句 It was parked 是被动, 搬进从句时被动结构要完整保留, 「The car which was parked outside the house」对。「The car which parked outside the house」少了 be 动词, 变成汽车自己去停车; 「The car who was parked outside」用 who 指物是错的; 「The car which it was parked outside」which 已经代替 the car 了, 后面不能再来一个 it。"},{"q":"The cake was delicious. My mum baked it for my birthday.","rule":"Combine using \"which\".","opts":["The cake whom my mum baked for my birthday was delicious.","The cake which my mum baked for my birthday was delicious.","The cake which my mum baked it for my birthday was delicious.","The cake which was my mum baked for my birthday was delicious."],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-relative-which","explain":"which 在从句里当宾语, 从句里就不能再留宾语代词, 「The cake which my mum baked for my birthday was delicious」对, 这种作宾语的 which 甚至可以整个省掉。「which my mum baked it for my birthday」多了一个 it, 和 which 重复; 「which was my mum baked」多了 was, 主动被动混在一起; 「The cake whom my mum baked」whom 只能指人。"},{"q":"The movie won the award. We watched the movie last night.","rule":"Combine using \"which\".","opts":["The movie that we watched last night, won the award.","The movie which we watched last night won the award.","The movie which won the award we watched last night.","The movie won the award which we watched last night."],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-relative-which","explain":"which 在从句里作 watched 的宾语, 从句要紧贴 movie, 限定从句不加逗号, 「The movie which we watched last night won the award」对。「we watched last night, won the award」在主语和谓语中间硬塞了逗号; 「which won the award we watched last night」语序乱了; 「won the award which we watched last night」让 which 挨着 award, 修饰错了名词。"},{"q":"The new park is beautiful. It was opened last month.","rule":"Combine using \"which\".","opts":["The new park which it was opened last month is beautiful.","The new park was opened last month which is beautiful.","The new park, who was opened last month, is beautiful.","The new park, which was opened last month, is beautiful."],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-relative-which","explain":"the new park 已经是确定的对象, 补充说明用非限定从句, 前后各一个逗号, 「The new park, which was opened last month, is beautiful」对。「which it was opened last month」which 后面又加 it, 重复; 「who was opened last month」用 who 指物是错的; 「was opened last month which is beautiful」让 which 跑到句尾, 修饰的名词错位。"},{"q":"The boy is my classmate. He won the spelling bee.","rule":"Combine using \"who\".","opts":["The boy he won the spelling bee is my classmate.","The boy which won the spelling bee is my classmate.","The boy whom won the spelling bee is my classmate.","The boy who won the spelling bee is my classmate."],"ans":3,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-relative-who","explain":"从句里缺的是主语(原句的 He), 所以用主格关系代词 who, 「The boy who won the spelling bee is my classmate」对。「The boy whom won the spelling bee」whom 是宾格, 这里要当主语; 「The boy which won the spelling bee」which 不能指人; 「The boy he won the spelling bee」直接留着 he, 没有关系代词把两句连起来。"},{"q":"I have a neighbour. She is a famous singer.","rule":"Combine using \"who\".","opts":["I have a neighbour which is a famous singer.","I have a neighbour whom is a famous singer.","I have a neighbour who is a famous singer.","I have a neighbour who she is a famous singer."],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-relative-who","explain":"从句在交代'哪一个邻居', 属于限定从句不加逗号, 而且 who 在从句里作主语, 「I have a neighbour who is a famous singer」对。「who she is a famous singer」who 后面又冒出 she, 主语写了两遍; 「whom is a famous singer」用宾格当主语; 「which is a famous singer」which 不能指人。"},{"q":"My grandmother makes the best cookies. She lives next door.","rule":"Combine using \"who\".","opts":["My grandmother who lives next door, makes the best cookies.","My grandmother that lives next door, makes the best cookies.","My grandmother, who lives next door makes the best cookies.","My grandmother, who lives next door, makes the best cookies."],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-relative-who","explain":"My grandmother 是独一无二的人, 从句只作补充说明, 非限定从句前后都要逗号, 「My grandmother, who lives next door, makes the best cookies」对。「My grandmother who lives next door, makes…」漏了左逗号; 「who lives next door makes the best cookies」漏了右逗号没封口; 「My grandmother that lives next door」用 that 引导非限定从句是错的, 非限定只能用 who/which。"},{"q":"The man is my uncle. I spoke to him yesterday.","rule":"Combine using \"whom\".","opts":["The man whom I spoke to yesterday is my uncle.","The man which I spoke to yesterday is my uncle.","The man who I spoke to him yesterday is my uncle.","The man whom I spoke to him yesterday is my uncle."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-relative-whom","explain":"从句里缺的是介词 to 的宾语(原句的 him), 所以用宾格 whom 并把 him 删掉, 「The man whom I spoke to yesterday is my uncle」对。「whom I spoke to him yesterday」whom 和 him 重复; 「who I spoke to him yesterday」既用错格又留着 him; 「The man which I spoke to yesterday」which 不能指人。"},{"q":"The teacher gave me extra help. I thanked her yesterday.","rule":"Combine using \"whom\".","opts":["The teacher who I thanked her yesterday gave me extra help.","The teacher whom I thanked yesterday gave me extra help.","The teacher whose I thanked yesterday gave me extra help.","The teacher whom gave me extra help I thanked yesterday."],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-relative-whom","explain":"原句里 her 是 thanked 的宾语, 所以用宾格 whom 并把 her 删掉, 「The teacher whom I thanked yesterday gave me extra help」对。「who I thanked her yesterday」多留了 her; 「whom gave me extra help I thanked yesterday」把主句从句对调, 语序错了; 「whose I thanked yesterday」whose 是所有格, 后面必须接名词。缺宾语用 whom, 缺所有格才用 whose。"},{"q":"Meiling is the most hardworking pupil in her class.","rule":"Rewrite using \"No other\".","opts":["No other pupil in her class is as more hardworking as Meiling.","No others pupil in her class is as hardworking as Meiling.","No other pupil in her class is so hardworking than Meiling.","No other pupil in her class is as hardworking as Meiling."],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-最高级-no other as as","explain":"最高级转换的固定模板是 No other + 单数名词 + is as + 形容词原级 + as + 人, 「No other pupil in her class is as hardworking as Meiling」对。「is so hardworking than Meiling」错在 as 要配 as 不能配 than; 「No others pupil in her class」错在 No other 不能写成 No others。 另加一个: 「is as more hardworking as」把原级比较 as…as 和比较级 more 混在一起, 两种结构只能用一种。"},{"q":"The Nile is the longest river in the world.","rule":"Rewrite using \"any other\".","opts":["The Nile is longer than the other river in the world.","The Nile is longer than any other rivers in the world.","The Nile is longer than any other river in the world.","The Nile is the longer than any other river in the world."],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-最高级-any other","explain":"模板是 主语 + 比较级 + than any other + 单数名词, 「The Nile is longer than any other river in the world」对。「than any other rivers in the world」错在 any other 后面要用单数 river; 「The Nile is the longer than any other river」比较级前多了 the; 「than the other river in the world」的 the other 表示'两者中的另一个', 但世界上不止两条河。考点: PSLE 最爱把 the + 最高级 与 比较级 + than any other 互换。"},{"q":"I spent two hours completing the science project.","rule":"Rewrite beginning with \"It\".","opts":["It spent me two hours to complete the science project.","It took me two hours to complete the science project.","It took two hours for me completing the science project.","It took me two hours completing the science project."],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-spend-take句型","explain":"spend 和 take 的句型是对应的: 人 + spend + 时间 + doing, 而 It + take + 人 + 时间 + to do, 所以「It took me two hours to complete the science project」对。「It spent me two hours to complete」错在 spend 的主语必须是人不能是 It; 「It took two hours for me completing」错在 take 后面要接 to do 不接 doing; 「It took me two hours completing」把两个句型混在了一起。考点: PSLE 常考 spend / take / cost 三个'花费'动词的句型互换。"},{"q":"I last saw my cousin three years ago.","rule":"Rewrite using \"since\".","opts":["It was three years since I last saw my cousin.","It has three years since I last saw my cousin.","It is three years since I last saw my cousin.","It is three years since I have last seen my cousin."],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-It is since句型","explain":"固定句型是 It is + 时间段 + since + 一般过去时从句, 主句用现在时, 「It is three years since I last saw my cousin」对。「It was three years since I last saw my cousin.」用 was 会变成在讲过去某个时点的事; 「It is three years since I have last seen my cousin」的 since 从句必须用一般过去时不能用完成时; 「It has three years since I last saw my cousin.」缺了 be 动词。考点: It is … since … 句型, 从句一律一般过去。"},{"q":"The boy finished his homework. He then went out to play.","rule":"Combine using \"Having\".","opts":["Having finished his homework, the boy went out to play.","Having finished his homework and he went out to play.","Having finished his homework, the boy had gone out to play.","Having finished his homework, his mother let him play."],"ans":0,"diff":6,"tag":"sst-Having done分词","explain":"Having + 过去分词表示先完成的动作, 它的逻辑主语必须和主句主语一致——做作业的是 the boy, 主句主语也得是 the boy, 所以「Having finished his homework, the boy went out to play」对。「Having finished his homework, his mother let him play」是典型的悬垂分词, 读起来变成妈妈做完了作业; 「Having finished his homework and he went out to play」多了 and; 「the boy had gone out to play」时态重复。考点: 判分点就是主句主语必须是这个动作的执行者。"},{"q":"As soon as she heard the news, she burst into tears.","rule":"Rewrite using \"On\".","opts":["On hearing the news, she burst into tears.","On to hear the news, she burst into tears.","On heard the news, she burst into tears.","On she heard the news, she burst into tears."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-On+ing","explain":"On 是介词, 后面只能接动名词, On + v-ing 相当于 as soon as, 所以「On hearing the news, she burst into tears」对。「On heard the news」用了过去式; 「On to hear the news」用了不定式, 介词后面不能接 to do; 「On she heard the news」在介词后面塞了完整句子。考点: '一…就…'有三种写法 — as soon as / On + ing / No sooner…than。"},{"q":"He woke up at five o'clock. He wanted to catch the first bus.","rule":"Combine using \"so as to\".","opts":["He woke up at five o'clock so as to catch the first bus.","He woke up at five o'clock so as catching the first bus.","He woke up at five o'clock so as he could catch the first bus.","He woke up at five o'clock so as to catching the first bus."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-so as to目的","explain":"so as to + 动词原形表示目的, 「so as to catch the first bus」对。「so as to catching the first bus」错在 to 后面要用原形; 「so as catching the first bus」直接漏了 to; 「so as he could catch the first bus」把 so as to 和 so that 混用了, 只有 so that 后面才跟从句。考点: to / in order to / so as to 后面都接动词原形, 只有 so that 接从句。"},{"q":"It is useless to argue with him about the rules.","rule":"Rewrite using \"no point\".","opts":["There is no point in arguing with him about the rules.","It is no point in arguing with him about the rules.","There is no point of arguing with him about the rules.","There is no point to argue with him about the rules."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-no point in doing","explain":"固定句型是 There is no point in + 动名词, 「There is no point in arguing with him about the rules」对。「There is no point to argue with him」错在 point 后面要用 in + ing 不是 to do; 「There is no point of arguing」介词选错了; 「It is no point in arguing」主语必须是 There 不是 It。考点: There is no point in doing / It is no use doing / It is pointless to do, 三个句型的主语和介词各不相同。"},{"q":"She would rather stay at home than go to the party.","rule":"Rewrite using \"prefer\".","opts":["She prefers to stay at home than to go to the party.","She prefers stay at home to go to the party.","She prefers staying at home than going to the party.","She prefers staying at home to going to the party."],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-prefer A to B","explain":"prefer 甲 to 乙 的两边都要用动名词, 中间的介词是 to 不是 than, 「She prefers staying at home to going to the party」对。「prefers staying at home than going to the party」和「prefers to stay at home than to go to the party」都错用了 than, 那是 would rather…than 的搭配; 「prefers stay at home to go to the party」两处都缺 -ing。考点: prefer 配 to, would rather 配 than, 这两个句型常放一起考。"},{"q":"My elder sister broke the window, not me.","rule":"Rewrite beginning with \"It was\".","opts":["It was my elder sister whom broke the window, not me.","It was my elder sister broke the window, not me.","It was my elder sister who broke the window, not me.","It was my elder sister which broke the window, not me."],"ans":2,"diff":6,"tag":"sst-强调句It was who","explain":"强调句型是 It is/was + 被强调部分 + who/that + 其余部分; 被强调的是人而且在从句里作主语, 所以「It was my elder sister who broke the window, not me」对。「It was my elder sister broke the window」漏了 who, 两个动词直接撞在一起; 「my elder sister whom broke the window」whom 只能作宾语; 「my elder sister which broke the window」which 只指物。考点: 强调句的判分点是 who/that 绝对不能省。"},{"q":"Although the question was very difficult, he answered it correctly.","rule":"Rewrite using \"However\".","opts":["However the difficult question was, he answered it correctly.","However difficult was the question, he answered it correctly.","However difficult the question was, he answered it correctly.","However the question was difficult, he answered it correctly."],"ans":2,"diff":6,"tag":"sst-However让步语序","explain":"However 表让步时语序固定: However + 形容词/副词 + 主语 + 动词, 所以「However difficult the question was, he answered it correctly」对。「However difficult was the question」多加了倒装; 「However the difficult question was」把形容词塞进了名词短语里; 「However the question was difficult」把形容词丢到了后面。考点: However / No matter how 让步句, 形容词必须紧跟在 However 后面。"},{"q":"You may borrow my bicycle if you return it before dinner.","rule":"Rewrite using \"provided that\".","opts":["You may borrow my bicycle provided that you return it before dinner.","You may borrow my bicycle provided that returning it before dinner.","You may borrow my bicycle provided that you will return it before dinner.","You may borrow my bicycle provided that you returned it before dinner."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-provided that条件","explain":"provided that 等于 if, 后面接完整从句并遵守'主将从现', 从句用一般现在时, 所以「provided that you return it before dinner」对。「provided that you will return it」用了 will; 「provided that you returned it」用了过去式, 和主句的 may 对不上; 「provided that returning it before dinner」没有主语, 不成从句。考点: if / provided that / as long as / on condition that, 从句一律用现在时表将来。"},{"q":"I am sorry that I did not revise for the spelling test.","rule":"Rewrite using \"wish\".","opts":["I wish I would revise for the spelling test.","I wish I have revised for the spelling test.","I wish I had revised for the spelling test.","I wish I revised for the spelling test."],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-wish过去完成","explain":"对已经发生的事表示后悔, wish 后面用过去完成时, 「I wish I had revised for the spelling test」对。「I wish I revised」的过去式表示与现在事实相反; 「I wish I would revise」的 would 表示对将来的愿望; 「I wish I have revised」的现在完成在 wish 后面不成立。考点: wish 三档时态 — 现在用过去式, 过去用过去完成, 将来用 would。"},{"q":"The headmaster awarded Siti a certificate for perfect attendance.","rule":"Rewrite in the passive voice, beginning with \"Siti\".","opts":["Siti was awarded a certificate for perfect attendance by the headmaster.","Siti awarded a certificate for perfect attendance by the headmaster.","Siti was awarded by the headmaster a certificate for perfect attendance.","Siti has awarded a certificate for perfect attendance by the headmaster."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-双宾语被动","explain":"双宾语动词变被动时, 间接宾语 Siti 做主语, 直接宾语 a certificate 留在动词后面, 施动者用 by 放句末, 所以「Siti was awarded a certificate for perfect attendance by the headmaster」对。「Siti awarded a certificate…by the headmaster」缺了 was, 变成 Siti 在发奖状; 「Siti has awarded a certificate…」的 has awarded 仍是主动; 「Siti was awarded by the headmaster a certificate…」把 by 短语插在中间, 语序不地道。考点: 判分点是保留哪个宾语以及 by 短语的位置。"},{"q":"People say that durians have a very strong smell.","rule":"Rewrite beginning with \"Durians\".","opts":["Durians are said to have a very strong smell.","Durians are said having a very strong smell.","Durians are said that they have a very strong smell.","Durians said to have a very strong smell."],"ans":0,"diff":6,"tag":"sst-be said to被动","explain":"People say that + 从句变被动有固定写法: 主语 + be said + to do, 所以「Durians are said to have a very strong smell」对。「Durians are said having a very strong smell」漏了 to 还用了 -ing, be said 后面固定接不定式; 「Durians are said that they have a very strong smell」把 that 从句和被动混用了; 「Durians said to have a very strong smell.」缺了 are, 变成主动。考点: People say / It is said that / X is said to… 三种写法互换是高分题。"},{"q":"\"You should see a doctor immediately,\" the coach said to Rahim.","rule":"Rewrite in reported speech using \"advised\".","opts":["The coach advised to Rahim to see a doctor immediately.","The coach advised Rahim that to see a doctor immediately.","The coach advised Rahim to see a doctor immediately.","The coach advised Rahim seeing a doctor immediately."],"ans":2,"diff":6,"tag":"sst-advise sb to do","explain":"advise sb to do sth 是固定结构, 人直接跟在动词后面, 「The coach advised Rahim to see a doctor immediately」对。「advised to Rahim to see a doctor」在人前面多加了 to; 「advised Rahim that to see a doctor」多了 that, that 后面得跟完整从句; 「advised Rahim seeing a doctor」用 -ing 不成立。考点: advise / remind / warn / order / beg + 人 + to do 这批动词后面都直接跟人。"},{"q":"\"Do not swim beyond the red flags,\" the lifeguard said to the boys.","rule":"Rewrite in reported speech using \"warned\".","opts":["The lifeguard warned the boys do not swim beyond the red flags.","The lifeguard warned the boys to not swim beyond the red flags.","The lifeguard warned the boys not to swim beyond the red flags.","The lifeguard warned to the boys not to swim beyond the red flags."],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-warn not to","explain":"否定祈使句转述用 warned + 人 + not to + 动词原形, not 要放在 to 前面, 所以「warned the boys not to swim beyond the red flags」对。「warned the boys to not swim」把 not 放到了 to 后面, 是分裂不定式, PSLE 判错; 「warned the boys do not swim」保留了原句的祈使形式; 「warned to the boys not to swim」在人前面多加了 to。考点: 每年都考否定祈使句转述, not to 的位置就是判分点。"},{"q":"The match was postponed because the pitch was flooded.","rule":"Rewrite using \"owing to\".","opts":["The match was postponed owing to that the pitch was flooded.","The match was postponed owing to the flooded pitch.","The match was postponed owing the flooded pitch.","The match was postponed owing to the pitch was flooded."],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-owing to名词化","explain":"owing to 是介词短语, 后面只能接名词或动名词, 所以要把从句名词化成「owing to the flooded pitch」。「owing the flooded pitch」漏了 to; 「owing to the pitch was flooded」和「owing to that the pitch was flooded」都在介词后面跟了句子, 一个直接跟, 一个还多加了 that。考点: because 接句子, 而 because of / due to / owing to / on account of 一律接名词。"},{"q":"The traffic was so heavy that we missed the opening ceremony.","rule":"Rewrite using \"such\".","opts":["It was such heavy traffic that we missed the opening ceremony.","It was so heavy traffic that we missed the opening ceremony.","It was such heavy traffic and we missed the opening ceremony.","It was such a heavy traffic that we missed the opening ceremony."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-such+不可数","explain":"traffic 是不可数名词, such 后面不能加 a, 所以「It was such heavy traffic that we missed the opening ceremony」对。「It was such a heavy traffic that…」多了 a; 「It was so heavy traffic that…」用 so 修饰名词短语是错的, so 只修饰形容词和副词; 「It was such heavy traffic and we missed…」把结果状语从句改成了并列句, 丢了 that。考点: 用 such 改写时先判断名词可数不可数 — 只有可数单数才加 a, traffic / weather / furniture / homework 都不加。"},{"q":"The soup was so salty that nobody could finish it.","rule":"Rewrite using \"too\".","opts":["The soup was too salty for nobody to finish.","The soup was too salty for anyone to finish it.","The soup was too salty that nobody could finish.","The soup was too salty for anyone to finish."],"ans":3,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-too to省略宾语","explain":"too…to 改写有两个判分点: 否定词换成 anyone, 而且不定式的宾语和主语重复时必须省掉, 所以「The soup was too salty for anyone to finish」句末不再补 it。「too salty for anyone to finish it」多了 it, 这是最常见的失分点; 「too salty for nobody to finish」的 too…to 本身已含否定, 再用 nobody 就成了双重否定; 「too salty that nobody could finish」保留了 that 从句, too 不能配 that。"},{"q":"Although he was seriously injured, the striker played the whole match.","rule":"Rewrite using \"Despite\".","opts":["Despite of his serious injury, the striker played the whole match.","Despite his serious injury, the striker played the whole match.","Despite he was seriously injured, the striker played the whole match.","Despite seriously injured, the striker played the whole match."],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-Despite名词化","explain":"Despite 是介词, 后面只能接名词短语, 所以把 he was seriously injured 名词化成「Despite his serious injury」。「Despite of his serious injury」多了 of, 那是 in spite of 的写法; 「Despite he was seriously injured」后面跟了完整句子, 那是 although 的用法; 「Despite seriously injured」缺主语和限定词, 不成短语。考点: although 接句子与 despite / in spite of 接名词的互换, 判分点是形容词要变成名词并加所有格。"},{"q":"My brother cannot swim. I cannot swim either.","rule":"Combine using \"Neither\".","opts":["My brother cannot swim, and neither can I.","My brother cannot swim, and neither I can.","My brother cannot swim, and neither cannot I.","My brother cannot swim, and neither can I too."],"ans":0,"diff":6,"tag":"sst-neither倒装","explain":"neither 放在句首要倒装: neither + 助动词或情态动词 + 主语, 而且 neither 已含否定, 所以「and neither can I」用 can 不用 cannot。「and neither cannot I」是双重否定; 「and neither I can」没有倒装; 「and neither can I too」多了 too, neither 已经含否定不能再加。考点: So / Neither + 助动词 + 主语, 肯定用 So, 否定用 Neither, 两者都必须倒装。"},{"q":"This is the classroom. We took our oral examination in this classroom.","rule":"Combine using \"in which\".","opts":["This is the classroom in which we took our oral examination.","This is the classroom in that we took our oral examination.","This is the classroom in which we took our oral examination in it.","This is the classroom which we took our oral examination."],"ans":0,"diff":6,"tag":"sst-in which关系从句","explain":"介词 in 提到关系代词前面之后, 原句末尾的 in this classroom 就要整个删掉, 所以「the classroom in which we took our oral examination」对。「in which we took our oral examination in it」把介词写了两遍; 「the classroom which we took our oral examination」漏了介词 in, 从句缺成分; 「This is the classroom in that we took our oral examination.」的 that 不能跟在介词后面。考点: 介词 + which/whom 结构, 判分点是原句里那个介词短语必须消失。"},{"q":"The rain stopped at six o'clock. Only then did we start the game.","rule":"Rewrite using \"Not until\".","opts":["Not until did the rain stop at six o'clock we started the game.","Not until the rain stopped at six o'clock we started the game.","Not until the rain stopped at six o'clock we did start the game.","Not until the rain stopped at six o'clock did we start the game."],"ans":3,"diff":6,"tag":"sst-not until倒装","explain":"Not until 放在句首时主句要部分倒装, 而 until 引导的从句本身不倒装, 所以「Not until the rain stopped at six o'clock did we start the game」对。「…at six o'clock we started the game」主句没倒装; 「…at six o'clock we did start the game」助动词放错位置, 没形成倒装; 「Not until did the rain stop at six o'clock we started the game」把倒装用在了从句上, 主句反而没倒。考点: 倒装只发生在主句, 从句照常语序。"}];

function getSstByDiff(diff, n) { return _sampleByDiff(SST_QUESTIONS, diff, n || 5); }

// ============= v19.4: Comprehension OE 训练 (PSLE Paper 2 Section D 风格) =============
// 格式: passage + questions (literal/inferential/evaluative) + model answers
// App 内无法自动批改, 用 "自评" 模式: 读题→思考→查看 model answer→打分
const COMP_OE_PASSAGES = [{"id":"comp1","title":"The Lost Dog","diff":3,"wordCount":180,"passage":"Tom was walking home from school when he noticed a small brown dog sitting by the roadside. It looked thin and dirty, with a torn collar around its neck. The dog whimpered softly and looked up at Tom with sad eyes. Tom knelt down and gently stroked its head. He noticed a phone number on the collar tag, though it was partly scratched off. Tom took the dog home, gave it water and some leftover chicken. He spent the evening trying different number combinations until finally reaching the owner — an elderly woman named Mrs Chen who had been searching for three days. When she arrived, tears of joy streamed down her face as the dog leaped into her arms.","questions":[{"q":"What two signs suggested that the dog had been without an owner for some time?","type":"literal","marks":2,"model":"Tom knew the dog was lost because it looked thin and dirty, with a torn collar around its neck (1m). It was sitting alone by the roadside and whimpered softly, suggesting it had been without an owner for some time (1m)."},{"q":"What does the phrase \"tears of joy streamed down her face\" tell us about Mrs Chen's feelings?","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"The phrase tells us that Mrs Chen was overwhelmed with happiness and relief (1m). She had been searching for her dog for three days and had probably feared she would never see it again, so finding it safe made her extremely emotional (1m)."},{"q":"Do you think Tom did the right thing by taking the dog home? Give a reason.","type":"evaluative","marks":2,"model":"Yes, Tom did the right thing because the dog was hungry and dirty, meaning it needed immediate care (1m). He also made the effort to contact the owner using the collar tag, showing responsibility rather than just ignoring the dog's plight (1m)."}]},{"id":"comp2","title":"The School Garden","diff":3,"wordCount":160,"passage":"Our school started a garden project last term. Every class was given a small plot to grow vegetables. At first, many students were reluctant to get their hands dirty. However, as the weeks went by, we noticed tiny green shoots emerging from the soil. The excitement was contagious. Even the most reluctant students began checking on their plants every morning before assembly. By the end of the term, our class had harvested enough tomatoes and lettuce to make a salad for everyone. The principal praised our efforts and announced that the garden would become a permanent feature of the school.","questions":[{"q":"Why were many students reluctant at first?","type":"literal","marks":1,"model":"Many students were reluctant because they did not want to get their hands dirty (1m)."},{"q":"What does \"the excitement was contagious\" mean?","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"It means that the feeling of excitement spread from one student to another (1m), just like how a disease spreads. When some students got excited about the growing plants, their enthusiasm influenced other students to feel the same way (1m)."},{"q":"What lesson can students learn from this garden project?","type":"evaluative","marks":2,"model":"Students can learn that patience and perseverance lead to rewarding results (1m). Even though the work seemed unpleasant at first, sticking with it brought a sense of achievement and brought the class together (1m)."}]},{"id":"comp3","title":"The Flood","diff":4,"wordCount":200,"passage":"It had been raining incessantly for three days. The monsoon drains, which usually handled the heavy rainfall efficiently, were overwhelmed. Water began seeping into the ground-floor flats along Bukit Timah Road. Mr Lim, a retired teacher who lived alone, woke up at 5am to find murky brown water ankle-deep in his living room. His precious collection of books — accumulated over forty years of teaching — was being destroyed before his eyes. Neighbours rallied together, forming a human chain to pass sandbags and move furniture to higher ground. A young polytechnic student named Aisha waded through the floodwater to help Mr Lim carry his most treasured books to safety on the second floor of a nearby block. \"Community spirit,\" Mr Lim said later, his voice cracking with emotion, \"is what makes Singapore special.\"","questions":[{"q":"Why were the monsoon drains unable to cope with the rain?","type":"literal","marks":1,"model":"The monsoon drains were unable to cope because it had been raining incessantly (continuously without stopping) for three days, which was more than they could usually handle (1m)."},{"q":"Why was Mr Lim particularly upset about the flood damage?","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"Mr Lim was particularly upset because his precious collection of books, which he had accumulated over forty years of teaching, was being destroyed (1m). These books likely held great sentimental value as they represented his life's work and passion as a teacher (1m)."},{"q":"What does Mr Lim's final statement suggest about his values?","type":"evaluative","marks":2,"model":"His statement suggests that he values community spirit and togetherness above material possessions (1m). Despite losing his books, he was moved by how his neighbours and a stranger (Aisha) came together to help, showing that human connections matter more to him than things (1m)."},{"q":"Give one piece of evidence that shows the community helped Mr Lim.","type":"literal","marks":1,"model":"任答一个即可 (1m): ①Neighbours formed a human chain to pass sandbags and move furniture to higher ground; ②Aisha waded through the floodwater to help Mr Lim carry his books to safety. 陷阱: 题目说 one, 写两个不会加分, 但第一个写不完整就丢掉这 1 分。"}]},{"id":"comp4","title":"The Exam","diff":3,"wordCount":170,"passage":"Priya stared at the mathematics paper in front of her. Question 15 — a problem involving speed, distance and time — seemed impossible. Her mind went blank. She could hear the clock ticking loudly on the wall. Twenty minutes left. She took a deep breath, remembering what her tutor had taught her: \"Draw a diagram. Label what you know. The answer will come.\" Priya picked up her pencil and sketched a simple timeline. Slowly, the numbers began to make sense. She worked through each step carefully, checking her calculations twice. When the bell rang, she had not only solved Question 15 but had also checked the rest of her paper. Walking out of the hall, she felt a quiet confidence she had never felt before.","questions":[{"q":"What was Priya's initial reaction to Question 15?","type":"literal","marks":1,"model":"Priya's mind went blank and she felt the question was impossible (1m)."},{"q":"How did Priya overcome her difficulty?","type":"literal","marks":2,"model":"She remembered her tutor's advice to draw a diagram and label what she knew (1m). By following this strategy step by step and staying calm (taking a deep breath), she was able to work through the problem logically (1m)."},{"q":"What does \"a quiet confidence she had never felt before\" suggest about how this experience changed Priya?","type":"evaluative","marks":2,"model":"It suggests that overcoming this challenge gave Priya a new belief in her own abilities (1m). Unlike before, she now knows she can handle difficult problems by staying calm and using strategies, which will help her in future exams too (1m)."}]},{"id":"comp5","title":"The Hawker","diff":4,"wordCount":210,"passage":"Uncle Tan has been selling laksa at his hawker stall for thirty-five years. Every morning at 4am, he begins preparing the coconut broth from scratch — a recipe passed down from his mother. \"Young people don't want to do this work anymore,\" he said, wiping sweat from his forehead. \"They think it is low-class. But I am proud of what I do.\" His laksa has won numerous awards, and food bloggers from around the world have featured his stall. Despite offers from restaurant chains to franchise his recipe, Uncle Tan has always refused. \"If I sell the recipe, they will cut corners. Use powder instead of fresh spices. My customers will taste the difference.\" Now 68, Uncle Tan worries about who will take over when he retires. His two children are both engineers. \"I don't blame them,\" he says. \"I just hope someone who loves food will continue this tradition.\"","questions":[{"q":"At what time does Uncle Tan start preparing his laksa?","type":"literal","marks":1,"model":"Uncle Tan starts preparing his laksa at 4am every morning (1m)."},{"q":"Why has Uncle Tan refused to franchise his recipe?","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"He refused because he believes restaurant chains will cut corners by using powder instead of fresh spices (1m). He takes pride in the quality of his food and does not want his customers to taste a lesser version of his laksa (1m)."},{"q":"What does this passage suggest about the challenges facing Singapore's hawker culture?","type":"evaluative","marks":2,"model":"The passage suggests that hawker culture faces the challenge of succession — younger Singaporeans prefer professional careers and view hawker work as undesirable (1m). Without young people willing to learn traditional recipes and endure the hard work, iconic dishes like Uncle Tan's laksa may disappear when the current generation of hawkers retires (1m)."}]},{"id":"comp6","title":"The Bully","diff":4,"wordCount":190,"passage":"Marcus had been dreading recess every day for the past month. A group of older boys would wait near the canteen and demand his pocket money. If he refused, they would push him and call him names. He never told anyone — not his parents, not his teachers. He was afraid it would get worse. One day, his classmate Wei Ling noticed the bruises on his arm. \"Marcus, who did this to you?\" she asked quietly. When he finally told her everything, Wei Ling insisted they tell their form teacher, Mrs Goh. \"You are not alone in this,\" she said firmly. Mrs Goh took immediate action. The bullies were called to the principal's office that very afternoon. Looking back, Marcus realised that his silence had only given the bullies more power.","questions":[{"q":"How long had Marcus been bullied?","type":"literal","marks":1,"model":"Marcus had been bullied for the past month (1m)."},{"q":"Why did Marcus not tell anyone about the bullying?","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"Marcus did not tell anyone because he was afraid that reporting the bullying would make it worse (1m). He kept it from everyone, including his parents and teachers, so he had no one to help him and the bullying went on for a whole month (1m)."},{"q":"What does the last sentence \"his silence had only given the bullies more power\" mean?","type":"evaluative","marks":2,"model":"It means that by staying quiet and not seeking help, Marcus was unintentionally allowing the bullies to continue their behaviour without consequences (1m). Speaking up would have stopped them sooner, but his silence made them bolder and more confident that they could get away with it (1m)."}]},{"id":"comp7","title":"Technology in Schools","diff":5,"wordCount":220,"passage":"The Ministry of Education recently announced that all primary schools would be equipped with tablets for every student by 2028. Proponents argue that digital learning allows students to access a wealth of educational resources instantly and learn at their own pace. Interactive apps can make difficult concepts more engaging and provide immediate feedback. However, critics worry about the impact on children's eyesight and attention spans. Dr Sarah Koh, a child psychologist, warns that \"excessive screen time before age 12 has been linked to difficulty concentrating and reduced physical activity.\" Teachers have expressed mixed feelings. Mr Ahmad, who has taught for twenty years, notes: \"Technology is a tool, not a replacement for good teaching. A tablet cannot inspire a child the way a passionate teacher can.\" The debate highlights a fundamental question: in our rush to modernise, are we considering what children actually need to learn effectively?","questions":[{"q":"State one advantage of digital learning mentioned in the passage.","type":"literal","marks":1,"model":"任答一个即可 (1m): ①Digital learning allows students to access educational resources instantly and learn at their own pace; ②Interactive apps make difficult concepts more engaging and provide immediate feedback. 陷阱: 题目说 one, 挑一个写完整比两个都写半截强。"},{"q":"What is Dr Sarah Koh concerned about?","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"Dr Koh is concerned that too much screen time before age 12 can harm children's ability to concentrate (1m) and lead to reduced physical activity, which could affect their overall health and development (1m)."},{"q":"Do you agree with Mr Ahmad that \"a tablet cannot inspire a child the way a passionate teacher can\"? Explain your view.","type":"evaluative","marks":2,"model":"Accept any well-reasoned answer. Example (Agree): Yes, because a teacher can respond to a child's emotions, provide encouragement, and adapt their teaching to the moment (1m). Technology follows fixed programmes and cannot build the personal relationships that motivate students to try harder (1m)."}]},{"id":"comp8","title":"The Race","diff":3,"wordCount":160,"passage":"It was the final race of Sports Day — the 4x100 metre relay. Our class had been training every morning for two weeks. I was the last runner, the anchor. As the third runner sprinted towards me, I could see we were in second place. My heart pounded as I grabbed the baton and ran with everything I had. The wind rushed past my ears. I could hear my classmates screaming my name from the stands. With ten metres to go, I was neck and neck with the boy from Class 6A. I leaned forward and crossed the finish line. For a breathless moment, nobody knew who had won. Then the announcement came: \"Winner — Class 6B!\" The roar from my class was deafening.","questions":[{"q":"What position was the narrator's team in before the final leg?","type":"literal","marks":1,"model":"The team was in second place (1m)."},{"q":"Why did nobody know who had won immediately after the race? Give two reasons.","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"The narrator and the boy from Class 6A were neck and neck with ten metres to go, so they crossed the line almost at the same moment (1m). The result was so close that it had to wait for an official announcement before anyone could be sure (1m)."}]},{"id":"comp9","title":"The Old Tree","diff":4,"wordCount":190,"passage":"The ancient rain tree at the corner of Orchard Road had stood there for over a hundred years. Its massive canopy provided shade for generations of Singaporeans. Children climbed its gnarled roots; couples had their photographs taken beneath its branches; old men played chess in its cool shadow every afternoon. When the government announced plans to widen the road, the tree was marked for removal. A petition started by a secondary school student gathered over fifty thousand signatures in three days. Social media erupted with the hashtag #SaveOurTree. After much deliberation, the Land Transport Authority redesigned the road expansion to curve around the tree instead. \"This tree is not just wood and leaves,\" the student wrote in her petition. \"It is a piece of our collective memory.\"","questions":[{"q":"How old is the rain tree?","type":"literal","marks":1,"model":"The rain tree is over a hundred years old (1m)."},{"q":"Why did so many people sign the petition?","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"Many people signed because the tree held sentimental value — it was part of their shared experiences and memories across generations (1m). The passage shows people of all ages using the tree (children climbing, couples photographing, old men playing chess), suggesting it was a beloved community landmark (1m)."},{"q":"What does the student mean by \"a piece of our collective memory\"?","type":"evaluative","marks":2,"model":"She means the tree is not just a plant but a symbol that connects different generations of Singaporeans through shared experiences (1m). Removing it would be like erasing a part of the community's history and identity (1m)."}]},{"id":"comp10","title":"The New Student","diff":3,"wordCount":170,"passage":"When Xiao Ming joined our class in Term 2, he could barely speak English. He had just arrived from China and everything about Singapore school life was unfamiliar to him. During lessons, he would stare blankly at the whiteboard. At recess, he sat alone. One day, our teacher paired him with me for a science project. At first, communication was difficult. He would draw pictures to explain his ideas. Slowly, I realised he was actually brilliant at science — he just could not express it in English yet. I started teaching him simple phrases during our project meetings. By the end of term, Xiao Ming scored the highest in our science test. He stood up and said, carefully but clearly, \"Thank you, everyone, for helping me.\" The whole class cheered.","questions":[{"q":"What were Xiao Ming's two main challenges when he first arrived?","type":"literal","marks":2,"model":"His two main challenges were that he could barely speak English (1m) and everything about Singapore school life was unfamiliar to him (1m)."},{"q":"How did the narrator discover that Xiao Ming was good at science?","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"The narrator discovered this when they were paired for a science project. Although Xiao Ming could not express ideas in English, he drew pictures to explain them (1m), which showed the narrator that he had strong scientific understanding despite the language barrier (1m)."},{"q":"What message does this story convey about judging others?","type":"evaluative","marks":2,"model":"The story conveys that we should not judge people's intelligence or abilities based on their language skills alone (1m). Someone who struggles with English may still be extremely capable in other areas, and with patience and support, they can overcome the language barrier (1m)."}]},{"id":"comp11","title":"The Charity Run","diff":3,"wordCount":170,"passage":"Our school organised a charity run to raise funds for the Children's Cancer Foundation. Each student had to find sponsors who would donate based on the number of laps completed. I managed to get five sponsors, including my grandmother who promised ten dollars per lap. On the day of the run, the sun was blazing. By the fifth lap, my legs felt like jelly. I wanted to give up. Then I thought of the children in hospital who could not even run. I pushed through the pain and completed eight laps. When I told my grandmother, she was so proud that she doubled her donation. Together, our school raised over fifteen thousand dollars.","questions":[{"q":"What was the purpose of the charity run?","type":"literal","marks":1,"model":"The purpose was to raise funds for the Children's Cancer Foundation (1m)."},{"q":"What motivated the narrator to keep running despite wanting to give up?","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"The narrator thought of the children in hospital who could not even run (1m). This made the narrator feel that their own discomfort was small compared to what sick children faced, giving them the determination to push through (1m)."},{"q":"Why do you think the grandmother doubled her donation?","type":"evaluative","marks":2,"model":"The grandmother was proud of the narrator's perseverance and effort in completing eight laps despite the heat (1m). By doubling her donation, she was rewarding the narrator's determination and showing that she valued effort over just results (1m)."}]},{"id":"comp12","title":"The Stray Cat","diff":4,"wordCount":190,"passage":"A thin ginger cat had been appearing at our void deck every evening for a week. Its ribs were visible beneath matted fur, and it flinched at every loud noise. My sister and I started leaving food and water for it. Gradually, it began to trust us, allowing us to stroke its head. We named it Marmalade. When we asked our parents if we could keep it, they hesitated. \"Who will clean the litter box? Who will take it to the vet?\" Dad asked. We made a written contract promising to share all responsibilities. Two months later, Marmalade is a healthy, playful cat who greets us at the door every day. Dad, who was the most reluctant, is now the one who sneaks Marmalade extra treats when he thinks nobody is watching.","questions":[{"q":"How do we know the cat was in poor condition when first found?","type":"literal","marks":2,"model":"The cat was thin with its ribs visible beneath matted fur (1m). It also flinched at every loud noise, suggesting it was frightened and possibly mistreated before (1m)."},{"q":"Why did the children make a \"written contract\"?","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"They made a written contract to show their parents they were serious and responsible enough to care for a pet (1m). It addressed their parents' concerns about who would do the work by formally committing to share responsibilities (1m)."},{"q":"What is ironic about the ending?","type":"evaluative","marks":2,"model":"It is ironic that Dad, who was the most reluctant to keep the cat and questioned whether the children would be responsible, has now become the most attached (1m). He sneaks the cat extra treats, showing that despite his initial resistance, he has grown to love Marmalade the most (1m)."}]},{"id":"comp13","title":"Water Conservation","diff":4,"wordCount":200,"passage":"Singapore imports much of its water from Malaysia under an agreement that expires in 2061. To reduce this dependency, PUB has invested heavily in four \"National Taps\": local catchment, imported water, NEWater (recycled water), and desalination. Schools play a crucial role in water conservation education. At Riverside Primary, students monitor the school's daily water usage displayed on a digital dashboard. \"When the students see the numbers go up after someone leaves a tap running, they become water ambassadors themselves,\" explains the principal. Despite these efforts, Singapore's per capita water consumption remains at 141 litres per day — higher than the PUB target of 130 litres by 2030. Experts warn that with climate change making rainfall patterns more unpredictable, every drop saved today is an investment in tomorrow's security.","questions":[{"q":"Name two of Singapore's four \"National Taps\".","type":"literal","marks":1,"model":"Any two of: local catchment, imported water, NEWater (recycled water), desalination (1m for naming 2)."},{"q":"How does the digital dashboard help students learn about water conservation?","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"The dashboard shows real-time water usage, so when students see the numbers increase (e.g., after a tap is left running), they understand the immediate impact of waste (1m). This visual, concrete feedback turns abstract conservation messages into something personal and actionable (1m)."},{"q":"Why does the writer call saving water \"an investment in tomorrow's security\"?","type":"evaluative","marks":2,"model":"Because climate change is making rainfall patterns unpredictable, Singapore cannot rely on nature alone for its water supply (1m). Singapore's usage (141 litres per person per day) is still above the 2030 target of 130 litres, so every litre saved now helps close that gap and protects against future shortages (1m)."}]},{"id":"comp14","title":"The Piano Recital","diff":3,"wordCount":160,"passage":"My fingers trembled as I walked onto the stage. Three hundred people sat in the audience, including my piano teacher Mrs Wong, who had prepared me for this moment over two years. The lights were blinding. I sat down, placed my hands on the keys, and froze. My mind went completely blank — I could not remember the first note. The silence felt eternal. Then Mrs Wong's voice echoed in my head: \"If you forget, just breathe and listen to the music inside you.\" I closed my eyes, took a deep breath, and my fingers found the keys on their own. The melody of Chopin's Nocturne flowed through me. When I finished, the applause was thunderous. But the proudest face in the crowd was Mrs Wong's.","questions":[{"q":"What happened when the narrator first sat at the piano?","type":"literal","marks":1,"model":"The narrator froze and could not remember the first note — their mind went completely blank (1m)."},{"q":"How did Mrs Wong's advice help the narrator?","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"Her advice to \"breathe and listen to the music inside you\" helped the narrator relax and stop panicking (1m). By closing their eyes and breathing, the narrator let muscle memory take over, and their fingers found the keys automatically without conscious recall (1m)."}]},{"id":"comp15","title":"The Food Waste Problem","diff":5,"wordCount":210,"passage":"Singapore generates approximately 744,000 tonnes of food waste annually — enough to fill over 1,000 Olympic swimming pools. While some of this is unavoidable (bones, shells), studies suggest that up to 40% is perfectly edible food discarded due to cosmetic imperfections, over-ordering, or expiry date confusion. \"Best before\" dates indicate quality, not safety, yet most consumers throw food away the moment this date passes. Social enterprise \"SG Food Rescue\" redistributes surplus food from hotels and supermarkets to low-income families. Volunteer driver Mr Raj makes three trips daily: \"Sometimes I collect enough food for two hundred families from just one hotel buffet. It breaks my heart to think this was headed for the bin.\" The government's \"30 by 30\" goal — producing 30% of nutritional needs locally by 2030 — will only succeed if consumption habits change alongside production capacity.","questions":[{"q":"How much food waste does Singapore generate each year?","type":"literal","marks":1,"model":"Singapore generates approximately 744,000 tonnes of food waste annually (1m)."},{"q":"What is the difference between \"best before\" and actual food safety?","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"\"Best before\" dates indicate the period during which food is at its peak quality (taste, texture), not when it becomes unsafe to eat (1m). Many consumers mistakenly believe food is dangerous after this date and throw it away, when in reality it may still be perfectly safe to consume (1m)."},{"q":"Why does the writer say \"30 by 30\" will only succeed if consumption habits change?","type":"evaluative","marks":2,"model":"Because even if Singapore produces more food locally, it will not solve the problem if people continue to waste 40% of edible food (1m). Producing more without reducing waste is inefficient — the real solution requires both increasing supply and decreasing wasteful consumption (1m)."}]},{"id":"comp16","title":"Grandfather's Lesson","diff":3,"wordCount":170,"passage":"Every Sunday, my grandfather takes me fishing at Bedok Reservoir. We never catch much — sometimes nothing at all. My friends think it is boring. \"Why don't you just buy fish from the market?\" they ask. But fishing with Grandfather is not about the fish. It is about the stories he tells while we wait — stories of growing up in a kampong, of catching real fish in rivers that no longer exist. It is about learning patience, about sitting still in a world that never stops moving. Last Sunday, after three hours without a single bite, Grandfather smiled and said, \"The best things in life cannot be rushed.\" I think he was not talking about fishing anymore.","questions":[{"q":"Where does the narrator go fishing with his grandfather?","type":"literal","marks":1,"model":"They go fishing at Bedok Reservoir (1m)."},{"q":"Why does the narrator continue fishing despite never catching much?","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"The narrator values the time spent with grandfather — hearing stories about his past and learning life lessons like patience (1m). The activity itself is less important than the bonding and wisdom shared between them (1m)."},{"q":"What do you think the grandfather meant by \"The best things in life cannot be rushed\"?","type":"evaluative","marks":2,"model":"He likely meant that important things like relationships, personal growth, and wisdom take time to develop and cannot be achieved quickly (1m). Just as fishing requires patience, life's most meaningful achievements — like the bond between grandfather and grandchild — grow slowly through consistent effort and presence (1m)."}]},{"id":"comp17","title":"The Group Project","diff":4,"wordCount":190,"passage":"We were assigned a group project on Singapore's biodiversity. I was grouped with three classmates: Mei Ling, who was hardworking; Ravi, who was creative; and Jason, who did nothing. While Mei Ling researched and I compiled the data, Jason claimed he was \"too busy\" with CCA. The deadline approached and his slides were still empty. Mei Ling wanted to report him. I suggested we talk to him first. When we did, Jason broke down. His parents were going through a divorce and he could barely concentrate on anything. We divided his portion among ourselves and told the teacher only that \"everyone contributed.\" Jason never forgot our kindness. The following term, when I was hospitalised with dengue, Jason visited every day and brought all my missed homework with detailed notes.","questions":[{"q":"What was Jason's reason for not contributing to the project?","type":"literal","marks":1,"model":"His parents were going through a divorce and he could barely concentrate on anything (1m)."},{"q":"Why did the narrator suggest talking to Jason first instead of reporting him?","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"The narrator showed empathy by wanting to understand Jason's situation before judging him (1m). Rather than assuming Jason was lazy, the narrator gave him a chance to explain, which revealed that Jason was going through a difficult personal crisis (1m)."},{"q":"What does Jason's behaviour in the following term show about the impact of kindness?","type":"evaluative","marks":2,"model":"It shows that kindness creates lasting bonds and inspires people to pay it forward (1m). Because the group showed compassion during Jason's difficult time, he felt genuine gratitude and willingly went out of his way to support the narrator when they were in need (1m)."}]},{"id":"comp18","title":"Digital Detox","diff":4,"wordCount":180,"passage":"Last month, our family tried a \"digital detox weekend\" — no phones, tablets, or computers from Friday evening to Sunday night. The first few hours were agony. I reached for my phone at least twenty times before remembering it was locked in a drawer. By Saturday morning, something shifted. We played board games, cooked together, and took a long walk at MacRitchie Reservoir. I noticed details I had never seen before: the patterns on tree bark, the sound of water flowing over rocks. My younger brother, usually glued to his iPad, built an elaborate fort out of cardboard boxes. On Sunday night, when we finally unlocked our devices, I had forty-seven notifications. None of them seemed important anymore.","questions":[{"q":"How long did the digital detox last?","type":"literal","marks":1,"model":"The digital detox lasted from Friday evening to Sunday night — one weekend (1m)."},{"q":"What does the narrator mean by \"something shifted\" on Saturday morning?","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"It means the narrator stopped feeling anxious about not having their phone and began to enjoy being present in the moment (1m). The discomfort of disconnection was replaced by an appreciation for real-world activities and family interaction (1m)."},{"q":"What is the significance of the last sentence: \"None of them seemed important anymore\"?","type":"evaluative","marks":2,"model":"It shows that the narrator gained perspective — what felt urgent and important digitally (notifications, messages) lost its significance after experiencing meaningful real-world connections (1m). This suggests that much of our phone usage is habit rather than genuine need (1m)."}]},{"id":"comp19","title":"The Dengue Crisis","diff":5,"wordCount":200,"passage":"In 2022, Singapore recorded over 32,000 dengue cases — the highest in its history. The Aedes mosquito, which thrives in tropical climates, breeds in stagnant water as shallow as a five-cent coin. Despite regular NEA inspections and heavy fines for breeding, the virus continues to surge. Scientists point to two factors: rising temperatures that accelerate mosquito reproduction, and urbanisation that creates countless hidden breeding spots in air-conditioning trays, roof gutters, and ornamental plants. Project Wolbachia, which releases male mosquitoes infected with bacteria that prevent reproduction, has shown promise in trial areas. However, Dr Tan from NUS warns: \"Technology alone cannot solve this. Every resident must check their home weekly. One careless household can undo the efforts of an entire neighbourhood.\"","questions":[{"q":"How many dengue cases were recorded in Singapore in 2022?","type":"literal","marks":1,"model":"Over 32,000 dengue cases were recorded (1m)."},{"q":"Why is urbanisation making the dengue problem worse?","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"Urbanisation creates many hidden spots where water can collect and stagnate — such as air-conditioning trays, roof gutters, and ornamental plants (1m). These are places that are difficult to inspect regularly and provide ideal breeding grounds for Aedes mosquitoes in dense residential areas (1m)."},{"q":"Do you agree with Dr Tan that \"one careless household can undo the efforts of an entire neighbourhood\"? Explain.","type":"evaluative","marks":2,"model":"Yes, because Aedes mosquitoes can breed in stagnant water as shallow as a five-cent coin, so even one careless household can keep producing mosquitoes that fly to neighbouring homes (1m). This means that community-wide efforts such as Wolbachia releases and weekly checks are undermined if even one household does not take part (1m)."}]},{"id":"comp20","title":"The Art Competition","diff":3,"wordCount":170,"passage":"I spent three weeks on my painting for the National Art Competition — a watercolour of the Singapore River at sunset. I was certain I would win. On results day, my name was not on the winners' list. Instead, first prize went to a simple charcoal sketch of an old woman selling tissue paper at a hawker centre. I was furious. My painting had more technique, more colour, more detail. Then my art teacher said something I have never forgotten: \"Art is not about showing what you can do. It is about making people feel something.\" Looking at the winning piece again, I understood. The sketch captured loneliness, dignity, and the reality of Singapore's elderly in a way my pretty sunset never could. That day, I stopped painting to impress and started painting to connect.","questions":[{"q":"What did the narrator paint for the competition?","type":"literal","marks":1,"model":"The narrator painted a watercolour of the Singapore River at sunset (1m)."},{"q":"Why did the simple charcoal sketch win over the narrator's detailed painting?","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"The sketch won because it conveyed genuine emotion — loneliness and dignity of an elderly tissue seller — which resonated with viewers (1m). While the narrator's painting showed technical skill, it lacked the emotional depth and social meaning that makes art truly powerful (1m)."},{"q":"What lesson did the narrator learn about art (and life)?","type":"evaluative","marks":2,"model":"The narrator learned that the purpose of art is not to display technical skill or impress others, but to create genuine human connection and evoke emotions (1m). This applies to life too — meaningful work comes from authenticity and empathy, not from showing off abilities (1m)."}]},{"id":"comp21","title":"The Bus Ride Home","diff":4,"wordCount":366,"passage":"Every weekday at half past one, Ravi waited at the bus stop outside his school for service 174. The ride home took twenty-two minutes if the traffic behaved, and he had counted the stops so many times that he no longer needed to look up from his book. That Tuesday, however, the rain came down in grey sheets, and the queue under the shelter grew longer and more impatient by the minute.\n\nWhen the bus finally arrived, an elderly man climbed on slowly ahead of Ravi. He patted one pocket, then another, then a third. His card was not there. Behind him, somebody sighed loudly. The driver tapped his fingers on the wheel and said, without turning his head, that the bus could not wait.\n\nRavi's own card had exactly four dollars and thirty cents on it, enough to get him to school and back for two more days, and his mother would not top it up until Friday. He knew this because he had checked the balance that morning. He stared at the card in his hand for what felt like a very long time. Then he stepped forward and tapped it twice.\n\nThe old man insisted on sitting beside him. His name was Mr Fong, he said, and he took this bus every single day to the hospital in Novena, where his wife had been for eleven weeks. He described the small window beside her bed and the way she still asked, every afternoon, whether he had eaten. He talked for eighteen minutes. Ravi did not read a single page of his book.\n\nAt the last assembly of the year, the principal held up a letter. It had been posted to the school by a Mr Fong, who had remembered only a name tag and a blue-striped uniform. The hall clapped. Ravi's ears burned. Walking back to class, he could not explain to his friends why the clapping had made him feel smaller rather than taller. He had hesitated on that bus, and he knew it. Besides, he thought, a boy who spends a dollar is not the brave one in that story. The brave one had been riding service 174 for seventy-seven days.","questions":[{"q":"How much value was left on Ravi's card that Tuesday, and why could he not simply add more money to it?","type":"literal","marks":2,"model":"There was exactly four dollars and thirty cents on the card (1m). He could not add more because his mother would not top it up until Friday (1m). 陷阱: 一题两问, 只写金额就收笔丢一半; \"and why\" 后面那半在同一句的后段(妈妈要到周五才充), 必须一起写。"},{"q":"The writer says \"the rain came down in grey sheets\". What does this tell you about the rain? Answer in your own words.","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"It tells us the rain was extremely heavy (1m). Instead of falling as separate drops, it came down in thick, unbroken curtains of water that were difficult to see through (1m). 陷阱: 题目写明 in your own words, 把 \"grey sheets\" 抄回去零分; 必须换成 heavy / thick / hard to see through 这类自己的说法。"},{"q":"Explain fully why the clapping at assembly made Ravi \"feel smaller rather than taller\". Give three reasons.","type":"inferential","marks":3,"model":"He remembered that he had hesitated before helping, so he did not feel he deserved to be called kind (1m). What he had given up was one tap of a card, while Mr Fong had travelled to the hospital for seventy-seven days, which Ravi thought was the braver act (1m). His ears burned and he could not explain himself to his friends, which shows that being praised in front of the whole hall for something he saw as small made him embarrassed rather than proud (1m)."},{"q":"How was Mr Fong able to find out where to send his letter?","type":"literal","marks":2,"model":"He had remembered the name tag on Ravi's uniform, which gave him Ravi's name (1m). He had also remembered the blue-striped uniform itself, which told him which school Ravi attended (1m). 陷阱: 两分要两个不同线索(名牌=名字, 蓝条纹校服=哪所学校), 只写\"他记得校服\"算一个点。"},{"q":"What does the detail that Ravi \"did not read a single page of his book\" show about him?","type":"inferential","marks":3,"model":"It shows that Mr Fong's story had captured his full attention (1m). Reading on the bus was Ravi's fixed daily habit, since he had counted the stops so often that he never needed to look up, so breaking it was very unusual for him (1m). It also suggests he had stopped seeing Mr Fong as a stranger he had helped and had begun to care about him as a person (1m). 陷阱: 只写\"他在听老人说话\"只能拿一分。第二个点要回到第一段的\"看书是他每天的习惯\", 第三个点是态度的转变, 三个点是三个维度。"},{"q":"Ravi thinks that \"a boy who spends a dollar is not the brave one in that story\". Do you agree with him? Give reasons for your answer.","type":"evaluative","marks":3,"model":"I agree, because Mr Fong made the same tiring journey for seventy-seven days without any praise, and keeping that up takes far more determination than a single act (1m). Ravi's help cost him one tap of a card, while Mr Fong gave up his time and energy every single day (1m). Even so, Ravi still deserves some credit, because he gave away money he genuinely could not spare, which shows real generosity even if it was not bravery (1m). 陷阱: 评价题不是只写 \"Yes, I agree\" 就完事。三分要三层: 支持的理由、比较两人付出的代价、再补一句让步或补充, 单写一句结论只拿一分。"}]},{"id":"comp22","title":"Ah Ma's Stall","diff":4,"wordCount":377,"passage":"The school holidays had barely begun when my mother announced that I would be spending them at Ah Ma's noodle stall in the hawker centre at Block 505. I protested. My friends were going to the pool, the stall was hot, and nobody my age wanted to smell of pork bone soup for a month.\n\nThe first morning, we arrived at half past four. I had never seen the estate so quiet. Ah Ma unlocked the metal shutter, switched on a single yellow bulb and set an enormous stockpot on the fire before she said a word to me. My job, she explained, was the bean sprouts: rinse, pick, drain, three times over. By six o'clock my back ached. By seven, the first customers had arrived, and I had not yet had breakfast.\n\nWhat surprised me most was that Ah Ma never once looked at the queue. She looked only at the bowl in front of her. Noodles, soup, three slices of pork, a pinch of spring onion, and always, always, a small extra ladle of soup on the side for the uncle in the wheelchair who came at eight. She did not charge him for it. When I asked why, she said that he had eaten at her stall since the year my mother was born, and that some things are not on the price list.\n\nHalfway through the holidays, a food blogger posted a photograph of our stall online. The queue on Saturday stretched past the drinks stall and around the corner. I was thrilled. Ah Ma was not. She sold out by half past ten, closed the shutter and sat down heavily on an upturned crate. When the uncle in the wheelchair arrived at eleven, there was nothing left for him.\n\nThe next Saturday, Ah Ma put one bowl aside before she opened. It sat covered on the back shelf, untouched, while dozens of strangers queued outside for a taste of the stall they had seen on their phones. I understood then that Ah Ma had never been running a business the way I imagined a business worked. She was keeping a promise she had never actually spoken aloud, to people whose names she knew, and she had been keeping it for thirty years.","questions":[{"q":"Give two reasons why the writer did not want to spend the holidays at his grandmother's stall.","type":"literal","marks":2,"model":"His friends were going to the pool, so he would miss out on what they were doing (1m). The stall itself was hot, and he did not want to smell of pork bone soup for a whole month (1m). 陷阱: 第一段一口气列了三样(朋友去游泳/很热/一身汤味), 题目要 two reasons, 只写一条丢一半。"},{"q":"\"I was thrilled. Ah Ma was not.\" What does the word \"thrilled\" tell you about the writer's reaction, and how was Ah Ma's reaction different? Use your own words.","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"\"Thrilled\" shows that the writer was extremely excited and delighted, because he saw the long queue as proof that the stall had become a success (1m). Ah Ma felt the opposite: she was worn out and unhappy, sitting down heavily on a crate after selling out far too early to serve her regular customer (1m). 陷阱: 一题两半(他的反应+她的反应), 只解释 thrilled 丢一分; 而且要求 use your own words, 直接抄 \"Ah Ma was not\" 不算答案。"},{"q":"Explain fully why Ah Ma was not pleased that the blogger's photograph had brought so many new customers.","type":"inferential","marks":3,"model":"She sold out by half past ten and had to close the shutter, so she could no longer serve customers for the rest of the day as she normally did (1m). The uncle in the wheelchair, who had eaten there since the year the writer's mother was born, arrived at eleven and found nothing left, which meant the crowd of strangers had pushed out her regulars (1m). She had never measured her work by the length of the queue in the first place, since she looked only at the bowl in front of her, so a bigger crowd was never what she wanted (1m). 陷阱: 三个点分散在第三段(她从不看队伍/轮椅叔叔的来历)和第四段(十点半卖完/十一点没得吃), 只在第四段找答案最多两分。这题就是典型\"答案跨两段\"。"},{"q":"What did Ah Ma do differently on the following Saturday, and why?","type":"literal","marks":2,"model":"Before she opened, she set one bowl aside and left it covered on the back shelf (1m). She did this so that the uncle in the wheelchair would still get his meal even if the stall sold out early again (1m). 陷阱: 只写\"她留了一碗\"是做法, 没写\"为了给轮椅叔叔留着\"这个原因, 就丢掉第二分。"},{"q":"Ah Ma said that \"some things are not on the price list\". In your own words, explain what she meant.","type":"inferential","marks":3,"model":"She meant that not everything she gives her customers can be counted in money (1m). The extra ladle of soup was a gesture of care and loyalty rather than an item to be paid for (1m). Their long relationship mattered more to her than what a bowl of noodles was worth, since he had eaten at her stall since the year the writer's mother was born (1m). 陷阱: 要求 in your own words, 把 \"not on the price list\" 抄一遍零分; 而且三分要三个不同角度(不能用钱算 / 那勺汤是心意 / 几十年的交情), 不是把同一句话换三种说法。"},{"q":"Do you think Ah Ma made the right decision to keep one bowl aside instead of selling it to a new customer? Give reasons.","type":"evaluative","marks":3,"model":"Yes, because the uncle in the wheelchair depends on her stall and cannot easily go elsewhere, so that one bowl means far more to him than to a passing stranger (1m). Keeping it also protects the trust she has built over thirty years, which will last much longer than a few weeks of online popularity (1m). Some might argue that she lost money by refusing a paying customer, but she has never treated the stall as only a business, so the decision matches what she has always valued (1m). 陷阱: 评价题要\"立场+理由+反方回应\"三层。只写 \"Yes, because she is kind\" 是一个点; 少了\"反对的人会说她少赚钱\"这一层, 三分题拿不满。"}]},{"id":"comp23","title":"The Blue Bin Problem","diff":4,"wordCount":364,"passage":"Look under almost any HDB block in Singapore and you will find one: a large blue bin with a rounded lid, meant for paper, plastic, metal and glass. There are more than twenty-two thousand of them across the island. On paper, the system is simple. In practice, it is not working as well as it should.\n\nThe National Environment Agency reports that about forty out of every hundred items placed in blue bins cannot be recycled at all. The most common problem is not that residents are lazy. It is that they are hopeful. Faced with an object they are unsure about, many people drop it into the blue bin anyway, guessing that someone at the sorting facility will work it out. Recyclers call this \"wish-cycling\".\n\nThe results are messy. A half-finished cup of bubble tea, thrown in with the plastic, leaks over the paper beneath it. Wet paper cannot be turned into new paper, so the whole load must be thrown away and burnt instead. One dirty item can therefore spoil the work of a hundred careful neighbours.\n\nSome items surprise people. Pizza boxes stained with oil are not recyclable. Neither are used tissues, disposable chopsticks, or plastic bags containing food waste. Styrofoam boxes, which many hawker centres still use, cannot go into the blue bin either. On the other hand, items that people often throw away, such as clean aluminium drink cans, glass jars with the lids removed, and empty shampoo bottles, are all perfectly recyclable once they have been rinsed.\n\n\"Rinse it, empty it, and if you truly do not know, leave it out,\" says Madam Serene Loh, who runs recycling workshops for residents' committees in Ang Mo Kio. \"People think the kind thing is to give the bin the benefit of the doubt. Actually, the kind thing is to be strict.\"\n\nSeveral towns have begun placing clear pictures on the bin lids instead of long lists of words, and early results suggest that contamination falls when residents can see, rather than read, what belongs inside. It is a small change. But with twenty-two thousand bins and five and a half million people, small changes add up quickly, in either direction.","questions":[{"q":"How many blue bins are there in Singapore, and what proportion of the items placed in them cannot be recycled?","type":"literal","marks":2,"model":"There are more than twenty-two thousand blue bins across the island (1m). About forty out of every hundred items placed in them cannot be recycled at all (1m). 陷阱: 两个数字在两个不同段落(第一段和第二段), 只答一个丢一半; 很多人读到第一段的数字就停笔了。"},{"q":"Recyclers use the word \"wish-cycling\". Explain in your own words what this means.","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"It means putting something into the recycling bin while only hoping, rather than knowing, that it can be recycled (1m). People do this when they are unsure about an object and assume that somebody at the sorting facility will decide for them (1m). 陷阱: 要求 in your own words, 把 \"wish-cycling\" 三个字抄回去零分; 两分要两层(只是\"希望\"不是\"知道\" + 把判断推给别人)。"},{"q":"Madam Loh says that \"the kind thing is to be strict\". Using information from the whole passage, explain fully why being strict is actually the kinder choice.","type":"inferential","marks":3,"model":"Dropping in a doubtful item feels generous, but it simply passes the problem on to the workers at the sorting facility instead of solving it (1m). A single dirty item, such as a leaking cup of bubble tea, can soak the paper below it so that the entire load has to be burnt, wasting the careful sorting done by a hundred neighbours (1m). Leaving out an item you are unsure about therefore protects everyone else's effort, which means the strict resident is helping the community rather than judging it (1m). 陷阱: 题目明说 \"using information from the whole passage\" —— 三个点分别在第二段(wish-cycling)、第三段(一杯饮料毁一整车)和第五段(她自己的话), 只引用她那句话最多拿一分。"},{"q":"Name two items that may NOT be placed in a blue bin, and two items that may.","type":"literal","marks":2,"model":"Two that may NOT go in, from: oily pizza boxes, used tissues, disposable chopsticks, plastic bags containing food waste, styrofoam boxes (1m). Two that may go in, from: clean aluminium drink cans, glass jars with the lids removed, empty shampoo bottles, all of which must first be rinsed (1m). 陷阱: 一题两半, 只写\"不能放的\"丢一分。可回收那一组藏在第四段 \"On the other hand\" 之后, 读到 \"Some items surprise people\" 就停笔的人一定丢分。"},{"q":"Why have some towns started to use pictures on the bin lids instead of written lists?","type":"inferential","marks":3,"model":"A picture can be understood in a single glance, so a resident does not have to stop and read a long list before throwing something away (1m). The passage shows that people drop doubtful items in because they are hopeful rather than lazy, so a clear picture removes the guessing that causes wish-cycling in the first place (1m). Early results show that contamination actually falls when residents can see, rather than read, what belongs inside, so the change works in practice and not only in theory (1m)."},{"q":"The writer ends by saying that small changes \"add up quickly, in either direction\". What does the writer want readers to understand, and do you agree?","type":"evaluative","marks":3,"model":"The writer means that with twenty-two thousand bins and five and a half million people, tiny individual habits multiply into a very large national result (1m). The phrase \"in either direction\" is a warning that carelessness spreads just as fast as good habits, so a few lazy households in every block would be enough to ruin the scheme (1m). I agree, because the passage shows that one leaking cup can destroy a whole load, which proves the outcome depends on ordinary daily choices rather than on better machines (1m). 陷阱: 最容易丢的是 \"in either direction\" 这半句 —— 它是\"好习惯和坏习惯都会放大\", 只写\"积少成多\"等于漏掉一半题意。而且题目还要 do you agree, 不表态就再丢一分。"}]},{"id":"comp24","title":"The Missing Water Bottle","diff":4,"wordCount":392,"passage":"My water bottle was the only thing I owned that nobody else in Primary Five had. It was dark green, dented near the base, and my father had brought it back from Japan the year before he started working overseas. On Wednesday afternoon it was not in my bag.\n\nI searched the classroom twice. Then I remembered that Wei Han had picked it up at recess to look at the sticker on the side, and that he had been the last one out of the room. Wei Han had transferred to our school in March. He kept his books in a supermarket plastic bag because his file had broken, and he never bought anything at the canteen except plain rice. By the time the bell rang for the next lesson, I had told four people what I thought had happened. By Thursday morning, the whole class had heard.\n\nWei Han did not deny it and he did not argue. He simply stopped sitting at our table. For three days he ate alone on the steps outside the hall, and every time I passed him I felt a small twist in my stomach that I chose to ignore.\n\nOn Friday, the cleaner, Auntie Rosnah, came to our classroom holding a dark green bottle. She had found it behind the recycling corner in the corridor, where it must have rolled after falling out of my bag. She had washed it. She was smiling, pleased to have solved a small mystery, and she did not understand why the room went so quiet.\n\nSaying sorry, I discovered, is much harder than being sorry. I had imagined that I would explain, and that Wei Han would nod, and that everything would return to how it had been on Tuesday. Instead he listened, said \"okay\", and went back to his book. He was not angry. That was the part I had not prepared for. He had simply expected it, expected that when something went missing, the new boy with the plastic bag would be the one people looked at.\n\nI still use that bottle. The dent near the base has not changed. But I no longer think of it as the thing my father gave me. I think of it as the thing that showed me what I was willing to believe about somebody I did not know.","questions":[{"q":"Where was the bottle finally found, and how had it got there?","type":"literal","marks":2,"model":"Auntie Rosnah found it behind the recycling corner in the corridor (1m). It had fallen out of the writer's own bag and rolled there (1m). 陷阱: 两问一题, 只答地点丢一半; \"how had it got there\" 是第二个采分点, 而且要点明是从他自己的书包掉出来的。"},{"q":"Explain fully why the writer suspected Wei Han rather than anybody else.","type":"inferential","marks":3,"model":"Wei Han had picked the bottle up at recess to look at the sticker, and he had been the last one to leave the classroom (1m). He was new, having transferred to the school only in March, so the writer did not know him well enough to trust him (1m). He was visibly poor, keeping his books in a supermarket plastic bag and buying only plain rice, and the writer assumed that a boy who had little would be the one to take something, which is exactly what Wei Han himself had come to expect (1m). 陷阱: 前两个点在第二段, 第三个点要把第二段的\"塑料袋/白饭\"和第五段 Wei Han 早就料到的那句连起来读。只写\"因为他最后一个离开教室\"是一分题的答法。"},{"q":"The writer felt \"a small twist in my stomach that I chose to ignore\". In your own words, explain what this tells us about how he felt.","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"He felt a sharp, uncomfortable pang of guilt each time he walked past Wei Han sitting alone (1m). The words \"chose to ignore\" show that he already suspected he might be wrong but deliberately pushed the feeling away instead of doing anything about it (1m). 陷阱: 要求 in your own words, 抄 \"a small twist in my stomach\" 不给分。第二分在 \"chose to ignore\" 上 —— 是\"明知道却故意不理\", 不是\"没注意到\"。"},{"q":"How did Wei Han behave during the three days after he was accused?","type":"literal","marks":2,"model":"He neither denied the accusation nor argued about it (1m). He stopped sitting at the writer's table and ate alone on the steps outside the hall for three days (1m). 陷阱: 两分是两个不同行为(不辩解 + 独自吃饭), 只写\"他一个人吃饭\"算一个点。"},{"q":"Why was Wei Han's calm reaction \"the part I had not prepared for\"?","type":"inferential","marks":3,"model":"The writer had expected anger or an argument, which he could have answered with an explanation and an apology (1m). Instead Wei Han simply said \"okay\" and returned to his book, showing that he was not surprised at all by what had happened (1m). That was worse for the writer, because it meant Wei Han had already learnt to expect to be blamed, so the unfairness was normal to him rather than shocking (1m). 陷阱: 三分题的第三个点最容易漏 —— 不是\"他很平静\", 而是\"平静说明他早就习惯被冤枉\", 这才是作者难受的原因。少了这层只能拿两分。"},{"q":"Do you think the writer has learnt the right lesson from what happened? Explain your answer.","type":"evaluative","marks":3,"model":"Yes, because he no longer sees the bottle as his father's gift but as a reminder of \"what I was willing to believe about somebody I did not know\", which shows he blames his own assumptions rather than bad luck (1m). Choosing to keep using the bottle rather than hiding it suggests that he wants to be reminded, which is a sign of real change rather than a quick apology (1m). However, the lesson is not complete, because he apologised in private but did nothing to correct the story he had spread to the whole class (1m). 陷阱: 只写 \"Yes, he learnt his lesson\" 加一句理由是一分。三分要包含\"他怎么证明自己变了\"和\"哪里还没做够\"两个方向, 一面倒地夸他反而拿不满。"}]},{"id":"comp25","title":"The Night Before the Race","diff":5,"wordCount":424,"passage":"For two years I had run the third leg. The third leg is the one nobody watches. On the Tuesday before Sports Day, Coach Lim read out the relay order in the corridor, and my name was at the end of it. Anchor. I read the list four times to be certain.\n\nDanial had run anchor since Primary Three. He was faster than me over the last twenty metres and both of us knew it. When Coach Lim read out the order, Danial said nothing at all, picked up his bag and left before the rest of us had finished changing.\n\nI found out why on Thursday, and not from him. Coach Lim had dropped Danial for turning up late to training three weeks in a row. What Coach Lim did not know, and what none of us knew, was that Danial's mother had started working the night shift at the airport in April, and that Danial now collected his younger sister from the childcare centre at Block 118 every evening before he could come to the field. He had never mentioned it. When I asked him about it at the bus stop, he shrugged and said that it was not the coach's problem.\n\nThat night I did not sleep well. I had wanted the anchor leg since Primary Three. It had arrived, and it had arrived for the wrong reason, and I was the only person who could say so. I told myself that Danial should have explained it himself. I told myself that a lot of times.\n\nOn Friday morning I knocked on the staff room door before the first bell. I told Coach Lim about the night shifts and the childcare centre and Block 118. He listened without writing anything down, then thanked me and said he would speak to Danial. He did not tell me what he had decided.\n\nAt the starting line on Saturday I was back on the third leg. Danial took the baton from me with eleven metres to make up, and he did not make up eleven metres. We finished second, the medal was silver, and my mother took a photograph of the four of us that I still have.\n\nPeople assume the story ends with me being noble. It does not. I was angry for a week. What changed was slower than that. Somewhere between Saturday and the end of the term, I stopped measuring the race by which leg I ran, and started measuring it by whether the four of us were still four.","questions":[{"q":"Why had Coach Lim dropped Danial from the anchor leg, and what was the real reason behind Danial's behaviour?","type":"literal","marks":2,"model":"Coach Lim dropped him because he had turned up late to training three weeks in a row (1m). The real reason for the lateness was that Danial had to collect his younger sister from the childcare centre at Block 118 every evening, since his mother had begun working the night shift at the airport in April (1m). 陷阱: \"迟到\"只是老师看到的表面原因, 真正原因在同一段后半句。只写迟到丢一半, 而且真正原因要写全(妈妈上夜班 + 他要接妹妹)。"},{"q":"The writer says the anchor leg \"had arrived for the wrong reason\". What does he mean by \"the wrong reason\"? Answer in your own words.","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"He means that the place had come to him not because he had run faster or improved in any way, but only because Danial had been removed as a punishment (1m). He calls the reason \"wrong\" because the punishment itself was based on a mistake: Danial's lateness came from having to fetch his little sister, not from carelessness (1m). 陷阱: 要求 in your own words, 抄 \"for the wrong reason\" 零分。两分是两层: 他不是靠实力得到的 + 那个处罚本身就是冤枉的, 只写\"他觉得不公平\"太笼统, 拿一分。"},{"q":"Explain fully why the writer \"did not sleep well\" on Thursday night.","type":"inferential","marks":3,"model":"He had wanted the anchor leg since Primary Three and had waited two years for it, so speaking up would mean giving up something he badly wanted (1m). He knew the place had come to him \"for the wrong reason\", so keeping it quietly would feel dishonest (1m). He also realised that he was the only person who could tell Coach Lim the truth, which meant that staying silent would be a deliberate choice of his own, not an accident (1m). 陷阱: 三个点分别在第一段(等了两年)和第四段(来路不正 / 只有他能说), 只在第四段找答案容易漏掉\"这个位置是他盼了两年的\", 而那正是他最难取舍的地方。"},{"q":"Why do you think Coach Lim \"did not tell me what he had decided\"?","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"He may have wanted the writer to speak up for Danial without expecting anything in return, so that the act stayed honest rather than becoming a bargain (1m). It also shows that the decision about the team was the coach's own responsibility, and not something a pupil had the right to negotiate over (1m). 陷阱: 这题问 \"why do you think\", 是推断不是找句子。只写\"因为他还没决定\"不给分, 要写出教练这样做背后的两层用意。"},{"q":"\"People assume the story ends with me being noble. It does not.\" Explain what the writer means and why he says this.","type":"inferential","marks":3,"model":"He means that doing the right thing did not immediately make him feel proud or satisfied (1m). He admits that he was angry for a week afterwards, which shows that losing the anchor leg genuinely hurt and that his good deed did not remove the disappointment (1m). He says it in order to correct the neat, heroic version of the story that others expect, insisting that real change in a person happens slowly rather than in one dramatic moment (1m). 陷阱: 只写\"他不觉得自己高尚\"是一个点。另外两个点是\"他生了一个星期的气\"这个证据, 和\"他为什么要特地澄清\", 三分题必须三层都写。"},{"q":"Do you think the writer was right to tell Coach Lim about Danial's situation, even though Danial had chosen not to? Give reasons.","type":"evaluative","marks":3,"model":"Yes, because Danial was being punished for something that was not laziness, and only the coach had the power to correct that unfairness (1m). The writer also knew that his own place had come to him \"for the wrong reason\", so staying silent would have meant benefiting from a mistake that he alone could fix (1m). On the other hand, Danial had deliberately kept his family situation private, so sharing it without asking took away his choice, and the writer could first have urged Danial to speak for himself (1m). 陷阱: 这题一定要给反方一层。只写\"对, 因为这样才公平\"最多两分, 少了\"但那是 Danial 的隐私, 他没有权利替他说\"就丢掉第三分。"}]},{"id":"comp26","title":"Eleven Kites","diff":5,"wordCount":423,"passage":"My grandfather made kites out of newspaper, bamboo skewers and rice glue, and he made them badly. The frames were crooked. The tails were too heavy. Every Sunday for six years he brought one down to the field beside our block, and every Sunday it climbed about two metres, turned over and came down in the grass.\n\nI was seven when I asked him why he did not simply buy one from the shop at the mall. There were kites there shaped like eagles, with plastic frames that never snapped. He said that a bought kite tells you nothing. Then he handed me the roll of string and told me to run.\n\nBy the time I was ten I had worked out the problem. The tails were the wrong length. I measured them, cut them, weighed them against fifty-cent coins and wrote the results in the back of my maths exercise book. On the fourth Sunday of that experiment, the kite went up, properly up, past the fifth storey, past the ninth, until the string pulled hard enough to hurt my hand. My grandfather did not say anything clever. He stood with his head back and his mouth slightly open, and he watched it for a very long time.\n\nHe passed away in the September of my Primary Five year. My mother packed his flat in two days because the family needed to return the keys. In a cupboard behind a stack of old calendars she found eleven kites, all finished, all unflown, and all with tails exactly the length I had written in my exercise book.\n\nThat was when I understood what he had been doing on those six years of Sundays. He had never been trying to fly a kite. He had been waiting for me to fix one.\n\nWe flew one of the eleven the following Sunday, my mother and I, on the same field. It flew beautifully, which I had expected, and it hurt, which I had not. I have kept the other ten in their newspaper wrapping. My mother asks occasionally whether I intend to fly them. I tell her that I will, one at a time, and that there is no hurry.\n\nI am thirteen now and I have never once bought a kite from the shop at the mall. My grandfather was right, though not in the way he meant it. A bought kite tells you nothing. A badly made one, brought back to the same field every Sunday for six years, tells you almost everything.","questions":[{"q":"What materials did the grandfather use to make his kites, and what was wrong with them?","type":"literal","marks":2,"model":"He used newspaper, bamboo skewers and rice glue (1m). The frames were crooked and the tails were too heavy, so the kites rose only about two metres before turning over (1m). 陷阱: 两问一题。材料要写齐三样, 缺点也要写出来才拿第二分, 只写\"他做得很差\"太笼统。"},{"q":"\"He stood with his head back and his mouth slightly open, and he watched it for a very long time.\" Explain in your own words what this description shows about the grandfather's feelings.","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"It shows that he was filled with wonder and quiet delight at seeing the kite finally fly (1m). Because the writer describes his body rather than his words, it suggests his feelings ran too deep to put into speech, and that his pride was in his grandson rather than in the kite (1m). 陷阱: 要求 in your own words, 把动作描写抄一遍不给分。第二分要读出\"他说不出话\"背后的意思 —— 骄傲的是孙子, 不是风筝。"},{"q":"Explain fully how the writer came to realise that his grandfather \"had never been trying to fly a kite\".","type":"inferential","marks":3,"model":"After his grandfather died, eleven finished but unflown kites were found hidden in a cupboard behind a stack of old calendars, which showed that he had been able to make kites that worked yet had chosen never to fly them (1m). Every one of those kites had a tail exactly the length the writer had worked out and recorded in the back of his maths exercise book, so his grandfather must have read the results and copied them (1m). His grandfather had also refused to buy a ready-made kite because \"a bought kite tells you nothing\", which shows the failures were deliberate and were meant to leave a problem for the writer to solve (1m)."},{"q":"The writer keeps ten kites unflown and tells his mother \"that there is no hurry\". Explain in your own words what he means by \"no hurry\".","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"He means that he does not want to use up the ten remaining kites quickly, so he is deliberately spacing them out (1m). Each flight is a way of spending more time with his grandfather's memory, so making them last keeps the connection between them going instead of bringing it to an end (1m). 陷阱: 要求 in your own words, 写 \"he is not in a hurry\" 等于没答。第二分要说出为什么慢慢飞 —— 飞完就真的没有了, 只写\"他很珍惜\"太笼统。"},{"q":"The writer says the kite \"flew beautifully, which I had expected, and it hurt, which I had not\". Why did it hurt?","type":"inferential","marks":3,"model":"Seeing the kite succeed proved that his grandfather had known how to make it work all along, so the six years of failure had been a gift that the writer only understood after it was too late to thank him (1m). The moment they had been building towards for six years finally arrived, but his grandfather was not there to see it (1m). It also made the loss real, because completing the flight meant that the project, and their Sundays together, were now over (1m). 陷阱: 只写\"因为爷爷去世了\"是一个点。三分题要写出三种不同的痛: 明白得太晚 / 他看不到 / 从此没有下一个星期天。同一个意思换三种说法不给三分。"},{"q":"Do you agree with the writer that a badly made kite can tell you \"almost everything\"? Give reasons.","type":"evaluative","marks":3,"model":"Yes, because the badly made kite left a problem that the writer had to solve himself, teaching him to measure, test and record rather than simply to buy something that already worked (1m). The repeated Sundays also gave the two of them six years of shared time, so the kite's real value lay in the habit it created rather than in whether it flew (1m). A shop-bought kite would have flown on the first day and been forgotten, so it was the failure, not the success, that made the memory last (1m). 陷阱: 这题不能只夸风筝。三分是三个不同好处: 学会解决问题 / 六年的相处 / 失败才让人记住。写成\"因为爷爷很爱他\"三句话都在讲同一件事, 只算一分。"}]},{"id":"comp27","title":"Why Singapore Keeps Planting Trees","diff":5,"wordCount":411,"passage":"On a hot afternoon, walk from a bare car park to a tree-lined pavement and you will feel the difference within seconds. Measured with an instrument, that difference is often four to five degrees Celsius. Multiply it across a whole island and you begin to understand why Singapore has spent sixty years planting.\n\nCities are hotter than the countryside around them, and the reason is mostly concrete. Buildings and roads absorb heat during the day and release it slowly through the night, so a city never fully cools down. Scientists call this the urban heat island effect. In Singapore, night-time temperatures in the most built-up districts can be up to seven degrees higher than in the least built-up ones, a gap that has widened as the city has grown.\n\nTrees work against this in two separate ways, and most people remember only the first. The obvious one is shade: leaves block sunlight before it reaches the pavement. The second is quieter. Trees draw water up from their roots and release it through their leaves as vapour, and turning water into vapour uses up heat. A single mature rain tree can move hundreds of litres of water in a day. In effect, the tree is running an air conditioner that costs nothing and makes no noise.\n\nThere are limits. A newly planted sapling provides almost no shade for its first decade, which means the benefit of today's planting will be felt by the children of today's residents rather than by the residents themselves. Trees also need soil, and in a dense city soil competes with drains, cables and car parks. \"The hardest part of my job is not planting,\" says Mr Ganesh Kumar, who has worked with trees for more than twenty years. \"It is arguing for the space underground that nobody can see.\"\n\nSingapore's response has been to stop treating greenery as decoration added at the end of a project. Under newer planning rules, developers must replace the greenery their building covers, often by putting it on roofs, walls and sky terraces. The target is no longer a garden city but a \"city in nature\", a phrase that reverses the order deliberately.\n\nWhether this is enough is still an open question. Temperatures continue to rise, and no amount of shade removes the need to burn less fuel. But on a hot afternoon, walking on the shaded side of the road, it is difficult to argue that the sixty years were wasted.","questions":[{"q":"How much cooler can a tree-lined pavement feel than a bare car park, and how much hotter can the most built-up districts be at night?","type":"literal","marks":2,"model":"A tree-lined pavement is often four to five degrees Celsius cooler (1m). At night, the most built-up districts can be up to seven degrees hotter than the least built-up ones (1m). 陷阱: 两个数字分别在第一段和第二段, 只答一个丢一半; 也不要把 4-5 度和 7 度混成同一个数字。"},{"q":"In your own words, explain the two ways in which trees cool a city, and say why the writer thinks one of them is often forgotten.","type":"inferential","marks":3,"model":"First, the leaves block the sunlight before it reaches the ground, so the pavement below stays in shade (1m). Second, trees pull water up from the soil and release it through their leaves as vapour, and changing water into vapour uses up heat, with a mature rain tree moving hundreds of litres in a single day (1m). The second way is forgotten because it is invisible and silent: shade can be seen and felt at once, while evaporation gives no obvious sign that it is happening (1m). 陷阱: 只写\"树可以遮阳\"直接丢两分。题目一句里藏了三个任务(第一种方式 / 第二种方式 / 为什么第二种被忽略), 三分就是三个任务, 少答一个就少一分。"},{"q":"Mr Kumar says the hardest part of his job is \"arguing for the space underground that nobody can see\". Using information from more than one paragraph, explain fully why this argument is so difficult to win.","type":"inferential","marks":3,"model":"In a dense city, soil under the ground has to compete with drains, cables and car parks, all of which have obvious and immediate uses (1m). A newly planted sapling also gives almost no shade for its first decade, so there is nothing visible to show for the space for many years (1m). On top of that, greenery has traditionally been treated as decoration added at the end of a project, so it is the first thing to be squeezed out whenever space runs short (1m). 陷阱: 题目明说 \"from more than one paragraph\" —— 前两个点在第四段, 第三个点在第五段。只在引语所在的那一段找答案, 最多拿两分。"},{"q":"Explain in your own words what is meant by \"the urban heat island effect\".","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"It means that a built-up city stays hotter than the countryside surrounding it (1m). This happens because concrete buildings and roads soak up heat all day and then give it out slowly through the night, so the city never gets a chance to cool down completely (1m). 陷阱: 把 \"urban heat island effect\" 这个名词本身抄一遍等于没答。要求 in your own words, 必须用自己的话说出两层: 城市比周边热 + 混凝土白天吸热夜里慢慢放热。"},{"q":"What is the new target described in the passage, and what must developers now do?","type":"literal","marks":2,"model":"The target is no longer a \"garden city\" but a \"city in nature\" (1m). Under the newer planning rules, developers must replace the greenery that their building covers, often by putting it on roofs, walls and sky terraces (1m). 陷阱: 两问一题, 只答目标名称丢一半; 开发商那半在同一段的前一句, 顺序是反的, 容易漏。"},{"q":"The writer admits that \"whether this is enough is still an open question\", yet ends by saying the sixty years were not wasted. Do you find this a convincing way to end? Explain.","type":"evaluative","marks":3,"model":"Yes, because the writer is honest about the limits, admitting that temperatures keep rising and that shade cannot replace burning less fuel, so the conclusion does not claim more than the evidence allows (1m). At the same time, the figures given earlier, such as the four-to-five-degree difference a walker can feel immediately, show that the planting has produced a real and measurable benefit (1m). Ending with the everyday experience of walking on the shaded side of the road also lets ordinary readers test the claim for themselves, which is more persuasive than another statistic (1m). 陷阱: 这题问的是\"这样收尾说不说服人\", 不是\"树好不好\"。只写\"我同意, 因为树很有用\"跑题, 三分要围绕\"承认局限 / 有数据支撑 / 用读者自己的体验收尾\"这三点写。"}]},{"id":"comp28","title":"Fourteen Floors","diff":5,"wordCount":398,"passage":"The notice went up on Monday morning, printed on orange paper and taped to the glass beside the letterboxes. The lift at Block 12 would be out of service for eleven days while the motor was replaced. My grandmother lives on the fourteenth floor.\n\nFor the first three days, this was an adventure. My cousin and I raced each other up, two steps at a time, carrying her groceries in reusable bags that cut red lines into our palms. We complained loudly and enjoyed complaining. On the fourth day it rained, and the stairwell smelled of wet cement, and my cousin had tuition. On the sixth day I went up alone with four litres of milk and did not race anybody.\n\nMy grandmother is seventy-nine. She has a bad left knee and a walking stick that she keeps behind the door and refuses to bring outside. When my mother telephoned to say that she would come after work each day, my grandmother said there was no need, because she had everything she required and the stairs were nothing. My mother came anyway.\n\nOn the ninth morning I forgot my water bottle at her flat and went back for it at a quarter past six. She was not there. Her slippers were gone from the doorway. I found her on the stairs between the seventh and the eighth floor, sitting sideways on a step with her shopping trolley beside her and her breath coming in short pulls, and she looked at me the way a person looks when they have been caught doing something wrong.\n\nShe had been going down before dawn every morning. At that hour the stairwell was empty. Nobody would see her stopping, nobody would offer to carry anything, and nobody would tell my mother. She had worked out that she needed twenty-five minutes to get down and fifty to get back up, and she had been building her whole morning around those numbers for nine days.\n\nI did not tell my mother that evening, and I have thought about that choice many times since. Instead I began arriving at a quarter past six myself, with no explanation, and we went down together. She never once thanked me, and I understood that thanking me would have meant admitting that she needed me. Some help has to be offered sideways, or it cannot be accepted at all.","questions":[{"q":"How long was the lift at Block 12 expected to be out of service, and why?","type":"literal","marks":2,"model":"It was expected to be out of service for eleven days (1m), because the lift motor was being replaced (1m). 陷阱: 送分题也有两个采分点。只写\"十一天\"丢一分, \"why\" 那半就在同一句后面。"},{"q":"Explain fully why the grandmother chose to go down the stairs before dawn.","type":"inferential","marks":3,"model":"At that hour the stairwell was completely empty, so nobody would see her stopping to rest on the steps (1m). Nobody would offer to carry her things either, and she is a woman who refuses help, since she keeps her walking stick behind the door and told her daughter there was no need to come (1m). It also meant that nobody would report back to her daughter, so she could keep her difficulty hidden from the family (1m). 陷阱: 三个点里有两个在第五段, 但\"她本来就拒绝别人帮忙\"这个证据在第三段(拐杖不肯带出门 / 叫女儿别来)。只抄第五段那三个 nobody, 答案是散的, 拿不到解释分。"},{"q":"\"She looked at me the way a person looks when they have been caught doing something wrong.\" In your own words, explain why she reacted like this, even though she had done nothing wrong.","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"She felt exposed and ashamed, because the struggle she had been hiding had suddenly been discovered (1m). In her own mind, needing help was the \"wrong\" thing, so being seen resting on the steps proved exactly the weakness she had worked so hard to keep from her family (1m). 陷阱: 要求 in your own words, 抄 \"caught doing something wrong\" 不给分。第二分要答出\"在她心里, 需要帮忙才是丢脸的事\", 而不是\"她怕被骂\"。"},{"q":"How much time had the grandmother worked out that she needed to go down the stairs, and how much to come back up?","type":"literal","marks":2,"model":"She needed twenty-five minutes to get down (1m) and fifty minutes to get back up (1m). 陷阱: 两个数字两分, 只写一个丢一半; 上楼是五十分钟不是二十五, 抄反了两分全没。"},{"q":"What does the detail about the walking stick \"that she keeps behind the door and refuses to bring outside\" tell us about the grandmother?","type":"inferential","marks":3,"model":"It shows that she is proud and does not want other people to see any sign that she is frail (1m). She is willing to accept help in private, since she keeps the stick and clearly needs it, but not to display that need in public (1m). This attitude also explains her later behaviour, because she would rather spend fifty minutes on an empty staircase than be seen being assisted (1m). 陷阱: 只写\"她很要强\"是一个点。三分要分开写: 怕被人看见 / 私下用但不肯公开用 / 这解释了她为什么天没亮就下楼。最后一点要往后一段连, 很多人写不到。"},{"q":"The writer says that \"some help has to be offered sideways, or it cannot be accepted at all\". Do you think he was right not to tell his mother? Give reasons.","type":"evaluative","marks":3,"model":"He was right in one sense, because his grandmother had already refused his mother's help directly, so telling her would most likely have led to an argument rather than to the grandmother accepting support (1m). By simply turning up at a quarter past six without explaining why, he gave her the help she needed while letting her keep her dignity, which is why she was able to accept it at all (1m). However, he was also taking a risk with a seventy-nine-year-old woman with a bad knee on a staircase, and an adult could have arranged proper help, so his silence protected her pride but not necessarily her safety (1m). 陷阱: 只顺着作者说\"他做得对\"最多两分。第三分在反方: 老人家七十九岁、膝盖不好、在楼梯上, 隐瞒是有风险的。三分题几乎都要有这一层。"}]},{"id":"comp29","title":"The Cat at Block 7","diff":5,"wordCount":399,"passage":"There is a ginger cat that lives under the staircase at Block 7. Nobody owns it. Everybody has an opinion about it.\n\nMadam Chua on the second floor feeds it at seven every morning. She uses a chipped saucer that she leaves behind the bicycle rack, and she talks to the cat in Cantonese while it eats, mostly about the weather. Mr Sivam on the fourth floor has complained to the town council four times. His complaint is not about the cat. It is about the saucer, and the ants, and the smell that rises past his kitchen window when the food is left out in the afternoon sun.\n\nFor most of last year I thought Mr Sivam was simply unkind. I was eleven, and it seemed obvious to me that a person who complains about a cat has something wrong with him. Then in June my class was assigned a project on community problems, and I had to interview a resident, and Mr Sivam was the only adult at home on a Tuesday afternoon.\n\nHe let me in and made me a glass of barley water. His flat was extremely clean. On the wall beside the door there was a photograph of a tabby cat, taken years ago, with a small red collar. He told me its name without my asking. Then he told me that his wife had died in April, that she had been the one who kept their windows open, and that he now closed them at two o'clock every afternoon because of the smell and sat in a flat with no air moving through it.\n\nI wrote none of that in my project. What I wrote was that the problem was not the cat, and not Madam Chua, and not Mr Sivam. The problem was a saucer left in the sun.\n\nMy teacher gave the project a B and wrote \"good observation\" in the margin, which I thought was a small reward for the largest thing I had learnt all year. In July I asked Madam Chua whether she might take the saucer away after the cat had finished. She looked at me for a moment, said that this was a reasonable request, and has done it ever since. Mr Sivam has not complained again. Neither of them knows that the other changed anything, and I have never seen a reason to tell them.","questions":[{"q":"What exactly was Mr Sivam complaining about, and how many times had he complained?","type":"literal","marks":2,"model":"He had complained to the town council four times (1m). His complaint was not about the cat itself but about the saucer left behind the bicycle rack, the ants it attracted, and the smell that rose past his kitchen window in the afternoon sun (1m). 陷阱: 写\"他讨厌那只猫\"直接零分 —— 第二段明明白白写了 \"His complaint is not about the cat\"。次数和内容是两个采分点, 缺一个丢一半。"},{"q":"Explain fully why the writer changed his mind about Mr Sivam.","type":"inferential","marks":3,"model":"At first he had assumed that anybody who complains about a cat \"has something wrong with him\", a judgement he made without knowing the man at all (1m). During the interview he saw a photograph of a tabby cat with a small red collar and heard Mr Sivam name it without being asked, which showed that Mr Sivam actually loved cats, so the complaint could not simply be cruelty (1m). He then learnt that Mr Sivam's wife had died in April and that he now sat alone in a flat with the windows shut, so the complaints came from grief and discomfort rather than from meanness (1m). 陷阱: 第一个点在第三段(他原来的偏见), 后两个点在第四段(照片 / 太太去世)。只写\"因为他知道了 Mr Sivam 的太太去世了\"是一分, 漏掉\"他原本怎么想的\"和\"照片说明他爱猫\"就丢两分。"},{"q":"The writer says a B grade was \"a small reward for the largest thing I had learnt all year\". Explain in your own words what he means.","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"He means that the mark he was given did not match the value of what he had actually gained (1m). The grade could only measure the written project, while the real lesson, that he had judged a neighbour unfairly without knowing his situation, was something that could not be shown on paper (1m). 陷阱: 要求 in your own words, 抄 \"a small reward for the largest thing\" 不给分。第二分要点明\"真正学到的东西是什么\", 只写\"他觉得B太低了\"是误解题意。"},{"q":"What two details from the writer's visit suggested that Mr Sivam was not simply an unkind man?","type":"literal","marks":2,"model":"A photograph of a tabby cat with a small red collar hung on the wall, and he knew and offered the cat's name without being asked (1m). He was also hospitable to the writer, letting him into the flat and making him a glass of barley water (1m). 陷阱: 题目要 two details, 只写照片丢一半; 大麦水那个细节在同一段第一句, 很容易被当成不重要的背景略过。"},{"q":"Why did the writer conclude that \"the problem was a saucer left in the sun\"?","type":"inferential","marks":3,"model":"Neither neighbour was actually doing anything wrong, since Madam Chua was being kind to a stray and Mr Sivam only wanted to be able to open his windows (1m). The single thing causing harm was the food left out in the afternoon heat, which brought the ants and the smell (1m). Defining the problem as an object rather than as a person also meant it could actually be solved, because a saucer can be taken away, whereas a quarrel between two neighbours cannot easily be settled (1m). 陷阱: 只写\"因为碟子招蚂蚁\"是一分。第三个点(把问题定在\"东西\"上而不是\"人\"上, 才有得解决)是这篇文章的中心, 漏掉就拿不满。"},{"q":"The writer has \"never seen a reason to tell them\" that the other one changed. Do you agree with his decision? Give reasons.","type":"evaluative","marks":3,"model":"I agree, because both neighbours got what they needed without either of them having to admit fault, which makes the peace much more likely to last (1m). Telling them would turn a quiet solution into an argument about who had been right, and Mr Sivam in particular is grieving and might feel exposed (1m). On the other hand, Madam Chua does not know that her small change helped a lonely neighbour, and knowing might have led to a friendship rather than merely to the end of the complaints (1m). 陷阱: 只写\"同意, 因为说了会吵架\"是一个点。第三分要给出反面(不说的代价: 两位邻居本来可能成为朋友), 缺这一层的评价题答案永远只有两分。"}]},{"id":"comp30","title":"The Handwriting","diff":6,"wordCount":422,"passage":"Between January and October of my Primary Six year, eleven folded notes appeared inside my desk. The first one arrived on the morning of a mathematics test I was certain I would fail. It said only: \"Question 12 is not as hard as it looks. Start with what you already know.\" There was no name.\n\nI decided quite early that the notes came from Priya, who sat two rows in front of me and who had once lent me a ruler. This theory survived for six months on very little evidence. Priya's handwriting sloped to the right; the notes did not slope at all. I explained this away by deciding that she was disguising it.\n\nThe notes were never encouraging in the way that adults are encouraging. None of them said that I was clever. They said things like: \"You spelt 'necessary' wrong in three different ways in one composition. Choose one and be consistent, then learn the right one.\" Another said: \"You gave up in the last ten minutes of the paper. I watched you put your pen down.\" That one bothered me for a week, because it meant that somebody had been watching, and because it was true.\n\nMr Rahim was the discipline master. He stood at the gate every morning at seven and checked shoes and hair, and he had a voice that carried the length of the parade square. In four years he had spoken to me exactly twice, both times about my shirt being untucked. Nobody I knew liked him.\n\nIn October the school held a fire drill. We stood in the field for forty minutes and came back to find that somebody had propped open the classroom windows against the rain. On Mr Rahim's clipboard, left on the front desk while he counted heads, was a list of names in a hand that did not slope at all.\n\nI never mentioned it. He never mentioned it. In November he shouted \"shirt\" at me across the parade square for the third time in four years, and I tucked it in, and something in my chest that I could not name went perfectly still.\n\nI am in secondary school now. I have not become the sort of person who leaves notes in other people's desks; I am not certain I would know how. But I have stopped assuming that the people who are kind to me will also be the people who are pleasant to me, and I think that particular lesson was the point of all eleven.","questions":[{"q":"How many notes did the writer receive, and over what period of time?","type":"literal","marks":2,"model":"He received eleven folded notes (1m), between January and October of his Primary Six year (1m). 陷阱: 两个采分点(数量 + 时间段)都在第一句。只写 \"eleven notes\" 丢一半, 时间段也不能只写\"六年级\", 要写清 January to October。"},{"q":"Explain fully how the writer finally worked out who had been writing the notes.","type":"inferential","marks":3,"model":"During the fire drill he saw Mr Rahim's clipboard left on the front desk, and the list of names on it was written \"in a hand that did not slope at all\" (1m). He had already noticed months earlier that the notes did not slope, unlike Priya's right-sloping handwriting, a difference he had spent six months explaining away (1m). One of the notes had said \"I watched you put your pen down\", which meant the writer of the notes was someone who could watch him during a paper without being noticed, which fits an adult in authority rather than a classmate sitting two rows in front (1m)."},{"q":"The writer says his theory about Priya \"survived for six months on very little evidence\". Explain in your own words what he is admitting about himself.","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"He is admitting that he went on believing something for which he had almost no proof (1m). He also admits that he actively protected the belief, explaining away the facts that contradicted it, such as the clear difference in handwriting (1m). 陷阱: 要求 in your own words, 抄 \"on very little evidence\" 不给分。第二分是\"他还主动替这个猜测找借口\"(把笔迹不同解释成\"她在伪装\"), 只写\"他没有证据\"拿一分。"},{"q":"Why did the note about giving up \"in the last ten minutes of the paper\" bother the writer for a week?","type":"inferential","marks":3,"model":"It was accurate, and an unflattering truth is much harder to dismiss than praise would be (1m). It also proved that somebody had been physically watching him during the examination, which was unsettling because he had no idea who it was (1m). It changed the notes from friendly encouragement into something closer to being held to account, which was not what he had expected from them (1m). 陷阱: 文章自己给了两个理由(\"because it meant somebody had been watching, and because it was true\"), 很多人抄完这两句就收笔 —— 那只有两分。第三分要自己推断: 纸条的性质变了, 从鼓励变成了监督。"},{"q":"In November, \"something in my chest that I could not name went perfectly still\". What do you think the writer was feeling, and why?","type":"inferential","marks":3,"model":"He was feeling a quiet certainty and peace (1m), because he now knew that the man shouting about his shirt was the same person who had quietly helped him for ten months, so the shout no longer felt like dislike and an ordinary moment that used to sting had lost its power to hurt (1m). He describes it as something he \"could not name\" because gratitude, relief and affection towards a man he had been taught to fear did not match any single feeling he had a word for (1m). 陷阱: 题目问 what he was feeling AND why, 是两件事; 而且第三个采分点在 \"could not name\" 这半句上 —— 为什么说不出名字, 不解释就丢一分。"},{"q":"The writer says he has \"stopped assuming that the people who are kind to me will also be the people who are pleasant to me\". Do you think this is a valuable lesson? Give reasons.","type":"evaluative","marks":3,"model":"Yes, because it protects him from misjudging people, just as he had misjudged Mr Rahim for four years on nothing more than a loud voice and a rule about shirts (1m). It also teaches him that genuine care can look like correction, since the notes helped him precisely because they pointed out his mistakes instead of flattering him (1m). The lesson does have a limit, though, because being unpleasant is not proof of kindness either, and he could just as easily begin excusing people who are simply rude (1m). 陷阱: d6 的评价题要能自己给结论\"划边界\"。只写\"是的, 因为不能以貌取人\"是一分, 第三分在\"但这个道理也不能反过来用\" —— 不写这一层拿不到满分。"}]},{"id":"comp31","title":"Second Place","diff":6,"wordCount":403,"passage":"The results of the Inter-School Storytelling Competition were emailed to my school on a Thursday. I came second. The girl who came first was from Rivervale Primary and her name was Nur Aisyah, and I had watched her perform in the morning session, and she had been better than me.\n\nI say this now because I want to be clear that I never believed I should have won.\n\nWhat happened was smaller than that. On the Friday, our teacher-in-charge, Miss Wong, forwarded the organisers' email to my parents. I read it over my father's shoulder at dinner. The scoresheet was attached. Three judges had scored each contestant out of thirty, and beneath the totals there was a line I do not think Miss Wong had noticed, because she is not a careful reader of attachments: Judge B's column for the morning session was empty.\n\nNur Aisyah had performed in the morning. Her total was out of sixty, not ninety. Mine, in the afternoon, was out of ninety.\n\nI sat with this for four days. I told myself that the organisers must have checked. I told myself that Judge B had probably scored her on paper and that somebody had simply failed to type it in, which was almost certainly true and which changed nothing about the fact that I could see the gap and nobody else had said a word.\n\nOn Tuesday I showed the attachment to Miss Wong. She read it twice, went very quiet, and said that she would write to the organisers that evening. She also said, in a tone I did not enjoy, that I had thought about it for four days.\n\nThe organisers replied within a week. Judge B's scores had indeed been recorded on paper. When they were added, Nur Aisyah's total rose, and mine did not, and second place stayed exactly where it had been. Nothing changed. I had risked nothing at all, it turned out, and I did not know that when I decided.\n\nAt the prize ceremony in November I shook Nur Aisyah's hand and did not mention any of it. She has no idea. What I keep returning to is not the four days of silence, which I am not proud of, and not the email, which took eleven seconds to forward. It is Miss Wong's tone. She was right. Four days is a long time to hold a thing you already know.","questions":[{"q":"What error had been made on the scoresheet, and who did it affect?","type":"literal","marks":2,"model":"Judge B's column for the morning session had been left empty, so one judge's scores were missing from the typed sheet (1m). It affected Nur Aisyah, who had performed in the morning, so her total was out of sixty while the writer's afternoon total was out of ninety (1m). 陷阱: 只写\"少了一个评委的分数\"丢一半。第二个采分点在第四段那个只有两行的短段落里 —— 受影响的是早场的 Nur Aisyah, 而且两人的满分不一样(60 对 90), 短段落最容易被跳过。"},{"q":"Explain fully why the writer did not act immediately when he noticed the missing column.","type":"inferential","marks":3,"model":"He told himself that the organisers must already have checked the sheet, so it was not his responsibility to raise it (1m). He also assumed that Judge B had scored on paper and that the marks had merely not been typed in, an explanation that turned out to be true and that allowed him to believe nothing was really wrong (1m). At the time he still believed his own second place might be at risk if the missing scores were added, since he only found out afterwards that \"I had risked nothing at all\", so staying silent protected him (1m). 陷阱: 前两个点在第五段, 第三个点要从最后两段倒推 —— 当时他并不知道自己不会掉名次, 所以沉默是有私心的。只抄第五段的两句自我安慰, 最多两分。"},{"q":"The writer says, \"I sat with this for four days.\" Explain in your own words what \"sat with this\" means here.","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"It means that he kept the knowledge to himself and turned it over in his mind without acting on it (1m). The phrase suggests an uncomfortable, motionless kind of waiting, in which he could neither forget the problem nor bring himself to do anything about it (1m). 陷阱: 要求 in your own words, 写 \"he sat with it\" 或 \"he thought about it\" 都太薄。两分要写出\"知道却不动\"的两面: 放不下, 又不肯行动。"},{"q":"What was the outcome after the organisers rechecked the scores?","type":"literal","marks":2,"model":"Judge B's scores had in fact been recorded on paper, and when they were added Nur Aisyah's total rose (1m). The writer's own total was unchanged, so second place stayed exactly where it had been (1m). 陷阱: 两个采分点(她的分数上升 / 他的名次没变)。只写 \"nothing changed\" 是概括, 拿不到第一分, 要说清楚到底哪一边变了、哪一边没变。"},{"q":"Why does the writer open by saying \"I never believed I should have won\"?","type":"inferential","marks":3,"model":"He wants the reader to understand from the start that the story is not a complaint about losing, so that his reason for reporting the error cannot be mistaken for self-interest (1m). He had watched Nur Aisyah perform and judged her to be genuinely better, which shows that he accepted the result on its merits (1m). Establishing this clears the way for the real subject of the piece, which is not who deserved the prize but why he waited four days before speaking (1m). 陷阱: 这题问的是\"作者为什么要在开头特地说这句话\", 不是\"他有没有赢\"。只写\"因为她比他厉害\"是复述, 不是回答; 第三分要说出这句话为后面的主题让路。"},{"q":"Miss Wong said, \"in a tone I did not enjoy\", that he had thought about it for four days. Was she right to say this? Give reasons.","type":"evaluative","marks":3,"model":"Yes, because he had known about a possible unfairness to another child and had allowed four days to pass, during which the wrong result could have been made final (1m). Her tone also refuses to let him treat reporting the error as something heroic, which is fair, since he admits the email took only eleven seconds to forward (1m). All the same, she was partly at fault herself, having forwarded the attachment without reading it carefully, so it would have been fairer to acknowledge her own oversight before commenting on his delay (1m). 陷阱: 只顺着作者写\"她说得对\"最多两分。第三分要抓住第三段里那句 \"she is not a careful reader of attachments\" —— 错先是她漏看的。评价题要两边都站一站。"}]},{"id":"comp32","title":"Should School Start Later?","diff":6,"wordCount":400,"passage":"Every weekday morning, close to two hundred thousand primary school pupils in Singapore leave home before seven o'clock. Most schools begin the day at half past seven; a few begin earlier. In recent years, a question that used to be dismissed has begun to be asked seriously: is that too early?\n\nThe case for a later start rests on how children's bodies actually work. Sleep researchers have found that the body clock of a growing child does not simply obey bedtime rules. As children approach their teenage years, the brain releases the chemical that makes them sleepy about two hours later than it did when they were younger. Telling a twelve-year-old to fall asleep at nine, in other words, is a little like telling an adult to fall asleep at seven. A study of one Singapore school that shifted its start time from 7.30 a.m. to 8.15 a.m. found that pupils gained an average of twenty-three minutes of sleep each night, and reported feeling less tired even a year later.\n\nAgainst this sit some practical objections, and they are not trivial. Many parents drop their children at school on the way to work, and a later start would leave those children waiting outside the gate anyway. Ending the school day later would push co-curricular activities into the evening, cutting into homework and family dinners. Bus operators and childcare centres have built their schedules around existing hours. \"A school does not run on its own timetable,\" says Mrs Serene Ho, a principal in the east. \"It runs on the timetable of every family it serves.\"\n\nThere is also a quieter argument that is easy to overlook. The children who would gain the most from a later start are often those with the longest journeys: pupils who travel across the island because of the school their parents chose, or because their family moved. These pupils already wake earliest. A later bell would help them most, and they are precisely the group least likely to be asked.\n\nNo decision has been made, and it is unlikely that one rule would suit every school. What has changed is that the question is now treated as a matter of evidence rather than of discipline. For a long time, a tired child at eight in the morning was simply a child who had gone to bed too late. That explanation is no longer taken for granted.","questions":[{"q":"According to the study mentioned in the passage, what happened when one Singapore school shifted its start time?","type":"literal","marks":2,"model":"Pupils gained an average of twenty-three minutes of sleep each night (1m). They also reported feeling less tired even a year after the change (1m). 陷阱: 只写\"多睡了 23 分钟\"丢一半。第二个采分点是 \"even a year later\" —— 说明效果是持续的, 就藏在同一句的最后几个字, 读到数字就停笔的人必丢。"},{"q":"Mrs Ho says that a school \"runs on the timetable of every family it serves\". Give three examples from the passage that show why this makes a later start difficult.","type":"inferential","marks":3,"model":"Many parents drop their children off on the way to work, so those families cannot simply shift their own morning and the children would end up waiting outside the gate anyway (1m). Ending the school day later would push co-curricular activities into the evening, cutting into the homework and family dinners that happen at home rather than at school (1m). Bus operators and childcare centres have built their schedules around the existing hours, so one school changing alone would break arrangements that other organisations depend on (1m). 陷阱: 题目要 three examples, 第三段一口气给了三条, 写两条就丢一分。而且不能只抄事实, 要说明它\"为什么牵动别人的时间表\", 否则拿不到解释分; Mrs Ho 那句引语本身是总结, 不能当第四条凑数。"},{"q":"The writer describes \"a quieter argument that is easy to overlook\". Using information from more than one paragraph, explain fully why this group of pupils would benefit most.","type":"inferential","marks":3,"model":"These pupils have the longest journeys, travelling across the island because of the school their parents chose or because the family moved, so they already wake the earliest of all (1m). Since most pupils must already leave home before seven for a half past seven start, a child travelling across the island has to leave even earlier than that (1m). They also cannot make up the lost sleep by going to bed earlier, because a growing child's brain releases the sleep chemical about two hours later than before, so the sleep is simply lost (1m). 陷阱: 题目明说 \"from more than one paragraph\"。第一个点在第四段, 第二个点要回到第一段那两个数字(七点前出门/七点半上课), 第三个点要回到第二段的生理解释。只在第四段答题最多一分 —— 这是全套题里跨段跨得最远的一道。"},{"q":"\"Telling a twelve-year-old to fall asleep at nine is a little like telling an adult to fall asleep at seven.\" Explain in your own words why the writer makes this comparison.","type":"inferential","marks":2,"model":"The writer wants adult readers to feel the difficulty for themselves rather than only read about it, so he turns the child's problem into a situation an adult would immediately recognise as unreasonable (1m). The comparison shows that the child is not being disobedient: his body is simply not ready for sleep yet, just as an adult's would not be at seven in the evening (1m). 陷阱: 要求 in your own words, 把那句比喻抄一遍不给分。第二分是\"这说明孩子不是不听话, 是身体还没准备好\", 只解释比喻本身拿不到。"},{"q":"At what time do most Singapore primary schools begin, and roughly how many pupils leave home before seven o'clock?","type":"literal","marks":2,"model":"Most schools begin at half past seven (1m). Close to two hundred thousand primary school pupils leave home before seven o'clock (1m). 陷阱: 两个数字都在第一段, 但顺序跟题目相反(先出现人数, 后出现上课时间)。按题目顺序答, 两个都要写。"},{"q":"The writer ends by saying that the old explanation for a tired child \"is no longer taken for granted\". What change of attitude is he describing, and do you think it is a good change?","type":"evaluative","marks":3,"model":"He is describing a shift from treating tiredness as a discipline problem, in which the child was simply blamed for going to bed too late, to treating it as a question of evidence about how children's bodies actually work (1m). This matters because blaming the child leads to punishment, while the research points instead to changing the timetable (1m). I think it is a good change, because the passage shows the main causes are largely outside a child's control, such as body clocks and long journeys; even so, evidence alone cannot settle the matter, since the costs to families are real and the writer himself admits that no single rule would suit every school (1m). 陷阱: 题目有两问(描述转变 + 你的看法), 只答其中一问最多两分。而且最后一分要承认\"光有证据也不能决定\", 一面倒地支持反而漏掉作者自己留的那句 \"no single rule would suit every school\"。"}]}];

window.COMP_OE_PASSAGES = COMP_OE_PASSAGES;
